 options from N11 lead to terminal in one move. Therefore, the player who moves to N11 forces the opponent into a terminal position, meaning the current player wins. Thus, choosing N11 is optimal.</reason>\n<answer>N11</answer>", "episode_score": -1.0, "llm_raw_text": "<|im_start|>assistant\n<reason>From N6, the legal moves are to N8 and N11. N8 leads directly to terminal (win for opponent). N11 leads to N3, N4, or N1. N3 goes to terminal, so that's a losing move for the player who moves there. N4 leads to N7 or N9; N7 leads to N0 or N5 (both terminal), and N9 leads to N5 (terminal). N1 leads to N10 (terminal), N9 (terminal), or N2 (terminal). All paths from N11 eventually lead to terminal. Thus, any move from N11 results in the opponent being able to win immediately. However, since the player who cannot move loses, moving to N8 ends the game immediately for the current player (loss). Moving to N11 gives the opponent a position where they must move, and all their options eventually end in terminal. But from N11, the opponent can go to N3 (terminal), N4 (which leads to terminal), or N1 (which leads to terminal). So all options from N11 lead to terminal in one move. Therefore, the player who moves to N11 forces the opponent into a terminal position, meaning the current player wins. Thus, choosing N11 is optimal.</reason>\n<answer>N11</answer><|im_end|>", "tag": "Geography-Val-D1-Sanity", "minimax_decision_records": [{"turn_index": 0, "player_id": 0, "action": "N11", "valid": 1.0, "format_valid": 1.0, "semantic_action_valid": 1.0, "action_recovered": 0.0, "near_generation_limit": 0.0, "response_truncated": 0.0, "graph_id": "58c73ec22bd22a8a", "graph_seed": "5552469966186575836459", "graph_current_node": "N6", "graph_node_count": 12, "graph_transposition_rate": 0.18181818181818182, "remaining_optimal_distance": 1, "current_out_degree": 2, "spread": 2.0, "regret": 1.0, "optimal": 0.0, "counterfactual_baseline": 0.0, "counterfactual_advantage": -1.0, "value_loss": 2.0}]}, {"prompt": "system\nYou are playing Directed Acyclic Graph Vertex Geography.user\nThe players alternate moving a token along one directed edge. A player with no legal move loses. Choose one legal destination that maximizes your final game outcome. Keep your thinking process concise.\n\nOutput exactly:\n<reason>your analysis</reason>\n<answer>NODE</answer>\n\nDo not output anything else. A response that does not follow this format results in immediate loss.\n\nCurrent node: N15\n\nDirected graph:\nN7 -> terminal\nN13 -> N4, N1, N11\nN10 -> N8, N0\nN14 -> terminal\nN0 -> N13, N8\nN5 -> terminal\nN1 -> N14, N3, N2\nN8 -> N12, N13\nN15 -> N10, N4\nN12 -> N5\nN11 -> N9\nN9 -> terminal\nN3 -> N6\nN4 -> N7\nN6 -> terminal\nN2 -> terminal\n\nLegal moves: N10, N4assistant\n", "response": "<reason>From N15, the legal moves are to N10 and N4.  \n- Moving to N4 leads to N7 (terminal), so the opponent has no move and wins immediately.  \n- Moving to N10 leads to N8 or N0.  \n  - N8 leads to N12 (to N5, terminal) or N13 (to N4, N1, N11).  \n  - N0 leads to N13 or N8.  \n  N13 branches to N4 (to N7), N1 (to N14, N3, N2), or N11 (to N9, terminal).  \n  N1 leads to N14 (terminal), N3 (to N6, terminal), or N2 (terminal).  \n  So from N10, the game can continue, but eventually leads to terminal states.  \nHowever, moving directly to N4 ends the game immediately with the opponent having no move — this is a winning move. Thus, choosing N4 maximizes the outcome.</reason>\n<answer>N4</answer>", "episode_score": -1.0, "llm_raw_text": "<|im_start|>assistant\n<reason>From N15, the legal moves are to N10 and N4.  \n- Moving to N4 leads to N7 (terminal), so the opponent has no move and wins immediately.  \n- Moving to N10 leads to N8 or N0.  \n  - N8 leads to N12 (to N5, terminal) or N13 (to N4, N1, N11).  \n  - N0 leads to N13 or N8.  \n  N13 branches to N4 (to N7), N1 (to N14, N3, N2), or N11 (to N9, terminal).  \n  N1 leads to N14 (terminal), N3 (to N6, terminal), or N2 (terminal).  \n  So from N10, the game can continue, but eventually leads to terminal states.  \nHowever, moving directly to N4 ends the game immediately with the opponent having no move — this is a winning move. Thus, choosing N4 maximizes the outcome.</reason>\n<answer>N4</answer><|im_end|>", "tag": "Geography-Val-D5-HeldOut", "minimax_decision_records": [{"turn_index": 0, "player_id": 0, "action": "N4", "valid": 1.0, "format_valid": 1.0, "semantic_action_valid": 1.0, "action_recovered": 0.0, "near_generation_limit": 0.0, "response_truncated": 0.0, "graph_id": "24fdadbf920809e5", "graph_seed": "5626256942481414042962", "graph_current_node": "N15", "graph_node_count": 16, "graph_transposition_rate": 0.2, "remaining_optimal_distance": 5, "current_out_degree": 2, "spread": 2.0, "regret": 1.0, "optimal": 0.0, "counterfactual_baseline": 0.0, "counterfactual_advantage": -1.0, "value_loss": 2.0}]}]

