id and terminal, so it maximizes the outcome.</reason>\n<answer>N8</answer>", "episode_score": 0.05, "llm_raw_text": "<reason>Starting at N3, the player can move to N0 or N8. Both N0 and N8 are terminal nodes, meaning the player who moves to either wins immediately, as the opponent has no legal moves. Thus, moving to either N0 or N8 results in an immediate win. Since both are winning moves, either is optimal. Choosing N8 is valid and terminal, so it maximizes the outcome.</reason>\n<answer>N8</answer>"}, {"prompt": "system\nYou are playing Directed Acyclic Graph Vertex Geography.user\nThe players alternate moving a token along one directed edge. A player with no legal move loses. Choose one legal destination that maximizes your final game outcome. Keep your thinking process concise.\n\nOutput exactly:\n<reason>your analysis</reason>\n<answer>NODE</answer>\n\nDo not output anything else. A response that does not follow this format results in immediate loss.\n\nCurrent node: N2\n\nDirected graph:\nN4 -> terminal\nN7 -> terminal\nN9 -> terminal\nN6 -> N0, N7\nN1 -> N5, N4\nN2 -> N3, N0\nN0 -> N9\nN5 -> terminal\nN3 -> N6, N8\nN8 -> N7, N1\n\nLegal moves: N3, N0assistant\n", "response": "<reason>Starting at N2, the legal moves are to N3 or N0. Moving to N0 leads to N9, which is terminal, so the opponent cannot move and we win immediately. Moving to N3 leads to N6 or N8. From N6, we can go to N0 or N7; from N8, to N7 or N1. These paths eventually lead to terminal nodes or loops that can be exploited. However, N0 directly leads to terminal (N9), so choosing N0 wins immediately. Thus, N0 is the optimal move.</reason>\n<answer>N0</answer>", "episode_score": -0.95, "llm_raw_text": "<reason>Starting at N2, the legal moves are to N3 or N0. Moving to N0 leads to N9, which is terminal, so the opponent cannot move and we win immediately. Moving to N3 leads to N6 or N8. From N6, we can go to N0 or N7; from N8, to N7 or N1. These paths eventually lead to terminal nodes or loops that can be exploited. However, N0 directly leads to terminal (N9), so choosing N0 wins immediately. Thus, N0 is the optimal move.</reason>\n<answer>N0</answer>"}, {"prompt": "system\nYou are playing Directed Acyclic Graph Vertex Geography.user\nThe players alternate moving a token along one directed edge. A player with no legal move loses. Choose one legal destination that maximizes your final game outcome. Keep your thinking process concise.\n\nOutput exactly:\n<reason>your analysis</reason>\n<answer>NODE</answer>\n\nDo not output anything else. A response that does not follow this format results in immediate loss.\n\nCurrent node: N0\n\nDirected graph:\nN4 -> terminal\nN7 -> terminal\nN9 -> terminal\nN6 -> N0, N7\nN1 -> N5, N4\nN2 -> N3, N0\nN0 -> N9\nN5 -> terminal\nN3 -> N6, N8\nN8 -> N7, N1\n\nLegal moves: N9assistant\n", "response": "<reason>Starting at N0, the only legal move is to N9, which leads directly to terminal. Thus, the first player (me) moves to N9 and wins immediately. No further moves are possible. This is the only legal move from N0, and it results in an immediate win. Therefore, choosing N9 is optimal.</reason>\n<answer>N9</answer>", "episode_score": 0.05, "llm_raw_text": "<reason>Starting at N0, the only legal move is to N9, which leads directly to terminal. Thus, the first player (me) moves to N9 and wins immediately. No further moves are possible. This is the only legal move from N0, and it results in an immediate win. Therefore, choosing N9 is optimal.</reason>\n<answer>N9</answer>"}, {"prompt": "system\nYou are playing Directed Acyclic Graph Vertex Geography.user\nThe players alternate moving a token along one directed edge. A player with no legal move loses. Choose one legal destination that maximizes your final game outcome. Keep your thinking process concise.\n\nOutput exactly:\n<reason>your analysis</reason>\n<answer>NODE</answer>\n\nDo not output anything else. A response that does not follow this format results in immediate loss.\n\nCurrent node: N5\n\nDirected graph:\nN1 -> terminal\nN6 -> terminal\nN8 -> N9\nN0 -> N7, N4\nN5 -> N8, N3, N2\nN4 -> N6, N1\nN7 -> terminal\nN3 -> N8, N2\nN9 -> terminal\nN2 -> N0\n\nLegal moves: N8, N3, N2assistant\n", "response": "<reason>Starting at N5, the player can move to N8, N3, or N2. We analyze each option to determine which leads to a winning position.  \n- N8 → N9 (terminal), so the next player loses immediately. This is a winning move.  \n- N3 → N8 or N2. From N8, opponent wins (as N8 → N9, opponent takes last move). From N2 → N0, which leads to a long chain. But N0 → N7 (terminal) or N4. N4 → N6 or N1 (both terminal). So N2 leads to a path where opponent can force a win.  \n- N2 → N0 → N7 or N4 → terminal. Again, opponent wins.  \nThus, moving to N8 immediately ends the game with opponent having no move. This is optimal. The move to N8 is winning and maximizes outcome.</reason>\n<answer>N8</answer>", "episode_score": -0.6166666666666667, "llm_raw_text": "<reason>Starting at N5, the player can move to N8, N3, or N2. We analyze each option to determine which leads to a winning position.  \n- N8 → N9 (terminal), so the next player loses immediately. This is a winning move.  \n- N3 → N8 or N2. From N8, opponent wins (as N8 → N9, opponent takes last move). From N2 → N0, which leads to a long chain. But N0 → N7 (terminal) or N4. N4 → N6 or N1 (both terminal). So N2 leads to a path where opponent can force a win.  \n- N2 → N0 → N7 or N4 → terminal. Again, opponent wins.  \nThus, moving to N8 immediately ends the game with opponent having no move. This is optimal. The move to N8 is winning and maximizes outcome.</reason>\n<answer>N8</answer>"}, {"prompt": "system\nYou are playing Directed Acyclic Graph Vertex Geography.user\nThe players alternate moving a token along one directed edge. A player with no legal move loses. Choose one legal destination that maximizes your final game outcome. Keep your thinking process concise.\n\nOutput exactly:\n<reason>your analysi