oosing N4 is arbitrary but valid; however, N6 and N4 are both terminal, so either is fine. Selecting N4 is sufficient.</reason>\n<answer>N4</answer>", "episode_score": 0.05, "llm_raw_text": "<reason>Starting at N5, the legal moves are to N6 or N4, both of which lead to terminal nodes. Moving to either N6 or N4 ends the game immediately, and the player who makes the move wins because the opponent has no legal move. Thus, both moves result in an immediate win for the current player. Since both options are winning and equivalent in outcome, either is optimal. Choosing N4 is arbitrary but valid; however, N6 and N4 are both terminal, so either is fine. Selecting N4 is sufficient.</reason>\n<answer>N4</answer>"}]
