e with the opponent having no move. This is a winning move. Therefore, the best choice is N8.</reason>  \n<answer>N8</answer>", "episode_score": 1.05, "llm_raw_text": "<reason>Starting at N5, the possible moves are to N8 or N7.  \n- Moving to N8 leads to terminal (win for the player who made the move, so opponent loses).  \n- Moving to N7 leads to N4 or N6, both of which go to terminal.  \nThus, moving to N8 immediately ends the game with the opponent having no move. This is a winning move. Therefore, the best choice is N8.</reason>  \n<answer>N8</answer>"}, {"prompt": "system\nYou are playing Directed Acyclic Graph Vertex Geography.user\nThe players alternate moving a token along one directed edge. A player with no legal move loses. Choose one legal destination that maximizes your final game outcome. Keep your thinking process concise.\n\nOutput exactly:\n<reason>your analysis</reason>\n<answer>NODE</answer>\n\nDo not output anything else. A response that does not follow this format results in immediate loss.\n\nCurrent node: N2\n\nDirected graph:\nN4 -> N9, N1\nN6 -> terminal\nN3 -> terminal\nN0 -> terminal\nN5 -> terminal\nN9 -> N1, N5\nN8 -> N3\nN2 -> N4, N7\nN1 -> N8, N6\nN7 -> N0, N3\n\nLegal moves: N4, N7assistant\n", "response": "<reason>Starting at N2, the legal moves are to N4 or N7. We analyze each:</reason>\n<answer>N7</answer>", "episode_score": -0.95, "llm_raw_text": "<reason>Starting at N2, the legal moves are to N4 or N7. We analyze each:</reason>\n<answer>N7</answer>"}, {"prompt": "system\nYou are playing Directed Acyclic Graph Vertex Geography.user\nThe players alternate moving a token along one directed edge. A player with no legal move loses. Choose one legal destination that maximizes your final game outcome. Keep your thinking process concise.\n\nOutput exactly:\n<reason>your analysis</reason>\n<answer>NODE</answer>\n\nDo not output anything else. A response that does not follow this format results in immediate loss.\n\nCurrent node: N7\n\nDirected graph:\nN4 -> N9, N1\nN6 -> terminal\nN3 -> terminal\nN0 -> terminal\nN5 -> terminal\nN9 -> N1, N5\nN8 -> N3\nN2 -> N4, N7\nN1 -> N8, N6\nN7 -> N0, N3\n\nLegal moves: N0, N3assistant\n", "response": "<reason>Starting at N7, the legal moves are to N0 or N3. Both N0 and N3 are terminal nodes, so any move to either ends the game immediately. The player who makes the move to a terminal node wins, because the opponent has no legal move. Thus, both moves lead to an immediate win for the current player. Since both options result in the same outcome (win), either is optimal. Choosing N3 is valid and leads to a win. However, N0 and N3 are both terminal, so either is acceptable. We select N3 as it appears in the graph's structure and is reachable directly.</reason>\n<answer>N3</answer>", "episode_score": 0.05, "llm_raw_text": "<reason>Starting at N7, the legal moves are to N0 or N3. Both N0 and N3 are terminal nodes, so any move to either ends the game immediately. The player who makes the move to a terminal node wins, because the opponent has no legal move. Thus, both moves lead to an immediate win for the current player. Since both options result in the same outcome (win), either is optimal. Choosing N3 is valid and leads to a win. However, N0 and N3 are both terminal, so either is acceptable. We select N3 as it appears in the graph's structure and is reachable directly.</reason>\n<answer>N3</answer>"}, {"prompt": "system\nYou are playing Directed Acyclic Graph Vertex Geography.user\nThe players alternate moving a token along one directed edge. A player with no legal move loses. Choose one legal destination that maximizes your final game outcome. Keep your thinking process concise.\n\nOutput exactly:\n<reason>your analysis</reason>\n<answer>NODE</answer>\n\nDo not output anything else. A response that does not follow this format results in immediate loss.\n\nCurrent node: N2\n\nDirected graph:\nN9 -> terminal\nN4 -> N12, N11\nN8 -> N9, N6\nN1 -> N7, N9\nN6 -> terminal\