sing N1 is optimal.</reason>\n<answer>N1</answer>"}, {"prompt": "system\nYou are playing Directed Acyclic Graph Vertex Geography.user\nThe players alternate moving a token along one directed edge. A player with no legal move loses. Choose one legal destination that maximizes your final game outcome. Keep your thinking process concise.\n\nOutput exactly:\n<reason>your analysis</reason>\n<answer>NODE</answer>\n\nDo not output anything else. A response that does not follow this format results in immediate loss.\n\nCurrent node: N1\n\nDirected graph:\nN6 -> N1, N0\nN3 -> N2, N6\nN7 -> terminal\nN1 -> N7\nN9 -> N4\nN5 -> N3, N9\nN8 -> N5, N3, N1\nN0 -> terminal\nN2 -> terminal\nN4 -> terminal\n\nLegal moves: N7assistant\n", "response": "<reason>Starting at N1, the only legal move is to N7, which is a terminal node. The player who moves to N7 wins immediately because the opponent has no legal move. Thus, moving to N7 is the only viable and optimal choice. This results in an immediate win for the current player.</reason>\n<answer>N7</answer>", "episode_score": 0.05, "llm_raw_text": "<reason>Starting at N1, the only legal move is to N7, which is a terminal node. The player who moves to N7 wins immediately because the opponent has no legal move. Thus, moving to N7 is the only viable and optimal choice. This results in an immediate win for the current player.</reason>\n<answer>N7</answer>"}, {"prompt": "system\nYou are playing Directed Acyclic Graph Vertex Geography.user\nThe players alternate moving a token along one directed edge. A player with no legal move loses. Choose one legal destination that maximizes your final game outcome. Keep your thinking process concise.\n\nOutput exactly:\n<reason>your analysis</reason>\n<answer>NODE</answer>\n\nDo not output anything else. A response that does not follow this format results in immediate loss.\n\nCurrent node: N9\n\nDirected graph:\nN10 -> N4, N1\nN11 -> N13, N3\nN8 -> terminal\nN2 -> terminal\nN7 -> N10, N6\nN12 -> N5, N0\nN