s in immediate loss.\n\nCurrent node: N13\n\nDirected graph:\nN4 -> N2, N6\nN5 -> terminal\nN7 -> N10, N5\nN9 -> N7, N12\nN10 -> N6, N12\nN6 -> terminal\nN1 -> terminal\nN12 -> terminal\nN8 -> N0, N9\nN13 -> N8, N4\nN3 -> terminal\nN11 -> terminal\nN2 -> N11, N3\nN0 -> N1, N11\n\nLegal moves: N8, N4assistant\n", "response": "<reason>Starting at N13, the player can move to N8 or N4. Moving to N4 leads to N2 or N6. N6 is terminal, so if we go N13 → N4 → N6, the opponent has no move and wins. But if we go N13 → N4 → N2, then N2 leads to N11 or N3, both terminal, so opponent loses. Thus, N13 → N4 → N2 is a winning move. Alternatively, N13 → N8 → N9 → N7 → N5 → terminal, or N8 → N9 → N7 → N10 → N6 or N12 (both terminal). But if we go to N8, the opponent can force a terminal path. The key is to avoid giving the opponent a winning path. The best move is N13 → N4 → N2 → N11 or N3, both terminal, so opponent has no move. Thus, N4 is better than N8. Therefore, choosing N4 maximizes outcome.</reason>\n<answer>N4</answer>", "episode_score": -0.95, "llm_raw_text": "<reason>Starting at N13, the player can move to N8 or N4. Moving to N4 leads to N2 or N6. N6 is terminal, so if we go N13 → N4 → N6, the opponent has no move and wins. But if we go N13 → N4 → N2, then N2 leads to N11 or N3, both terminal, so opponent loses. Thus, N13 → N4 → N2 is a winning move. Alternatively, N13 → N8 → N9 → N7 → N5 → terminal, or N8 → N9 → N7 → N10 → N6 or N12 (both terminal). But if we go to N8, the opponent can force a terminal path. The key is to avoid giving the opponent a winning path. The best move is N13 → N4 → N2 → N11 or N3, both terminal, so opponent has no move. Thus, N4 is better than N8. Therefore, choosing N4 maximizes outcome.</reason>\n<answer>N4</answer>"}, {"prompt": "system\nYou are playing Directed Acyclic Graph Vertex Geography.user\nThe players alternate moving a token along one directed edge. A player with no legal move loses. Choose one legal destination that maximizes your final game outcome. Keep your thinking process concise.\n\nOutput exactly:\n<reason>your analysis</reason>\n<answer>NODE</answer>\n\nDo not output anything else. A response that does not follow this format results in immediate loss.\n\nCurrent node: N4\n\nDirected graph:\nN4 -> N2, N6\nN5 -> terminal\nN7 -> N10, N5\nN9 -> N7, N12\nN10 -> N6, N12\nN6 -> terminal\nN1 -> terminal\nN12 -> terminal\nN8 -> N0, N9\nN13 -> N8, N4\nN3 -> terminal\nN11 -> terminal\nN2 -> N11, N3\nN0 -> N1, N11\n\nLegal moves: N2, N6assistant\n", "response": "<reason>The current node is N4. From N4, the legal moves are to N2 or N6.  \n- Moving to N6 leads directly to terminal (win for the player who makes the move).  \n- Moving to N2 leads to N11 or N3, both of which are terminal. So, from N2, the next player has no moves and loses.  \nThus, moving to N6 wins immediately. Choosing N6 is optimal.</reason>  \n<answer>N6</answer>", "episode_score": 1.05, "llm_raw_text": "<reason>The current node is N4. From N4, the legal moves are to N2 or N6.  \n- Moving to N6 leads directly to terminal (win for the player who makes the move).  \n- Moving to N2 leads to N11 or N3, both of which are terminal. So, from N2, the next player has no moves and loses.  \nThus, moving to N6 wins immediately. Choosing N6 is optimal.</reason>  \n<answer>N6</answer>"}, {"prompt": "system\nYou are playing Directed Acyclic Graph Vertex Geography.user\nThe players alternate moving a token along one directed edge. A player with no legal move loses. Choose one legal destination that maximizes your final game outcome. Keep your thinking process concise.\n\nOutput exactly:\n<reason>your analysis</reason>\n<answer>NODE</answer>\n\nDo not output anything else. A response that does not follow this format results in immediate loss.\n\nCurrent node: N0\n\nDirected graph:\nN9 -> N4\nN3 -> N2\nN2 -> terminal\nN5 -> N8\nN1 -> N5, N6\nN4 -> N7, N1, N3\nN6 -> terminal\nN0 -> N9, N3, N4\nN7 -> terminal\nN8 -> terminal\n\nLegal moves: N9, N3, 