[2026-08-13 14:08:59] [agentic_pipeline.py (516)] [INFO] [DRIVER 0 / 1][PID 1538566] [{"prompt": "system\nYou are playing Directed Acyclic Graph Vertex Geography.user\nThe players alternate moving a token along one directed edge. A player with no legal move loses. Choose one legal destination that maximizes your final game outcome. Keep your thinking process concise.\n\nOutput exactly:\n<reason>your analysis</reason>\n<answer>NODE</answer>\n\nDo not output anything else. A response that does not follow this format results in immediate loss.\n\nCurrent node: N4\n\nDirected graph:\nN0 -> terminal\nN6 -> N5, N9\nN9 -> N0, N3\nN2 -> N7, N5\nN1 -> terminal\nN8 -> N6, N2\nN7 -> N1\nN5 -> terminal\nN4 -> N8, N7\nN3 -> terminal\n\nLegal moves: N8, N7assistant\n", "response": "<reason>Starting at N4, the legal moves are to N8 or N7.  \n- Moving to N7: N7 → N1 → terminal. The opponent has no move, so current player wins.  \n- Moving to N8: N8 → N6 → (N5 or N9).  \n  - If N6 → N5: N5 → terminal → opponent wins.  \n  - If N6 → N9: N9 → N0 or N3, both terminal. So opponent wins.  \nThus, any move from N8 leads to opponent winning.  \nOnly move to N7 results in immediate win. Therefore, choosing N7 is optimal.</reason>\n<answer>N7</answer>", "episode_score": -0.95, "llm_raw_text": "<reason>Starting at N4, the legal moves are to N8 or N7.  \n- Moving to N7: N7 → N1 → terminal. The opponent has no move, so current player wins.  \n- Moving to N8: N8 → N6 → (N5 or N9).  \n  - If N6 → N5: N5 → terminal → opponent wins.  \n  - If N6 → N9: N9 → N0 or N3, both terminal. So opponent wins.  \nThus, any move from N8 leads to opponent winning.  \nOnly move to N7 results in immediate win. Therefore, choosing N7 is optimal.</reason>\n<answer>N7</answer>"}, {"prompt": "system\nYou are playing Directed Acyclic Graph Vertex Geography.user\nThe players alternate moving a token along one directed edge. A player with no legal move loses. Choose one legal destination that maximizes your final game outcome. Keep your thinking process concise.\n\nOutput exactly:\n<reason>your analysis</reason>\n<answer>NODE</answer>\n\nDo not output anything else. A response that does not follow this format results in immediate loss.\n\nCurrent node: N7\n\nDirected graph:\nN0 -> terminal\nN6 -> N5, N9\nN9 -> N0, N3\nN2 -> N7, N5\nN1 -> terminal\nN8 -> N6, N2\nN7 -> N1\nN5 -> terminal\nN4 -> N8, N7\nN3 -> terminal\n\nLegal moves: N1assistant\n", "response": "<reason>Starting at N7, the only legal move is to N1, which leads to terminal. Since the player who moves to a terminal node wins (the opponent has no legal move), moving to N1 ends the game immediately. Thus, N1 is the only choice, and it results in an immediate win for the current player. No other move is available, so this is the optimal choice.</reason>\n<answer>N1</answer>", "episode_score": 0.05, "llm_raw_text": "<reason>Starting at N7, the only legal move is to N1, which leads to terminal. Since the player who moves to a terminal node wins (the opponent has no legal move), moving to N1 ends the game immediately. Thus, N1 is the only choice, and it results in an immediate win for the current player. No other move is available, so this is the optimal choice.</reason>\n<answer>N1</answer>"}, {"prompt": "system\nYou are playing Directed Acyclic Graph Vertex Geography.user\nThe players alternate moving a token along one directed edge. A player with no legal move loses. Choose one legal destination that maximizes your final game outcome. Keep your thinking process concise.\n\nOutput exactly:\n<reason>your analysis</reason>\n<answer>NODE</answer>\n\nDo not output anything else. A response that does not follow this format results in immediate loss.\n\nCurrent node: N2\n\nDirected graph:\nN10 -> N11, N9\nN4 -> N1, N11\nN8 -> N5, N0\nN7 -> terminal\nN3 -> N1, N8\nN2 -> N13, N12\nN11 -> terminal\nN12 -> N4, N3\nN6 -> terminal\nN5 -> N9, N10\nN0 -> terminal\nN1 -> terminal\nN9 -> terminal\nN13 -> N7, N6\n\nLegal moves: N13, N12assistant\n", "response": "<reason>Starting at N2, the legal moves are to N13 or N12. N13 leads to N7 or N6, both of which are terminal nodes, so the player who moves to N13 wins immediately (opponent has no move). N12 leads to N4 or N3. From N4, paths go to N1 or N11 (both terminal), and from N3 to N1 or N8. N8 leads to N5 or N0 (both terminal). Thus, N12 opens paths that eventually lead to terminal nodes, but the game may continue longer. However, since N13 results in an immediate win (the opponent cannot move), choosing N13 guarantees a win. Therefore, N13 is the optimal move.</reason>\n<answer>N13</answer>", "episode_score": -0.95, "llm_raw_text": "<reason>Starting at N2, the legal moves are to N13 or N12. N13 leads to N7 or N6, both of which are terminal nodes, so the player who moves to N13 wins immediately (opponent has no move). N12 leads to N4 or N3. From N4, paths go to N1 or N11 (both terminal), and from N3 to N1 or N8. N8 leads to N5 or N0 (both terminal). Thus, N12 opens paths that eventually lead to terminal nodes, but the game may continue longer. However, since N13 results in an immediate win (the opponent cannot move), choosing N13 guarantees a win. Therefore, N13 is the optimal move.</reason>\n<answer>N13</answer>"}, {"prompt": "system\nYou are playing Directed Acyclic Graph Vertex Geography.user\nThe players alternate moving a token along one directed edge. A player with no legal move loses. Choose one legal destination that maximizes your final game outcome. Keep your thinking process concise.\n\nOutput exactly:\n<reason>your analysis</reason>\n<answer>NODE</answer>\n\nDo not output anything else. A response that does not follow this format results in immediate loss.\n\nCurrent node: N13\n\nDirected graph:\nN10 -> N11, N9\nN4 -> N1, N11\nN8 -> N5, N0\nN7 -> terminal\nN3 -> N1, N8\nN2 -> N13, N12\nN11 -> terminal\nN12 -> N4, N3\nN6 -> terminal\nN5 -> N9, N10\nN0 -> terminal\nN1 -> terminal\nN9 -> terminal\nN13 -> N7, N6\n\nLegal moves: N7, N6assistant\n", "response": "<reason>The current node is N13. From N13, the legal moves are to N7 and N6. Both N7 and N6 lead to terminal nodes (i.e., the game ends immediately). Since the player who cannot move loses, making a move to either N7 or N6 ends the game immediately, and the opponent has no move. Thus, either move wins. Both are terminal, so either is equally good. Choosing one maximizes outcome. We select N6 as it appears earlier in the list.</reason>\n<answer>N6</answer>", "episode_score": 0.05, "llm_raw_text": "<reason>The current node is N13. From N13, the legal moves are to N7 and N6. Both N7 and N6 lead to terminal nodes (i.e., the game ends immediately). Since the player who cannot move loses, making a move to either N7 or N6 ends the game immediately, and the opponent has no move. Thus, either move wins. Both are terminal, so either is equally good. Choosing one maximizes outcome. We select N6 as it appears earlier in the list.</reason>\n<answer>N6</answer>"}, {"prompt": "system\nYou are playing Directed Acyclic Graph Vertex Geography.user\nThe players alternate moving a token along one directed edge. A player with no legal move loses. Choose one legal destination that maximizes your final game outcome. Keep your thinking process concise.\n\nOutput exactly:\n<reason>your analysis</reason>\n<answer>NODE</answer>\n\nDo not output anything else. A response that does not follow this format results in immediate loss.\n\nCurrent node: N11\n\nDirected graph:\nN2 -> terminal\nN13 -> terminal\nN6 -> N3\nN5 -> N12, N9, N1\nN11 -> N1, N9, N4\nN9 -> N0\nN10 -> N6, N2\nN0 -> terminal\nN7 -> terminal\nN8 -> terminal\nN12 -> N13\nN4 -> N7, N13, N5, N8\nN3 -> terminal\nN1 -> N10\n\nLegal moves: N1, N9, N4assistant\n", "response": "<reason>Starting at N11, the legal moves are to N1, N9, or N4. We analyze each option for winning potential.  \n- N9 leads to N0 (terminal), so the next player loses immediately — good for current player.  \n- N1 leads to N10, which branches to N6