g N13 is a winning move.</reason>\n<answer>N13</answer>"}, {"prompt": "system\nYou are playing Directed Acyclic Graph Vertex Geography.user\nThe players alternate moving a token along one directed edge. A player with no legal move loses. Choose one legal destination that maximizes your final game outcome. Keep your thinking process concise.\n\nOutput exactly:\n<reason>your analysis</reason>\n<answer>NODE</answer>\n\nDo not output anything else. A response that does not follow this format results in immediate loss.\n\nCurrent node: N13\n\nDirected graph:\nN13 -> N2, N3\nN11 -> N1, N12\nN2 -> terminal\nN1 -> N8, N9\nN3 -> N9, N5\nN5 -> terminal\nN0 -> N10, N2\nN4 -> terminal\nN8 -> terminal\nN6 -> N4, N0\nN12 -> N6, N8\nN9 -> terminal\nN10 -> terminal\nN7 -> N11, N13\n\nLegal moves: N2, N3assistant\n", "response": "<reason>Starting at N13, the legal moves are to N2 or N3. N2 leads directly to terminal, so the player who moves to N2 wins immediately (opponent has no move). N3 leads to N9 or N5, both of which are terminal. Thus, moving to N3 results in immediate loss for the opponent. Therefore, choosing N2 is optimal as it ends the game immediately for the opponent. Hence, N2 is the best move.</reason>\n<answer>N2</answer>", "episode_score": 1.05, "llm_raw_text": "<reason>Starting at N13, the legal moves are to N2 or N3. N2 leads directly to terminal, so the player who moves to N2 wins immediately (opponent has no move). N3 leads to N9 or N5, both of which are terminal. Thus, moving to N3 results in immediate loss for the opponent. Therefore, choosing N2 is optimal as it ends the game immediately for the opponent. Hence, N2 is the best move.</reason>\n<answer>N2</answer>"}, {"prompt": "system\nYou are playing Directed Acyclic Graph Vertex Geography.user\nThe players alternate moving a token along one directed edge. A player with no legal move loses. Choose one legal destination that maximizes your final game outcome. Keep your thinking process concise.\n\nOutput exactl