, since opponent has no move). So from N6, the next player wins.  \n- N4 → N0 → N9 or N3; both eventually lead to terminal or loops. From N0, next move is to N9 or N3, which then go to N5, N1, or terminal. But N9 → N5 or N1, both terminal. So N4 leads to a path that eventually ends, and the player who moves to N0 or N9 can force the next player into a terminal. However, chains from N4 go to N0, then to N9 or N3, which are terminal. So the player who moves to N4 must eventually allow the opponent to reach terminal.  \n- N2 → N8 or N6; both N8 and N6 lead to terminal. So from N2, opponent can win immediately.  \n\nBest move: N6 → leads to N3 → terminal. So the opponent cannot move, and current player wins. This is a winning move.  \nThus, choosing N6 is optimal.</reason>  \n<answer>N6</answer>", "episode_score": -0.6166666666666667, "llm_raw_text": "<reason>From N7, the legal moves are to N6, N4, or N2. We analyze each:  \n- N6 → N3 → terminal (player who moves to N3 wins, since opponent has no move). So from N6, the next player wins.  \n- N4 → N0 → N9 or N3; both eventually lead to terminal or loops. From N0, next move is to N9 or N3, which then go to N5, N1, or terminal. But N9 → N5 or N1, both terminal. So N4 leads to a path that eventually ends, and the player who moves to N0 or N9 can force the next player into a terminal. However, chains from N4 go to N0, then to N9 or N3, which are terminal. So the player who moves to N4 must eventually allow the opponent to reach terminal.  \n- N2 → N8 or N6; both N8 and N6 lead to terminal. So from N2, opponent can win immediately.  \n\nBest move: N6 → leads to N3 → terminal. So the opponent cannot move, and current player wins. This is a winning move.  \nThus, choosing N6 is optimal.</reason>  \n<answer>N6</answer>"}, {"prompt": "system\nYou are playing Directed Acyclic Graph Vertex Geography.user\nThe players alternate moving a token along one directed edge. A player with no legal move loses. Choose one legal destination that maximizes your final game outcome. Keep your thinking process concise.\n\nOutput exactly:\n<reason>your analysis</reason>\n<answer>NODE</answer>\n\nDo not output anything else. A response that does not follow this format results in immediate loss.\n\nCurrent node: N6\n\nDirected graph:\nN6 -> N3\nN7 -> N6, N4, N2\nN9 -> N5, N1\nN4 -> N0\nN2 -> N8, N6\nN5 -> terminal\nN3 -> terminal\nN0 -> N9, N3\nN1 -> terminal\nN8 -> terminal\n\nLegal moves: N3assistant\n", "response": "<reason>Starting at N6, the only legal move is to N3. N3 leads to terminal, so the player who moves to N3 wins immediately. Thus, moving to N3 results in an immediate win. No other move is available from N6. Therefore, N3 is the optimal choice.</reason>\n<answer>N3</answer>", "episode_score": 0.05, "llm_raw_text": "<reason>Starting at N6, the only legal move is to N3. N3 leads to terminal, so the player who moves to N3 wins immediately. Thus, moving to N3 results in an immediate win. No other move is available from N6. Therefore, N3 is the optimal choice.</reason>\n<answer>N3</answer>"}]
