666666667, "llm_raw_text": "<reason>From N6, the legal moves are to N2, N9, or N3. We analyze each option:  \n- N2 → leads to N4 or N7. N4 → N1 or N0; N1 → terminal (win for next player), N0 → N8 → terminal. N7 → terminal. So paths eventually end.  \n- N9 → leads to N2 or N3; same branching as from N2/N3.  \n- N3 → leads to N5 → terminal. This is a direct win for the next player.  \n\nThus, moving to N3 leads to immediate terminal state on the next turn, meaning current player wins. All other options allow opponent to win eventually. So N3 is best. However, note: the player who makes the move to terminal wins? No — the player with no move loses. So if you move to a node that leads to opponent's win, you lose. But if you move to a node that forces opponent into a losing position, you win.  \n\nBut here, from N3 → N5 → terminal → opponent has no move → opponent loses → current player wins. So move to N3 is winning. Similarly, from N2: N2 → N4 or N7. N4 → N1 or N0; both lead to terminal eventually. But the path may allow opponent to win. But N3 gives immediate terminal after one step. So best choice is N3.</reason>\n<answer>N3</answer>"}]
