[2026-08-13 14:22:19] [agentic_pipeline.py (516)] [INFO] [DRIVER 0 / 1][PID 1538566] [{"prompt": "system\nYou are playing Directed Acyclic Graph Vertex Geography.user\nThe players alternate moving a token along one directed edge. A player with no legal move loses. Choose one legal destination that maximizes your final game outcome. Keep your thinking process concise.\n\nOutput exactly:\n<reason>your analysis</reason>\n<answer>NODE</answer>\n\nDo not output anything else. A response that does not follow this format results in immediate loss.\n\nCurrent node: N0\n\nDirected graph:\nN8 -> N5, N3\nN4 -> terminal\nN3 -> N7, N6\nN6 -> N1, N9\nN2 -> terminal\nN7 -> terminal\nN9 -> terminal\nN5 -> N2\nN1 -> N4, N9\nN0 -> N8, N5\n\nLegal moves: N8, N5assistant\n", "response": "<reason>Starting at N0, the player can move to either N8 or N5. Moving to N5 leads to N2 (terminal), so the opponent has no move and wins immediately. Moving to N8 leads to N5 or N3. From N5, the opponent goes to N2 (terminal), so again, the current player would have no move and lose. From N3, they go to N7 or N6. N7 and N6 both eventually lead to terminals. The key is to avoid giving the opponent a winning path. The path N0 → N8 → N5 → N2 ends immediately after the opponent’s move. Thus, N0 → N5 leads to opponent moving to N2 (win for first player). Actually, N0 → N5 → N2 is terminal, so first player forces opponent to lose on move. Thus, N5 is better than N8. Therefore, choosing N5 is optimal.</reason>\n<answer>N5</answer>", "episode_score": -0.95, "llm_raw_text": "<reason>Starting at N0, the player can move to either N8 or N5. Moving to N5 leads to N2 (terminal), so the opponent has no move and wins immediately. Moving to N8 leads to N5 or N3. From N5, the opponent goes to N2 (terminal), so again, the current player would have no move and lose. From N3, they go to N7 or N6. N7 and N6 both eventually lead to terminals. The key is to avoid giving the opponent a winning path. The path N0 → N8 → N5 → N2 ends immediately after the opponent’s move. Thus, N0 → N5 leads to opponent moving to N2 (win for first player). Actually, N0 → N5 → N2 is terminal, so first player forces opponent to lose on move. Thus, N5 is better than N8. Therefore, choosing N5 is optimal.</reason>\n<answer>N5</answer>"}, {"prompt": "system\nYou are playing Directed Acyclic Graph Vertex Geography.user\nThe players alternate moving a token along one directed edge. A player with no legal move loses. Choose one legal destination that maximizes your final game outcome. Keep your thinking process concise.\n\nOutput exactly:\n<reason>your analysis</reason>\n<answer>NODE</answer>\n\nDo not output anything else. A response that does not follow this format results in immediate loss.\n\nCurrent node: N5\n\nDirected graph:\nN8 -> N5, N3\nN4 -> terminal\nN3 -> N7, N6\nN6 -> N1, N9\nN2 -> terminal\nN7 -> terminal\nN9 -> terminal\nN5 -> N2\nN1 -> N4, N9\nN0 -> N8, N5\n\nLegal moves: N2assistant\n", "response": "<reason>Starting at N5, the only legal move is to N2. N2 leads to terminal, so the player who moves to N2 wins immediately (the opponent has no move). Thus, moving to N2 is the only option and results in an immediate win. No other move is available from N5. Therefore, N2 is the optimal choice.</reason>\n<answer>N2</answer>", "episode_score": 0.05, "llm_raw_text": "<reason>Starting at N5, the only legal move is to N2. N2 leads to terminal, so the player who moves to N2 wins immediately (the opponent has no move). Thus, moving to N2 is the only option and results in an immediate win. No other move is available from N5. Therefore, N2 is the optimal choice.</reason>\n<answer>N2</answer>"}, {"prompt": "system\nYou are playing Directed Acyclic Graph Vertex Geography.user\nThe players alternate moving a token along one directed edge. A player with no legal move loses. Choose one legal destination that maximizes your final game outcome. Keep your thinking process concise.\n\nOutput exactly:\n<reason>your analysis</reason>\n<answer>NODE</answer>\n\nDo not output anything else. A response that does not follow this format results in immediate loss.\n\nCurrent node: N4\n\nDirected graph:\nN7 -> N6\nN5 -> N0\nN3 -> terminal\nN1 -> terminal\nN9 -> terminal\nN8 -> N9, N3\nN0 -> N1, N8\nN6 -> terminal\nN4 -> N7, N2, N5\nN2 -> N8, N5\n\nLegal moves: N7, N2, N5assistant\n", "response": "<reason>From N4, the legal moves are to N7, N2, and N5. N7 leads to N6, which is terminal, so the player who moves to N7 wins immediately (opponent has no move). N5 leads to N0, then from N0, the opponent can go to N1 or N8. N1 and N9 are terminal, so if the opponent chooses N1 or N8, they win. From N8, they can go to N9 or N3, both terminal. Thus, from N4 → N5, the opponent can force a win via N0 → N8 → N9. N2 leads to N8 or N5. From N8 again, the opponent may have winning paths. However, the critical point is that N7 → N6 is terminal, so moving to N7 wins immediately. Thus, choosing N7 is optimal.</reason>\n<answer>N7</answer>", "episode_score": -0.6166666666666667, "llm_raw_text": "<reason>From N4, the legal moves are to N7, N2, and N5. N7 leads to N6, which is terminal, so the player who moves to N7 wins immediately (opponent has no move). N5 leads to N0, then from N0, the opponent can go to N1 or N8. N1 and N9 are terminal, so if the opponent chooses N1 or N8, they win. From N8, they can go to N9 or N3, both terminal. Thus, from N4 → N5, the opponent can force a win via N0 → N8 → N9. N2 leads to N8 or N5. From N8 again, the opponent may have winning paths. However, the critical point is that N7 → N6 is terminal, so moving to N7 wins immediately. Thus, choosing N7 is optimal.</reason>\n<answer>N7</answer>"}, {"prompt": "system\nYou are playing Directed Acyclic Graph Vertex Geography.user\nThe players alternate moving a token along one directed edge. A player with no legal move loses. Choose one legal destination that maximizes your final game outcome. Keep your thinking process concise.\n\nOutput exactly:\n<reason>your analysis</reason>\n<answer>NODE</answer>\n\nDo not output anything else. A response that does not follow this format results in immediate loss.\n\nCurrent node: N7\n\nDirected graph:\nN7 -> N6\nN5 -> N0\nN3 -> terminal\nN1 -> terminal\nN9 -> terminal\nN8 -> N9, N3\nN0 -> N1, N8\nN6 -> terminal\nN4 -> N7, N2, N5\nN2 -> N8, N5\n\nLegal moves: N6assistant\n", "response": "<reason>Starting at N7, the only legal move is to N6. N6 leads to terminal, so the player who moves to N6 wins immediately. Thus, moving to N6 results in an immediate win. No other move is available from N7. Therefore, N6 is the optimal choice.</reason>\n<answer>N6</answer>", "episode_score": 0.05, "llm_raw_text": "<reason>Starting at N7, the only legal move is to N6. N6 leads to terminal, so the player who moves to N6 wins immediately. Thus, moving to N6 results in an immediate win. No other move is available from N7. Therefore, N6 is the optimal choice.</reason>\n<answer>N6</answer>"}, {"prompt": "system\nYou are playing Directed Acyclic Graph Vertex Geography.user\nThe players alternate moving a token along one directed edge. A player with no legal move loses. Choose one legal destination that maximizes your final game outcome. Keep your thinking process concise.\n\nOutput exactly:\n<reason>your analysis</reason>\n<answer>NODE</answer>\n\nDo not output anything else. A response that does not follow this format results in immediate loss.\n\nCurrent node: N6\n\nDirected graph:\nN4 -> terminal\nN7 -> N0, N4\nN3 -> N1\nN8 -> terminal\nN5 -> N3, N4\nN1 -> terminal\nN9 -> terminal\nN2 -> N7, N5\nN6 -> N2, N3\nN0 -> N9, N8\n\nLegal moves: N2, N3assistant\n", "response": "<reason>From N6, the player can move to N2 or N3. Moving to N3 leads to N1, which is terminal, so the opponent gets no move and wins. Moving to N2 leads to either N7 or N5. From N7, the opponent can go to N0 or N4 (both eventually terminal). From N5, they go to N3 or N4 — again, N3 leads to N1 (terminal), and N4 leads to terminal. Thus, from N2, the opponent has winning options. The move to N3 leads to immediate end of game (win for current player). Thus, choosing N3 is optimal.</reason>\n<answer>N3</answer>", "episode_score": -0.95, "llm_raw_text": "<reason>From N6, the player can move to N2 or N3. Moving to N3 leads to N1, which is terminal, so the opponent gets no move and wins. Moving to N2 leads to either N7 or N5. From N7, the opponent can go to N0 or N4 (both eventually terminal). From N5, they go to N3 or N4 — again, N3 leads to N1 (terminal), and N4 leads to terminal. Thus, from N2, the opponent has winning options. The move to N3 leads to immediate end of game (win for current player). Thus, choosing N3 is optimal.</reason>\n<answer>N3</answer>"}, {"prompt": "system\nYou are playing Directed Acyclic Graph Vertex Geography.user\nThe players alternate moving a token along one directed edge. A player with no legal move loses. Choose one legal destination that maximizes your final game outcome. Keep your thinking process concise.\n\nOutput exactly:\n<reason>your analysis</reason>\n<answer>NODE</answer>\n\nDo not output anything else. A response that does not follow this format results in immediate loss.\n\nCurrent node: N3\n\nDirected graph:\nN4 -> terminal\nN7 -> N0, N4\nN3 -> N1\nN8 -> terminal\nN5 -> N3, N4\nN1 -> terminal\nN9 -> terminal\nN2 -> N7, N5\nN6 -> N2, N3\nN0 -> N9, N8\n\nLegal moves: N1assistant\n", "response": "<reason>Starting at N3, the only legal move is to N1. N1 leads to terminal, so the player who moves to N1 wins immediately. Thus, moving to N1 results in an immediate win. No other move is available from N3. Therefore, N1 is the optimal choice.</reason>\n<answer>N1</answer>", "episode_score": 0.05, "llm_raw_text": "<reason>Starting at N3, the only legal move is to N1. N1 leads to terminal, so the player who moves to N1 wins immediately. Thus, moving to N1 results in an immediate win. No other move is available from N3. Therefore, N1 is the optimal choice.</reason>\n<answer>N1</answer>"}, {"prompt": "system\nYou are playing Directed Acyclic Graph Vertex Geography.user\nThe players alternate moving a token along one directed edge. A player with no legal move loses. Choose one legal destination that maximizes your final game outcome. Keep your thinking process concise.\n\nOutput exactly:\n<reason>your analysis</reason>\n<answer>NODE</answer>\n\nDo not output anything else. A response that does not follow this format results in immediate loss.\n\nCurrent node: N2\n\nDirected graph:\nN7 -> terminal\nN3 -> N9, N7\nN4 -> terminal\nN8 -> terminal\nN6 -> N7\nN2 -> N5, N6\nN1 -> terminal\nN0 -> N1, N4\nN5 -> N3, N0\nN9 -> N8, N6\n\nLegal moves: N5, N6assistant\n", "response": "<reason>From N2, the legal moves are to N5 or N6. Moving to N6 leads to N7, which leads to terminal (win for the player who moved there). Moving to N5 leads to N3 or N0: N3 branches to N9 (to N8 or N6), and N0 to N1 or N4 (both terminal). Branching paths eventually reach terminal. The critical insight: all paths from N5 or N6 eventually end in terminal. However, from N6 directly to N7, the next player faces terminal and thus loses. So moving to N6 forces opponent into terminal move and wins. Thus, choosing N6 is optimal.</reason>\n<answer>N6</answer>", "episode_score": -0.95, "llm_raw_text": "<reason>From N2, the legal moves are to N5 or N6. Moving to N6 leads to N7, which leads to terminal (win for the player who moved there). Moving to N5 leads to N3 or N0: N3 branches to N9 (to N8 or N6), and N0 to N1 or N4 (both terminal). Branching paths eventually reach terminal. The critical insight: all paths from N5 or N6 eventually end in terminal. However, from N6 directly to N7, the next player faces terminal and thus loses. So moving to N6 forces opponent into terminal move and wins. Thus, choosing N6 is optimal.</reason>\n<answer>N6</answer>"}, {"prompt": "system\nYou are playing Directed Acyclic Graph Vertex Geography.user\nThe players alternate moving a token along one directed edge. A player with no legal move loses. Choose one legal destination that maximizes your final game outcome. Keep your thinking process concise.\n\nOutput exactly:\n<reason>your analysis</reason>\n<answer>NODE</answer>\n\nDo not output anything else. A response that does not follow this format results in immediate loss.\n\nCurrent node: N6\n\nDirected graph:\nN7 -> terminal\nN3 -> N9, N7\nN4 -> terminal\nN8 -> terminal\nN6 -> N7\nN2 -> N5, N6\nN1 -> terminal\nN0 -> N1, N4\nN5 -> N3, N0\nN9 -> N8, N6\n\nLegal moves: N7assistant\n", "response": "<reason>Starting at N6, the only legal move is to N7. N7 leads to terminal, so the player who moves to N7 wins immediately. Thus, moving from N6 to N7 results in an immediate win. No other move is available, so this is the only option. Therefore, N7 is the optimal choice.</reason>\n<answer>N7</answer>", "episode_score": 0.05, "llm_raw_text": "<reason>Starting at N6, the only legal move is to N7. N7 leads to terminal, so the player who moves to N7 wins immediately. Thus, moving from N6 to N7 results in an immediate win. No other move is available, so this is the only option. Therefore, N7 is the optimal choice.</reason>\n<answer>N7</answer>"}, {"prompt": "system\nYou are playing Directed Acyclic Graph Vertex Geography.user\nThe players alternate moving a token along one directed edge. A player with no legal move loses. Choose one legal destination that maximizes your final game outcome. Keep your thinking process concise.\n\nOutput exactly:\n<reason>your analysis</reason>\n<answer>NODE</answer>\n\nDo not output anything else. A response that does not follow this format results in immediate loss.\n\nCurrent node: N11\n\nDirected graph:\nN2 -> terminal\nN11 -> N9, N6, N0\nN7 -> N2, N13\nN12 -> N5, N8\nN13 -> terminal\nN4 -> N1, N10\nN5 -> terminal\nN1 -> N6, N7, N5\nN9 -> N12\nN6 -> N3\nN0 -> N4, N9\nN8 -> terminal\nN10 -> terminal\nN3 -> terminal\n\nLegal moves: N9, N6, N0assistant\n", "response": "<reason>Starting at N11, the player can move to N9, N6, or N0. We analyze the outcome of each:  \n- N9 → N12 → (N5 or N8): both N5 and N8 lead to terminal, so N12 ends in a win for the opponent. From N12, no further play, so the player who moves to N12 loses.  \n- N6 → N3 → terminal: player who moves to N3 wins immediately (opponent loses).  \n- N0 → N4 or N9: N4 → N1 or N10. N10 is terminal, so move to N10 ends in opponent's win. N1 → leads to N6, N7, N5 (some are terminal). But chains from N1 can loop or end in win/loss. However, the immediate path from N6 → N3 gives direct terminal, which is a win. Thus, moving to N6 is best as it leads directly to terminal (N3). The other branches lead to longer chains, possibly allowing opponent to win. So, best move is N6.</reason>  \n<answer>N6</answer>", "episode_score": -0.6166666666666667, "llm_raw_text": "<reason>Starting at N11, the player can move to N9, N6, or N0. We analyze the outcome of each:  \n- N9 → N12 → (N5 or N8): both N5 and N8 lead to terminal, so N12 ends in a win for the opponent. From N12, no further play, so the player who moves to N12 loses.  \n- N6 → N3 → terminal: player who moves to N3 wins immediately (opponent loses).  \n- N0 → N4 or N9: N4 → N1 or N10. N10 is terminal, so move to N10 ends in opponent's win. N1 → leads to N6, N7, N5 (some are terminal). But chains from N1 can loop or end in win/loss. However, the immediate path from N6 → N3 gives direct terminal, which is a win. Thus, moving to N6 is best as it leads directly to terminal (N3). The other branches lead to longer chains, possibly allowing opponent to win. So, best move is N6.</reason>  \n<answer>N6</answer>"}, {"prompt": "system\nYou are playing Directed Acyclic Graph Vertex Geography.user\nThe players alternate moving a token along one directed edge. A player with no legal move loses. Choose one legal destination that maximizes your final game outcome. Keep your thinking process concise.\n\nOutput exactly:\n<reason>your analysis</reason>\n<answer>NODE</answer>\n\nDo not output anything else. A response that does not follow this format results in immediate loss.\n\nCurrent node: N6\n\nDirected graph:\nN2 -> terminal\nN11 -> N9, N6, N0\nN7 -> N2, N13\nN12 -> N5, N8\nN13 -> terminal\nN4 -> N1, N10\nN5 -> terminal\nN1 -> N6, N7, N5\nN9 -> N12\nN6 -> N3\nN0 -> N4, N9\nN8 -> terminal\nN10 -> terminal\nN3 -> terminal\n\nLegal moves: N3assistant\n", "response": "<reason>From N6, the only legal move is to N3, which leads to terminal. Thus, the player who moves from N6 to N3 wins immediately, as the opponent has no move. This is the only option, so it is the optimal choice.</reason>\n<answer>N3</answer>", "episode_score": 0.05, "llm_raw_text": "<reason>From N6, the only legal move is to N3, which leads to terminal. Thus, the player who moves from N6 to N3 wins immediately, as the opponent has no move. This is the only option, so it is the optimal choice.</reason>\n<answer>N3</answer>"}]
