[2026-08-13 14:28:48] [agentic_pipeline.py (516)] [INFO] [DRIVER 0 / 1][PID 1538566] [{"prompt": "system\nYou are playing Directed Acyclic Graph Vertex Geography.user\nThe players alternate moving a token along one directed edge. A player with no legal move loses. Choose one legal destination that maximizes your final game outcome. Keep your thinking process concise.\n\nOutput exactly:\n<reason>your analysis</reason>\n<answer>NODE</answer>\n\nDo not output anything else. A response that does not follow this format results in immediate loss.\n\nCurrent node: N5\n\nDirected graph:\nN1 -> N2, N7\nN6 -> terminal\nN0 -> N3\nN8 -> N1, N7\nN4 -> N6, N8\nN7 -> terminal\nN2 -> terminal\nN5 -> N9, N0\nN3 -> terminal\nN9 -> N4, N0\n\nLegal moves: N9, N0assistant\n", "response": "<reason>From N5, the legal moves are to N9 and N0. N0 leads to N3, which is terminal, so the player who moves to N0 wins immediately (the opponent has no move). N9 leads to N4 or N0. N4 leads to N6 (terminal) or N8 (N8 leads to N1 or N7; both eventually lead to terminals). Thus, moving to N9 gives opponent control over longer chains. However, moving directly to N0 ends the game immediately for the opponent. Thus, choosing N0 wins the game. Therefore, N0 is optimal.</reason>\n<answer>N0</answer>", "episode_score": -0.95, "llm_raw_text": "<reason>From N5, the legal moves are to N9 and N0. N0 leads to N3, which is terminal, so the player who moves to N0 wins immediately (the opponent has no move). N9 leads to N4 or N0. N4 leads to N6 (terminal) or N8 (N8 leads to N1 or N7; both eventually lead to terminals). Thus, moving to N9 gives opponent control over longer chains. However, moving directly to N0 ends the game immediately for the opponent. Thus, choosing N0 wins the game. Therefore, N0 is optimal.</reason>\n<answer>N0</answer>"}, {"prompt": "system\nYou are playing Directed Acyclic Graph Vertex Geography.user\nThe players alternate moving a token along one directed edge. A player with no legal move loses. Choose one legal destination that maximizes your final game outcome. Keep your thinking process concise.\n\nOutput exactly:\n<reason>your analysis</reason>\n<answer>NODE</answer>\n\nDo not output anything else. A response that does not follow this format results in immediate loss.\n\nCurrent node: N0\n\nDirected graph:\nN1 -> N2, N7\nN6 -> terminal\nN0 -> N3\nN8 -> N1, N7\nN4 -> N6, N8\nN7 -> terminal\nN2 -> terminal\nN5 -> N9, N0\nN3 -> terminal\nN9 -> N4, N0\n\nLegal moves: N3assistant\n", "response": "<reason>Starting at N0, the only legal move is to N3, which leads to terminal. Thus, the first player (me) moves to N3 and wins immediately. No other move from N0 is available. Therefore, choosing N3 is the only option and results in an immediate win.</reason>\n<answer>N3</answer>", "episode_score": 0.05, "llm_raw_text": "<reason>Starting at N0, the only legal move is to N3, which leads to terminal. Thus, the first player (me) moves to N3 and wins immediately. No other move from N0 is available. Therefore, choosing N3 is the only option and results in an immediate win.</reason>\n<answer>N3</answer>"}, {"prompt": "system\nYou are playing Directed Acyclic Graph Vertex Geography.user\nThe players alternate moving a token along one directed edge. A player with no legal move loses. Choose one legal destination that maximizes your final game outcome. Keep your thinking process concise.\n\nOutput exactly:\n<reason>your analysis</reason>\n<answer>NODE</answer>\n\nDo not output anything else. A response that does not follow this format results in immediate loss.\n\nCurrent node: N5\n\nDirected graph:\nN7 -> N0, N6, N9\nN5 -> N9, N1, N4\nN3 -> terminal\nN4 -> N7\nN8 -> N6\nN1 -> N2\nN9 -> N8, N3\nN0 -> terminal\nN6 -> terminal\nN2 -> terminal\n\nLegal moves: N9, N1, N4assistant\n", "response": "<reason>From N5, the legal moves are to N9, N1, and N4. \n- N1 leads to N2 (terminal), so the player who moves to N1 wins immediately (opponent loses).\n- N4 leads to N7, and then from N7 we can go to N0 (terminal), N6 (terminal), or N9. From any of these, it eventually ends up in a terminal. So N4 eventually leads to a chain where the opponent eventually wins.\n- N9 leads to N8 or N3. N3 is terminal, so opponent wins immediately. N8 leads to N6 (terminal), so opponent will eventually win after the move chain.\n\nN1 is the only move that immediately ends the game on the opponent’s turn after their move. Thus, choosing N1 wins immediately. Therefore, N1 is optimal.</reason>\n<answer>N1</answer>", "episode_score": -0.6166666666666667, "llm_raw_text": "<reason>From N5, the legal moves are to N9, N1, and N4. \n- N1 leads to N2 (terminal), so the player who moves to N1 wins immediately (opponent loses).\n- N4 leads to N7, and then from N7 we can go to N0 (terminal), N6 (terminal), or N9. From any of these, it eventually ends up in a terminal. So N4 eventually leads to a chain where the opponent eventually wins.\n- N9 leads to N8 or N3. N3 is terminal, so opponent wins immediately. N8 leads to N6 (terminal), so opponent will eventually win after the move chain.\n\nN1 is the only move that immediately ends the game on the opponent’s turn after their move. Thus, choosing N1 wins immediately. Therefore, N1 is optimal.</reason>\n<answer>N1</answer>"}, {"prompt": "system\nYou are playing Directed Acyclic Graph Vertex Geography.user\nThe players alternate moving a token along one directed edge. A player with no legal move loses. Choose one legal destination that maximizes your final game outcome. Keep your thinking process concise.\n\nOutput exactly:\n<reason>your analysis</reason>\n<answer>NODE</answer>\n\nDo not output anything else. A response that does not follow this format results in immediate loss.\n\nCurrent node: N1\n\nDirected graph:\nN7 -> N0, N6, N9\nN5 -> N9, N1, N4\nN3 -> terminal\nN4 -> N7\nN8 -> N6\nN1 -> N2\nN9 -> N8, N3\nN0 -> terminal\nN6 -> terminal\nN2 -> terminal\n\nLegal moves: N2assistant\n", "response": "<reason>Starting at N1, the only legal move is to N2. N2 is a terminal node, so the player who moves to N2 wins immediately, as the opponent has no legal move. Thus, moving to N2 is the only option and results in an immediate win. No other move is available from N1. Therefore, N2 is the optimal choice.</reason>\n<answer>N2</answer>", "episode_score": 0.05, "llm_raw_text": "<reason>Starting at N1, the only legal move is to N2. N2 is a terminal node, so the player who moves to N2 wins immediately, as the opponent has no legal move. Thus, moving to N2 is the only option and results in an immediate win. No other move is available from N1. Therefore, N2 is the optimal choice.</reason>\n<answer>N2</answer>"}, {"prompt": "system\nYou are playing Directed Acyclic Graph Vertex Geography.user\nThe players alternate moving a token along one directed edge. A player with no legal move loses. Choose one legal destination that maximizes your final game outcome. Keep your thinking process concise.\n\nOutput exactly:\n<reason>your analysis</reason>\n<answer>NODE</answer>\n\nDo not output anything else. A response that does not follow this format results in immediate loss.\n\nCurrent node: N1\n\nDirected graph:\nN5 -> terminal\nN2 -> terminal\nN9 -> N0\nN8 -> terminal\nN0 -> terminal\nN3 -> N6, N7\nN1 -> N9, N3\nN7 -> N4, N2\nN6 -> N5, N2\nN4 -> N8, N6\n\nLegal moves: N9, N3assistant\n", "response": "<reason>Starting at N1, the player can move to N9 or N3.  \n- Moving to N9 leads to N0, then terminal (loss for the next player). So current player wins.  \n- Moving to N3 leads to either N6 or N7:  \n  - From N6: leads to N5 or N2 (both end at terminal eventually).  \n    Path N3 → N6 → N5 ends: terminal.  \n    Path N3 → N6 → N2 ends: terminal.  \n  - From N7: leads to N4 and N2.  \n    Path N3 → N7 → N4 → N8 or N6 → both lead to terminal.  \n    Ultimately, all paths from N3 or N9 eventually lead to terminal in opponent’s turn after one of our moves.  \nThus, moving into N9 immediately leads to terminal after one step. From any of N3’s children, the game ends eventually.  \nBest outcome: immediate terminal on opponent’s move by choosing N9. Hence, optimal is N9.</reason>\n<answer>N9</answer>", "episode_score": -0.95, "llm_raw_text": "<reason>Starting at N1, the player can move to N9 or N3.  \n- Moving to N9 leads to N0, then terminal (loss for the next player). So current player wins.  \n- Moving to N3 leads to either N6 or N7:  \n  - From N6: leads to N5 or N2 (both end at terminal eventually).  \n    Path N3 → N6 → N5 ends: terminal.  \n    Path N3 → N6 → N2 ends: terminal.  \n  - From N7: leads to N4 and N2.  \n    Path N3 → N7 → N4 → N8 or N6 → both lead to terminal.  \n    Ultimately, all paths from N3 or N9 eventually lead to terminal in opponent’s turn after one of our moves.  \nThus, moving into N9 immediately leads to terminal after one step. From any of N3’s children, the game ends eventually.  \nBest outcome: immediate terminal on opponent’s move by choosing N9. Hence, optimal is N9.</reason>\n<answer>N9</answer>"}, {"prompt": "system\nYou are playing Directed Acyclic Graph Vertex Geography.user\nThe players alternate moving a token along one directed edge. A player with no legal move loses. Choose one legal destination that maximizes your final game outcome. Keep your thinking process concise.\n\nOutput exactly:\n<reason>your analysis</reason>\n<answer>NODE</answer>\n\nDo not output anything else. A response that does not follow this format results in immediate loss.\n\nCurrent node: N9\n\nDirected graph:\nN5 -> terminal\nN2 -> terminal\nN9 -> N0\nN8 -> terminal\nN0 -> terminal\nN3 -> N6, N7\nN1 -> N9, N3\nN7 -> N4, N2\nN6 -> N5, N2\nN4 -> N8, N6\n\nLegal moves: N0assistant\n", "response": "<reason>Starting at N9, the only legal move is to N0. N0 leads to terminal, so the player who moves to N0 wins immediately (the opponent has no move). Thus, moving to N0 results in an immediate win. No other move is available from N9. Therefore, N0 is the optimal choice.</reason>\n<answer>N0</answer>", "episode_score": 0.05, "llm_raw_text": "<reason>Starting at N9, the only legal move is to N0. N0 leads to terminal, so the player who moves to N0 wins immediately (the opponent has no move). Thus, moving to N0 results in an immediate win. No other move is available from N9. Therefore, N0 is the optimal choice.</reason>\n<answer>N0</answer>"}, {"prompt": "system\nYou are playing Directed Acyclic Graph Vertex Geography.user\nThe players alternate moving a token along one directed edge. A player with no legal move loses. Choose one legal destination that maximizes your final game outcome. Keep your thinking process concise.\n\nOutput exactly:\n<reason>your analysis</reason>\n<answer>NODE</answer>\n\nDo not output anything else. A response that does not follow this format results in immediate loss.\n\nCurrent node: N3\n\nDirected graph:\nN0 -> N2, N6\nN9 -> N4, N8\nN2 -> terminal\nN7 -> N0, N5\nN4 -> terminal\nN5 -> N9, N1\nN8 -> N2\nN1 -> terminal\nN6 -> terminal\nN3 -> N7, N0\n\nLegal moves: N7, N0assistant\n", "response": "<reason>From N3, the legal moves are to N7 or N0. N0 leads to N2 or N6, both of which are terminal (winning for the player who moves to them). N7 leads to N0 or N5. N0 is already analyzed. N5 leads to N9 (to N4 or N8), and eventually N8 to N2 (terminal). Moving to N5 opens a chain that may result in loss due to the backtracking path to N2. Hence, moving directly to N0 leads to immediate win, whereas N7 may result in opponent advantage. Thus, choosing N0 ensures immediate terminal outcome for the opponent and guarantees win.</reason>\n<answer>N0</answer>", "episode_score": -0.95, "llm_raw_text": "<reason>From N3, the legal moves are to N7 or N0. N0 leads to N2 or N6, both of which are terminal (winning for the player who moves to them). N7 leads to N0 or N5. N0 is already analyzed. N5 leads to N9 (to N4 or N8), and eventually N8 to N2 (terminal). Moving to N5 opens a chain that may result in loss due to the backtracking path to N2. Hence, moving directly to N0 leads to immediate win, whereas N7 may result in opponent advantage. Thus, choosing N0 ensures immediate terminal outcome for the opponent and guarantees win.</reason>\n<answer>N0</answer>"}, {"prompt": "system\nYou are playing Directed Acyclic Graph Vertex Geography.user\nThe players alternate moving a token along one directed edge. A player with no legal move loses. Choose one legal destination that maximizes your final game outcome. Keep your thinking process concise.\n\nOutput exactly:\n<reason>your analysis</reason>\n<answer>NODE</answer>\n\nDo not output anything else. A response that does not follow this format results in immediate loss.\n\nCurrent node: N0\n\nDirected graph:\nN0 -> N2, N6\nN9 -> N4, N8\nN2 -> terminal\nN7 -> N0, N5\nN4 -> terminal\nN5 -> N9, N1\nN8 -> N2\nN1 -> terminal\nN6 -> terminal\nN3 -> N7, N0\n\nLegal moves: N2, N6assistant\n", "response": "<reason>Starting at N0, the legal moves are to N2 or N6. N2 and N6 both lead directly to terminal nodes, so moving to either ends the game immediately. Thus, the first player wins by choosing either N2 or N6. Since both are winning moves, either is optimal. N6 is simpler and direct. Therefore, N6 is the best choice.</reason>\n<answer>N6</answer>", "episode_score": 0.05, "llm_raw_text": "<reason>Starting at N0, the legal moves are to N2 or N6. N2 and N6 both lead directly to terminal nodes, so moving to either ends the game immediately. Thus, the first player wins by choosing either N2 or N6. Since both are winning moves, either is optimal. N6 is simpler and direct. Therefore, N6 is the best choice.</reason>\n<answer>N6</answer>"}, {"prompt": "system\nYou are playing Directed Acyclic Graph Vertex Geography.user\nThe players alternate moving a token along one directed edge. A player with no legal move loses. Choose one legal destination that maximizes your final game outcome. Keep your thinking process concise.\n\nOutput exactly:\n<reason>your analysis</reason>\n<answer>NODE</answer>\n\nDo not output anything else. A response that does not follow this format results in immediate loss.\n\nCurrent node: N10\n\nDirected graph:\nN10 -> N5, N4\nN6 -> N3, N2\nN5 -> N0, N8\nN7 -> terminal\nN4 -> N1, N9\nN0 -> terminal\nN2 -> terminal\nN13 -> terminal\nN11 -> N12, N6\nN9 -> N13, N11\nN3 -> N7, N13\nN12 -> terminal\nN1 -> N12, N0\nN8 -> terminal\n\nLegal moves: N5, N4assistant\n", "response": "<reason>Starting at N10, the player can move to N5 or N4. \n\n- Moving to N5: Next moves are to N0 or N8, both terminal. The opponent will lose immediately (they can't move). So this is a winning move.\n- Moving to N4: Next moves go to N1 or N9. \n    - N1 leads to N12 or N0 (terminal), so a move into terminal, opponent loses.\n    - N9 leads to N13 or N11. \n        - N11 leads to N12 or N6. N6 leads to N3/N2. N3 to terminal. N2 terminal.\n        - This chain may allow longer play but eventually leads to dead-ends. Still, due to presence of terminal nodes, these paths are risky and not immediately winning.\n\nHowever, the direct move from N5 (to terminal nodes) wins immediately. N5 → N0/N8 both terminal: game ends after one move to opponent's turn with no options.\n\nThus, N5 is best. Winning move.</reason>\n<answer>N5</answer>", "episode_score": -0.95, "llm_raw_text": "<reason>Starting at N10, the player can move to N5 or N4. \n\n- Moving to N5: Next moves are to N0 or N8, both terminal. The opponent will lose immediately (they can't move). So this is a winning move.\n- Moving to N4: Next moves go to N1 or N9. \n    - N1 leads to N12 or N0 (terminal), so a move into terminal, opponent loses.\n    - N9 leads to N13 or N11. \n        - N11 leads to N12 or N6. N6 leads to N3/N2. N3 to terminal. N2 terminal.\n        - This chain may allow longer play but eventually leads to dead-ends. Still, due to presence of terminal nodes, these paths are risky and not immediately winning.\n\nHowever, the direct move from N5 (to terminal nodes) wins immediately. N5 → N0/N8 both terminal: game ends after one move to opponent's turn with no options.\n\nThus, N5 is best. Winning move.</reason>\n<answer>N5</answer>"}, {"prompt": "system\nYou are playing Directed Acyclic Graph Vertex Geography.user\nThe players alternate moving a token along one directed edge. A player with no legal move loses. Choose one legal destination that maximizes your final game outcome. Keep your thinking process concise.\n\nOutput exactly:\n<reason>your analysis</reason>\n<answer>NODE</answer>\n\nDo not output anything else. A response that does not follow this format results in immediate loss.\n\nCurrent node: N5\n\nDirected graph:\nN10 -> N5, N4\nN6 -> N3, N2\nN5 -> N0, N8\nN7 -> terminal\nN4 -> N1, N9\nN0 -> terminal\nN2 -> terminal\nN13 -> terminal\nN11 -> N12, N6\nN9 -> N13, N11\nN3 -> N7, N13\nN12 -> terminal\nN1 -> N12, N0\nN8 -> terminal\n\nLegal moves: N0, N8assistant\n", "response": "<reason>From N5, the legal moves are to N0 and N8. Both N0 and N8 lead to terminal nodes, so the player who moves to either wins immediately (the opponent has no move). Thus, both moves end the game on the next turn. Since the current player moves first from N5, choosing either N0 or N8 results in an immediate win. Both are equivalent in outcome. We choose one. N8 is selected.</reason>\n<answer>N8</answer>", "episode_score": 0.05, "llm_raw_text": "<reason>From N5, the legal moves are to N0 and N8. Both N0 and N8 lead to terminal nodes, so the player who moves to either wins immediately (the opponent has no move). Thus, both moves end the game on the next turn. Since the current player moves first from N5, choosing either N0 or N8 results in an immediate win. Both are equivalent in outcome. We choose one. N8 is selected.</reason>\n<answer>N8</answer>"}]
