re terminal nodes, meaning the player who moves to them wins immediately since the opponent has no legal move. Thus, either move ends the game in a win for the current player. Since both options lead to an immediate win, either is optimal. However, choosing N9 or N8 is equivalent in outcome. We select one. N9 is chosen.</reason>\n<answer>N9</answer>", "episode_score": 0.05, "llm_raw_text": "<reason>Starting at N11, the legal moves are to N8 and N9. Both N8 and N9 are terminal nodes, meaning the player who moves to them wins immediately since the opponent has no legal move. Thus, either move ends the game in a win for the current player. Since both options lead to an immediate win, either is optimal. However, choosing N9 or N8 is equivalent in outcome. We select one. N9 is chosen.</reason>\n<answer>N9</answer>"}, {"prompt": "system\nYou are playing Directed Acyclic Graph Vertex Geography.user\nThe players alternate moving a token along one directed edge. A player with no legal move loses. Choose one legal destination that maximizes your final game outcome. Keep your thinking process concise.\n\nOutput exactly:\n<reason>your analysis</reason>\n<answer>NODE</answer>\n\nDo not output anything else. A response that does not follow this format results in immediate loss.\n\nCurrent node: N4\n\nDirected graph:\nN8 -> N7, N3\nN3 -> N6\nN4 -> N2, N5\nN2 -> N5, N0\nN9 -> terminal\nN6 -> terminal\nN0 -> N8, N1\nN1 -> terminal\nN5 -> N1, N9\nN7 -> terminal\n\nLegal moves: N2, N5assistant\n", "response": "<reason>From N4, the legal moves are to N2 and N5. N2 leads to N5 or N0. N5 leads to N1 or N9. Both N1 and N9 are terminal. From N0, a move leads to N8 or N1, which eventually leads to a terminal node. N8 leads to N7 or N3. N3 leads to N6 (terminal). N7 and N6 are terminal nodes. All paths eventually end in terminal nodes. The key is to avoid giving the opponent control over the edge leading to a terminal node. Since N5 directly goes to terminal nodes N1 and N9, and N2 leads int