on that maximizes your final game outcome. Keep your thinking process concise.\n\nOutput exactly:\n<reason>your analysis</reason>\n<answer>NODE</answer>\n\nDo not output anything else. A response that does not follow this format results in immediate loss.\n\nCurrent node: N1\n\nDirected graph:\nN0 -> N9, N2\nN4 -> N6\nN3 -> terminal\nN8 -> N0, N2\nN2 -> terminal\nN7 -> N5, N1\nN9 -> terminal\nN5 -> N4, N8\nN1 -> N3, N4\nN6 -> terminal\n\nLegal moves: N3, N4assistant\n", "response": "<reason>Starting at N1, the legal moves are to N3 or N4. N3 leads directly to terminal, so the player who moves to N3 wins immediately (the opponent has no move). Thus, moving to N3 is a winning move. Moving to N4 leads to N6, which is terminal, so the opponent wins. Therefore, choosing N3 maximizes the outcome.</reason>\n<answer>N3</answer>", "episode_score": 1.05, "llm_raw_text": "<reason>Starting at N1, the legal moves are to N3 or N4. N3 leads directly to terminal, so the player who moves to N3 wins immediately (the opponent has no move). Thus, moving to N3 is a winning move. Moving to N4 leads to N6, which is terminal, so the opponent wins. Therefore, choosing N3 maximizes the outcome.</reason>\n<answer>N3</answer>"}, {"prompt": "system\nYou are playing Directed Acyclic Graph Vertex Geography.user\nThe players alternate moving a token along one directed edge. A player with no legal move loses. Choose one legal destination that maximizes your final game outcome. Keep your thinking process concise.\n\nOutput exactly:\n<reason>your analysis</reason>\n<answer>NODE</answer>\n\nDo not output anything else. A response that does not follow this format results in immediate loss.\n\nCurrent node: N9\n\nDirected graph:\nN1 -> terminal\nN6 -> N8, N2\nN5 -> terminal\nN3 -> N4, N9\nN8 -> N5\nN9 -> N6, N7\nN7 -> terminal\nN0 -> N1, N2\nN4 -> N0, N9\nN2 -> terminal\n\nLegal moves: N6, N7assistant\n", "response": "<reason>Starting at N9, the legal moves are to N6 or N7. N7 leads directly to terminal