ed edge. A player with no legal move loses. Choose one legal destination that maximizes your final game outcome. Keep your thinking process concise.\n\nOutput exactly:\n<reason>your analysis</reason>\n<answer>NODE</answer>\n\nDo not output anything else. A response that does not follow this format results in immediate loss.\n\nCurrent node: N4\n\nDirected graph:\nN6 -> terminal\nN1 -> terminal\nN8 -> N0, N3\nN4 -> N1, N6\nN9 -> N2, N6\nN5 -> N7, N4\nN7 -> N8\nN2 -> terminal\nN3 -> N0, N9\nN0 -> terminal\n\nLegal moves: N1, N6assistant\n", "response": "<reason>From N4, the legal moves are to N1 and N6. N1 and N6 both lead to terminal nodes, so moving to either results in an immediate win for the player who makes the move (the opponent gets no move). Thus, both moves end the game immediately. Since the player who moves to a terminal node wins (the opponent has no legal move), either choice is winning. However, N6 leads directly to terminal, and N1 also does. Both are equivalent in outcome. Choosing either is optimal. We pick N6 as it is a direct terminal move.</reason>\n<answer>N6</answer>", "episode_score": 0.05, "llm_raw_text": "<reason>From N4, the legal moves are to N1 and N6. N1 and N6 both lead to terminal nodes, so moving to either results in an immediate win for the player who makes the move (the opponent gets no move). Thus, both moves end the game immediately. Since the player who moves to a terminal node wins (the opponent has no legal move), either choice is winning. However, N6 leads directly to terminal, and N1 also does. Both are equivalent in outcome. Choosing either is optimal. We pick N6 as it is a direct terminal move.</reason>\n<answer>N6</answer>"}, {"prompt": "system\nYou are playing Directed Acyclic Graph Vertex Geography.user\nThe players alternate moving a token along one directed edge. A player with no legal move loses. Choose one legal destination that maximizes your final game outcome. Keep your thinking process concise.\n\nOutput exactly:\n<reason>your analysis</reason>\n<answer>NODE</answer>\n\nDo not output anything else. A response that does not follow this format results in immediate loss.\n\nCurrent node: N2\n\nDirected graph:\nN6 -> N0, N8\nN9 -> N12, N1\nN13 -> N8, N11\nN1 -> terminal\nN11 -> terminal\nN5 -> terminal\nN10 -> N13, N11\nN8 -> terminal\nN12 -> N3, N0\nN3 -> terminal\nN4 -> N5, N10\nN7 -> N6, N4\nN0 -> terminal\nN2 -> N7, N9\n\nLegal moves: N7, N9assistant\n", "response": "<reason>From N2, the player can move to N7 or N9. Moving to N9 leads to N12 or N1. N1 and N11 are terminal, so N9 leads to a terminal node immediately via N1. Moving to N7 leads to N6 or N4. From N6, the path goes to N0 or N8, both terminal. From N4, path leads to N5 (terminal) or N10. N10 leads to N13 or N11, both terminal. All branches from N7 and N9 eventually end. Since the player who runs out of moves loses, we want to force the opponent into the terminal state. Moving to N9 gives immediate terminal move to the opponent. So choosing N9 wins the game. Thus, N9 is optimal.</reason>\n<answer>N9</answer>", "episode_score": -0.95, "llm_raw_text": "<reason>From N2, the player can move to N7 or N9. Moving to N9 leads to N12 or N1. N1 and N11 are terminal, so N9 leads to a terminal node immediately via N1. Moving to N7 leads to N6 or N4. From N6, the path goes to N0 or N8, both terminal. From N4, path leads to N5 (terminal) or N10. N10 leads to N13 or N11, both terminal. All branches from N7 and N9 eventually end. Since the player who runs out of moves loses, we want to force the opponent into the terminal state. Moving to N9 gives immediate terminal move to the opponent. So choosing N9 wins the game. Thus, N9 is optimal.</reason>\n<answer>N9</answer>"}, {"prompt": "system\nYou are playing Directed Acyclic Graph Vertex Geography.user\nThe players alternate moving a token along one directed edge. A player with no legal move loses. Choose one legal destination that maximizes your final game outcome. Keep your thinking process concise.\n\nOutput exactly:\n<reason>your analysis</reason>\n<answer>NODE</answer>\n\nDo not output anything else. A response that does not follow this format results in immediate loss.\n\nCurrent node: N9\n\nDirected graph:\nN6 -> N0, N8\nN9 -> N12, N1\nN13 -> N8, N11\nN1 -> terminal\nN11 -> terminal\nN5 -> terminal\nN10 -> N13, N11\nN8 -> terminal\nN12 -> N3, N0\nN3 -> terminal\nN4 -> N5, N10\nN7 -> N6, N4\nN0 -> terminal\nN2 -> N7, N9\n\nLegal moves: N12, N1assistant\n", "response": "<reason>Starting at N9, the legal moves are to N12 or N1. N1 leads directly to terminal, so the player who moves to N1 wins immediately (the opponent has no move). Thus, moving to N1 is a winning move. Therefore, the optimal choice is N1.</reason>\n<answer>N1</answer>", "episode_score": 1.05, "llm_raw_text": "<reason>Starting at N9, the legal moves are to N12 or N1. N1 leads directly to terminal, so the player who moves to N1 wins immediately (the opponent has no move). Thus, moving to N1 is a winning move. Therefore, the optimal choice is N1.</reason>\n<answer>N1</answer>"}, {"prompt": "system\nYou are playing Directed Acyclic Graph Vertex Geography.user\nThe players alternate moving a token along one directed edge. A player with no legal move loses. Choose one legal destination that maximizes your final game outcome. Keep your thinking process concise.\n\nOutput exactly:\n<reason>your analysis</reason>\n<answer>NODE</answer>\n\nDo not output anything else. A response that does not follow this format results in immediate loss.\n\nCurrent node: N1\n\nDirected graph:\nN3 -> terminal\nN6 -> N9, N7\nN0 -> terminal\nN8 -> N0, N3\nN4 -> N5\nN1 -> N6, N9\nN9 -> N2, N8\nN2 -> terminal\nN5 -> terminal\nN7 -> N4, N5\n\nLegal moves: N6, N9assistant\n", "response": "<reason>Starting at N1, the player can move to N6 or N9. Moving to N9 leads to N2 (terminal) or N8. From N8, further moves go to N0 (terminal) or N3 (terminal). Moving to N6 leads to N9 or N7. N9 leads to terminal or N8 (a