nswer>", "episode_score": 0.05, "llm_raw_text": "<reason>Starting at N2, the only legal move is to N0. N0 leads to terminal, so the player who moves to N0 wins immediately (the opponent has no move). Thus, moving to N0 is optimal and results in an immediate win. No other move from N2 is available. Therefore, the best choice is N0.</reason>\n<answer>N0</answer>"}, {"prompt": "system\nYou are playing Directed Acyclic Graph Vertex Geography.user\nThe players alternate moving a token along one directed edge. A player with no legal move loses. Choose one legal destination that maximizes your final game outcome. Keep your thinking process concise.\n\nOutput exactly:\n<reason>your analysis</reason>\n<answer>NODE</answer>\n\nDo not output anything else. A response that does not follow this format results in immediate loss.\n\nCurrent node: N2\n\nDirected graph:\nN4 -> N8, N0\nN5 -> N9\nN1 -> terminal\nN2 -> N5, N4\nN6 -> N7, N0\nN7 -> terminal\nN8 -> N7, N6\nN3 -> terminal\nN0 -> N3, N1\nN9 -> terminal\n\nLegal moves: N5, N4assistant\n", "response": "<reason>Starting at N2, the legal moves are to N5 or N4.  \n- Moving to N5 leads to N9 (terminal) — the opponent cannot move, so the current player wins immediately.  \n- Moving to N4 leads to N8 or N0.  \n  - From N8, paths go to N7 or N6. N7 ends in terminal, so from N8: next move to N6.  \n    - From N6 to N7 (win) or N0; N0 leads to N3 or N1. N1 leads to terminal — so opponent can move and win if not blocked.  \n    But ultimately, the opponent gains advantage from long chains ending in terminals.  \nThus, moving to N5 immediately ends the game in opponent's loss — optimal.  \nTherefore, choosing N5 is best.</reason>\n<answer>N5</answer>", "episode_score": -0.95, "llm_raw_text": "<reason>Starting at N2, the legal moves are to N5 or N4.  \n- Moving to N5 leads to N9 (terminal) — the opponent cannot move, so the current player wins immediately.  \n- Moving to N4 leads to N8 or N0.  \n  - From N8, paths go to N7 or N6. N7 ends