o N7 ends the game immediately. N9 also leads to terminal. Thus, both moves end the game immediately. Since the player who cannot move loses, making a move that ends the game wins. Both N9 and N7 are winning moves. However, N7 is a direct terminal move, so it is simpler and safer. Thus, choosing N7 is optimal.</reason>\n<answer>N7</answer>", "episode_score": 0.05, "llm_raw_text": "<reason>Starting at N3, the legal moves are to N9 or N7. N7 leads directly to terminal (win for the player who moves there), so moving to N7 ends the game immediately. N9 also leads to terminal. Thus, both moves end the game immediately. Since the player who cannot move loses, making a move that ends the game wins. Both N9 and N7 are winning moves. However, N7 is a direct terminal move, so it is simpler and safer. Thus, choosing N7 is optimal.</reason>\n<answer>N7</answer>"}]
