imal. We pick N6 as it is a direct terminal move.</reason>  \n<answer>N6</answer>"}, {"prompt": "system\nYou are playing Directed Acyclic Graph Vertex Geography.user\nThe players alternate moving a token along one directed edge. A player with no legal move loses. Choose one legal destination that maximizes your final game outcome. Keep your thinking process concise.\n\nOutput exactly:\n<reason>your analysis</reason>\n<answer>NODE</answer>\n\nDo not output anything else. A response that does not follow this format results in immediate loss.\n\nCurrent node: N6\n\nDirected graph:\nN7 -> N2, N3\nN0 -> terminal\nN2 -> N0\nN8 -> terminal\nN4 -> N5, N6, N1\nN6 -> N8\nN5 -> N7\nN1 -> terminal\nN9 -> N6, N5, N4\nN3 -> terminal\n\nLegal moves: N8assistant\n", "response": "<reason>Starting at N6, the only legal move is to N8, which is a terminal node. Moving to N8 ends the game immediately, and the player who made the move wins (since the opponent has no legal move). Thus, choosing N8 is optimal and guarantees a win.</reason>\n<answer>N8</answer>", "episode_score": 0.05, "llm_raw_text": "<reason>Starting at N6, the only legal move is to N8, which is a terminal node. Moving to N8 ends the game immediately, and the player who made the move wins (since the opponent has no legal move). Thus, choosing N8 is optimal and guarantees a win.</reason>\n<answer>N8</answer>"}, {"prompt": "system\nYou are playing Directed Acyclic Graph Vertex Geography.user\nThe players alternate moving a token along one directed edge. A player with no legal move loses. Choose one legal destination that maximizes your final game outcome. Keep your thinking process concise.\n\nOutput exactly:\n<reason>your analysis</reason>\n<answer>NODE</answer>\n\nDo not output anything else. A response that does not follow this format results in immediate loss.\n\nCurrent node: N8\n\nDirected graph:\nN7 -> N4\nN4 -> terminal\nN2 -> N6\nN9 -> terminal\nN1 -> terminal\nN6 -> terminal\nN0 -> N2, N9\nN8 -> N7, N2, N3\nN5 -> N7, N0, N1\nN3 -> N5\n\nLegal moves: N7, N2, N3assistant\n", "response": "<reason>From N8, the legal moves are to N7, N2, or N3.  \n- N7 → N4 → terminal: the player who moves to N4 wins immediately (the opponent has no move).  \n- N2 → N6 → terminal: opponent wins immediately.  \n- N3 → N5 → N7 → N4 → terminal: opponent eventually wins.  \n\nThus, moving to N7 leads to an immediate win (opponent moves to terminal after N4), while moving to N2 or N3 allows the opponent to win. The best move is to N7.</reason>  \n<answer>N7</answer>", "episode_score": -0.6166666666666667, "llm_raw_text": "<reason>From N8, the legal moves are to N7, N2, or N3.  \n- N7 → N4 → terminal: the player who moves to N4 wins immediately (the opponent has no move).  \n- N2 → N6 → terminal: opponent wins immediately.  \n- N3 → N5 → N7 → N4 → terminal: opponent eventually wins.  \n\nThus, moving to N7 leads to an immediate win (opponent moves to terminal after N4), while moving to N2 or N3 allows the opponent to win. The best move is to N7.</reason>  \n<answer>N7</answer>"}, {"prompt": "system\nYou are playing Directed Acyclic Graph Vertex Geography.user\nThe players alternate moving a token along one directed edge. A player with no legal move loses. Choose one legal destination that maximizes your final game outcome. Keep your thinking process concise.\n\nOutput exactly:\n<reason>your analysis</reason>\n<answer>NODE</answer>\n\nDo not output anything else. A response that does not follow this format results in immediate loss.\n\nCurrent node: N7\n\nDirected graph:\nN7 -> N4\nN4 -> terminal\nN2 -> N6\nN9 -> terminal\nN1 -> terminal\nN6 -> terminal\nN0 -> N2, N9\nN8 -> N7, N2, N3\nN5 -> N7, N0, N1\nN3 -> N5\n\nLegal moves: N4assistant\n", "response": "<reason>Starting at N7, the only legal move is to N4. N4 leads directly to terminal, so the player who moves to N4 wins immediately (the opponent has no move). Thus, moving to N4 is a winning move. No other move from N7 is available. Therefore, the op