[2026-08-13 15:21:42] [agentic_pipeline.py (516)] [INFO] [DRIVER 0 / 1][PID 1538566] [{"prompt": "system\nYou are playing Directed Acyclic Graph Vertex Geography.user\nThe players alternate moving a token along one directed edge. A player with no legal move loses. Choose one legal destination that maximizes your final game outcome. Keep your thinking process concise.\n\nOutput exactly:\n<reason>your analysis</reason>\n<answer>NODE</answer>\n\nDo not output anything else. A response that does not follow this format results in immediate loss.\n\nCurrent node: N3\n\nDirected graph:\nN9 -> terminal\nN3 -> N5, N7, N6\nN8 -> N2, N1\nN5 -> N0\nN6 -> N9\nN0 -> terminal\nN1 -> terminal\nN4 -> terminal\nN7 -> N8\nN2 -> N1, N6, N4\n\nLegal moves: N5, N7, N6assistant\n", "response": "<reason>From N3, the legal moves are to N5, N7, or N6.  \n- N5 → N0 → terminal: First player wins by forcing second player into terminal after a loss.  \n- N7 → N8 → leads to N2 or N1 or N4. All of these eventually go to terminal. So N7 leads to N8, where opponent will have options to go to terminal or to N1/N4 which are terminal. All lead to terminal. So N7 leads to opponent winning.  \n- N6 → N9 → terminal, opponent wins.  \n\nThus, N5 is the best choice as it leads to N0 → terminal, which forces the opponent into losing. So moving to N5 wins the game.</reason>\n<answer>N5</answer>", "episode_score": -0.6166666666666667, "llm_raw_text": "<reason>From N3, the legal moves are to N5, N7, or N6.  \n- N5 → N0 → terminal: First player wins by forcing second player into terminal after a loss.  \n- N7 → N8 → leads to N2 or N1 or N4. All of these eventually go to terminal. So N7 leads to N8, where opponent will have options to go to terminal or to N1/N4 which are terminal. All lead to terminal. So N7 leads to opponent winning.  \n- N6 → N9 → terminal, opponent wins.  \n\nThus, N5 is the best choice as it leads to N0 → terminal, which forces the opponent into losing. So moving to N5 wins the game.</reason>\n<answer>N5</answer>"}, {"prompt": "system\nYou are playing Directed Acyclic Graph Vertex Geography.user\nThe players alternate moving a token along one directed edge. A player with no legal move loses. Choose one legal destination that maximizes your final game outcome. Keep your thinking process concise.\n\nOutput exactly:\n<reason>your analysis</reason>\n<answer>NODE</answer>\n\nDo not output anything else. A response that does not follow this format results in immediate loss.\n\nCurrent node: N5\n\nDirected graph:\nN9 -> terminal\nN3 -> N5, N7, N6\nN8 -> N2, N1\nN5 -> N0\nN6 -> N9\nN0 -> terminal\nN1 -> terminal\nN4 -> terminal\nN7 -> N8\nN2 -> N1, N6, N4\n\nLegal moves: N0assistant\n", "response": "<reason>Starting at N5, the only legal move is to N0. N0 leads to terminal, so the player who moves to N0 wins immediately (the opponent has no move). Thus, moving to N0 is optimal and results in an immediate win. No other move from N5 is available. Therefore, the best choice is N0.</reason>\n<answer>N0</answer>", "episode_score": 0.05, "llm_raw_text": "<reason>Starting at N5, the only legal move is to N0. N0 leads to terminal, so the player who moves to N0 wins immediately (the opponent has no move). Thus, moving to N0 is optimal and results in an immediate win. No other move from N5 is available. Therefore, the best choice is N0.</reason>\n<answer>N0</answer>"}, {"prompt": "system\nYou are playing Directed Acyclic Graph Vertex Geography.user\nThe players alternate moving a token along one directed edge. A player with no legal move loses. Choose one legal destination that maximizes your final game outcome. Keep your thinking process concise.\n\nOutput exactly:\n<reason>your analysis</reason>\n<answer>NODE</answer>\n\nDo not output anything else. A response that does not follow this format results in immediate loss.\n\nCurrent node: N0\n\nDirected graph:\nN1 -> N2, N6\nN11 -> terminal\nN3 -> terminal\nN7 -> N13, N3\nN13 -> N10, N3\nN5 -> N11, N9\nN2 -> terminal\nN12 -> terminal\nN9 -> N2, N12\nN10 -> terminal\nN0 -> N4, N5\nN8 -> N12, N7\nN4 -> N8, N1\nN6 -> terminal\n\nLegal moves: N4, N5assistant\n", "response": "<reason>Starting at N0, the player can move to N4 or N5. We analyze each option:\n\nOption 1: N4 → leads to N8 or N1.  \n- N8 → leads to N12 (terminal) or N7.  \n   → N1 leads to N2 (terminal) or N11 → terminal. So N → terminal.  \n   → N7 → leads to N13 or N3 (both eventually terminal via N13 → N3 or N13 → N10). So all paths from N7 are terminal.  \n- So N4 → N1 ends the game immediately. But N → N8 → N7 → leads to terminal. All paths lead to terminal. So N4 leads to opponent winning from any branching unless player controls N7/N13.  \n\nOption 2: N5 → leads to N11 or N9  \n- N11 → terminal  \n- N9 → N2 → terminal; N9 → N12 → terminal  \n→ both end immediately → all moves to N11/N9 end game (opponent loses on next move). So N5 leads to opponent immediate loss — best choice\n\nSince N5 leads to terminal for opponent, it is optimal to move to N5. The player who chooses N5 wins immediately (opponent loses on next move). Therefore, N5 is optimal.</reason>\n<answer>N5</answer>", "episode_score": -0.95, "llm_raw_text": "<reason>Starting at N0, the player can move to N4 or N5. We analyze each option:\n\nOption 1: N4 → leads to N8 or N1.  \n- N8 → leads to N12 (terminal) or N7.  \n   → N1 leads to N2 (terminal) or N11 → terminal. So N → terminal.  \n   → N7 → leads to N13 or N3 (both eventually terminal via N13 → N3 or N13 → N10). So all paths from N7 are terminal.  \n- So N4 → N1 ends the game immediately. But N → N8 → N7 → leads to terminal. All paths lead to terminal. So N4 leads to opponent winning from any branching unless player controls N7/N13.  \n\nOption 2: N5 → leads to N11 or N9  \n- N11 → terminal  \n- N9 → N2 → terminal; N9 → N12 → terminal  \n→ both end immediately → all moves to N11/N9 end game (opponent loses on next move). So N5 leads to opponent immediate loss — best choice\n\nSince N5 leads to terminal for opponent, it is optimal to move to N5. The player who chooses N5 wins immediately (opponent loses on next move). Therefore, N5 is optimal.</reason>\n<answer>N5</answer>"}, {"prompt": "system\nYou are playing Directed Acyclic Graph Vertex Geography.user\nThe players alternate moving a token along one directed edge. A player with no legal move loses. Choose one legal destination that maximizes your final game outcome. Keep your thinking process concise.\n\nOutput exactly:\n<reason>your analysis</reason>\n<answer>NODE</answer>\n\nDo not output anything else. A response that does not follow this format results in immediate loss.\n\nCurrent node: N5\n\nDirected graph:\nN1 -> N2, N6\nN11 -> terminal\nN3 -> terminal\nN7 -> N13, N3\nN13 -> N10, N3\nN5 -> N11, N9\nN2 -> terminal\nN12 -> terminal\nN9 -> N2, N12\nN10 -> terminal\nN0 -> N4, N5\nN8 -> N12, N7\nN4 -> N8, N1\nN6 -> terminal\n\nLegal moves: N11, N9assistant\n", "response": "<reason>Starting at N5, the legal moves are to N11 or N9. N11 leads directly to terminal (win for the player who moves there, as the opponent has no move). N9 leads to N2 or N12, both of which are terminal. Thus, moving to N11 wins immediately. Choosing N11 is optimal.</reason>\n<answer>N11</answer>", "episode_score": 1.05, "llm_raw_text": "<reason>Starting at N5, the legal moves are to N11 or N9. N11 leads directly to terminal (win for the player who moves there, as the opponent has no move). N9 leads to N2 or N12, both of which are terminal. Thus, moving to N11 wins immediately. Choosing N11 is optimal.</reason>\n<answer>N11</answer>"}, {"prompt": "system\nYou are playing Directed Acyclic Graph Vertex Geography.user\nThe players alternate moving a token along one directed edge. A player with no legal move loses. Choose one legal destination that maximizes your final game outcome. Keep your thinking process concise.\n\nOutput exactly:\n<reason>your analysis</reason>\n<answer>NODE</answer>\n\nDo not output anything else. A response that does not follow this format results in immediate loss.\n\nCurrent node: N3\n\nDirected graph:\nN6 -> terminal\nN8 -> N6\nN9 -> N4, N7\nN0 -> N2, N6\nN5 -> N9, N0\nN7 -> terminal\nN3 -> N9, N5\nN2 -> terminal\nN1 -> terminal\nN4 -> N8, N1\n\nLegal moves: N9, N5assistant\n", "response": "<reason>Starting at N3, the legal moves are to N9 or N5.  \n- If we move to N9, we reach N4 or N7.  \n  - From N4: N8 or N1. N1 → terminal, so N8 is a move to N6 → terminal. So either path leads to terminal (losing if opponent plays optimally).  \n  - From N7 → terminal, so losing.  \n- From N5 → N0 or N9 → N0 → N2 (terminal) or N6 (terminal). So both terminal paths.  \n\nAll paths from N3 eventually reach terminal. So either choice leads to opponent winning. However, to maximize outcome, we must avoid immediate loss. Both N9 and N5 lead to opponent winning. But since both result in the same outcome, we pick one. Choosing N9 allows access to N4 → N1 (terminal), or N8 → N6 (terminal). Either way, the opponent wins. Similarly N5 leads to terminal quickly. Since both are equivalent, we pick N9 as it is a valid move and does not offer advantage. However, the goal is to maximize final outcome; if both are losing, either is optimal. Choosing N9 is safe and reachable. Thus, N9 is selected.</reason>\n<answer>N9</answer>", "episode_score": -0.95, "llm_raw_text": "<reason>Starting at N3, the legal moves are to N9 or N5.  \n- If we move to N9, we reach N4 or N7.  \n  - From N4: N8 or N1. N1 → terminal, so N8 is a move to N6 → terminal. So either path leads to terminal (losing if opponent plays optimally).  \n  - From N7 → terminal, so losing.  \n- From N5 → N0 or N9 → N0 → N2 (terminal) or N6 (terminal). So both terminal paths.  \n\nAll paths from N3 eventually reach terminal. So either choice leads to opponent winning. However, to maximize outcome, we must avoid immediate loss. Both N9 and N5 lead to opponent winning. But since both result in the same outcome, we pick one. Choosing N9 allows access to N4 → N1 (terminal), or N8 → N6 (terminal). Either way, the opponent wins. Similarly N5 leads to terminal quickly. Since both are equivalent, we pick N9 as it is a valid move and does not offer advantage. However, the goal is to maximize final outcome; if both are losing, either is optimal. Choosing N9 is safe and reachable. Thus, N9 is selected.</reason>\n<answer>N9</answer>"}, {"prompt": "system\nYou are playing Directed Acyclic Graph Vertex Geography.user\nThe players alternate moving a token along one directed edge. A player with no legal move loses. Choose one legal destination that maximizes your final game outcome. Keep your thinking process concise.\n\nOutput exactly:\n<reason>your analysis</reason>\n<answer>NODE</answer>\n\nDo not output anything else. A response that does not follow this format results in immediate loss.\n\nCurrent node: N9\n\nDirected graph:\nN6 -> terminal\nN8 -> N6\nN9 -> N4, N7\nN0 -> N2, N6\nN5 -> N9, N0\nN7 -> terminal\nN3 -> N9, N5\nN2 -> terminal\nN1 -> terminal\nN4 -> N8, N1\n\nLegal moves: N4, N7assistant\n", "response": "<reason>Starting at N9, the legal moves are to N4 or N7. N7 leads directly to terminal (win for the player who moves there, as the opponent has no move). N4 leads to N8 or N1; N8 leads to N6 (terminal), and N1 is terminal. Thus, moving to N7 wins immediately. Choosing N7 is optimal.</reason>\n<answer>N7</answer>", "episode_score": 1.05, "llm_raw_text": "<reason>Starting at N9, the legal moves are to N4 or N7. N7 leads directly to terminal (win for the player who moves there, as the opponent has no move). N4 leads to N8 or N1; N8 leads to N6 (terminal), and N1 is terminal. Thus, moving to N7 wins immediately. Choosing N7 is optimal.</reason>\n<answer>N7</answer>"}, {"prompt": "system\nYou are playing Directed Acyclic Graph Vertex Geography.user\nThe players alternate moving a token along one directed edge. A player with no legal move loses. Choose one legal destination that maximizes your final game outcome. Keep your thinking process concise.\n\nOutput exactly:\n<reason>your analysis</reason>\n<answer>NODE</answer>\n\nDo not output anything else. A response that does not follow this format results in immediate loss.\n\nCurrent node: N0\n\nDirected graph:\nN7 -> N1\nN3 -> terminal\nN9 -> N7\nN0 -> N2, N5, N7\nN1 -> N3\nN6 -> terminal\nN2 -> N4, N9, N8\nN5 -> N2, N6\nN8 -> terminal\nN4 -> terminal\n\nLegal moves: N2, N5, N7assistant\n", "response": "<reason>Starting at N0, the players can move to N2, N5, or N7. We analyze each choice:\n\n- N7 → N1 → N3 (win for next player, so terminal after N1 to N3, current player loses on next move).\n- N2 → splits: N4 (terminal, win), N9 → N7 → N2 → infinite or N6 (terminal), N8 (terminal). N2 → N4 or N8 wins immediately (opponent loses). So N2 is good.\n- N5 → N2 → N4 or N8 (wins), N5 → N6 → terminal, so opponent wins immediately. But can move to N2 → winning.\n\nBest is to move to N2. From N2, choosing N4 or N8 leads directly to terminal and opponent loses. Thus, choosing N2 gives control. N7 leads to N1 then N3 or back, risky. N5 can be good, but N2 provides more control. Optimal choice is N2 to exploit terminal moves and force opponent to face a terminal node. Thus, the optimal first move is to N2.</reason>\n<answer>N2</answer>", "episode_score": -0.6166666666666667, "llm_raw_text": "<reason>Starting at N0, the players can move to N2, N5, or N7. We analyze each choice:\n\n- N7 → N1 → N3 (win for next player, so terminal after N1 to N3, current player loses on next move).\n- N2 → splits: N4 (terminal, win), N9 → N7 → N2 → infinite or N6 (terminal), N8 (terminal). N2 → N4 or N8 wins immediately (opponent loses). So N2 is good.\n- N5 → N2 → N4 or N8 (wins), N5 → N6 → terminal, so opponent wins immediately. But can move to N2 → winning.\n\nBest is to move to N2. From N2, choosing N4 or N8 leads directly to terminal and opponent loses. Thus, choosing N2 gives control. N7 leads to N1 then N3 or back, risky. N5 can be good, but N2 provides more control. Optimal choice is N2 to exploit terminal moves and force opponent to face a terminal node. Thus, the optimal first move is to N2.</reason>\n<answer>N2</answer>"}, {"prompt": "system\nYou are playing Directed Acyclic Graph Vertex Geography.user\nThe players alternate moving a token along one directed edge. A player with no legal move loses. Choose one legal destination that maximizes your final game outcome. Keep your thinking process concise.\n\nOutput exactly:\n<reason>your analysis</reason>\n<answer>NODE</answer>\n\nDo not output anything else. A response that does not follow this format results in immediate loss.\n\nCurrent node: N2\n\nDirected graph:\nN7 -> N1\nN3 -> terminal\nN9 -> N7\nN0 -> N2, N5, N7\nN1 -> N3\nN6 -> terminal\nN2 -> N4, N9, N8\nN5 -> N2, N6\nN8 -> terminal\nN4 -> terminal\n\nLegal moves: N4, N9, N8assistant\n", "response": "<reason>Starting at N2, the legal moves are to N4, N9, or N8. N4 and N8 lead directly to terminal nodes, so the player who moves to them wins immediately (the opponent has no move). N9 leads to N7, and from N7 we go to N1, then to N3 (terminal). Thus, moving to N9 results in a loss. Therefore, the optimal moves are to N4 or N8, both of which end the game immediately. Since both are winning moves, either is valid. Choosing N8 is safe and terminal. However, N4 also wins. But as both are terminal, either is optimal. We pick one. N8 is chosen.</reason>\n<answer>N8</answer>", "episode_score": 0.7166666666666668, "llm_raw_text": "<reason>Starting at N2, the legal moves are to N4, N9, or N8. N4 and N8 lead directly to terminal nodes, so the player who moves to them wins immediately (the opponent has no move). N9 leads to N7, and from N7 we go to N1, then to N3 (terminal). Thus, moving to N9 results in a loss. Therefore, the optimal moves are to N4 or N8, both of which end the game immediately. Since both are winning moves, either is valid. Choosing N8 is safe and terminal. However, N4 also wins. But as both are terminal, either is optimal. We pick one. N8 is chosen.</reason>\n<answer>N8</answer>"}, {"prompt": "system\nYou are playing Directed Acyclic Graph Vertex Geography.user\nThe players alternate moving a token along one directed edge. A player with no legal move loses. Choose one legal destination that maximizes your final game outcome. Keep your thinking process concise.\n\nOutput exactly:\n<reason>your analysis</reason>\n<answer>NODE</answer>\n\nDo not output anything else. A response that does not follow this format results in immediate loss.\n\nCurrent node: N12\n\nDirected graph:\nN0 -> N6, N2\nN5 -> terminal\nN13 -> N6, N11\nN2 -> N5, N9\nN8 -> N10\nN3 -> N0, N4\nN12 -> N11, N3, N8\nN9 -> terminal\nN7 -> terminal\nN10 -> terminal\nN6 -> terminal\nN11 -> N1\nN1 -> terminal\nN4 -> N2, N7, N13\n\nLegal moves: N11, N3, N8assistant\n", "response": "<reason>Starting at N12, the legal moves are to N11, N3, or N8. We analyze each:\n\n- N3 leads to N0 or N4. N0 leads to N6 or N2. N2 leads to N5 (terminal) or N9 (terminal); N6 or N9 end the game immediately. N4 leads to N2, N7, or N13. N7 ends; N2 as above; N13 → N6 (terminal) or N11 → N1 (terminal). All paths lead to terminal. Thus N3 leads to a loss for the player who moves next (opponent wins).\n\n- N8 leads to N10 (terminal). So opponent has no move, so current player wins.\n\n- N11 leads to N1 → terminal, opponent wins.\n\nClearly, N8 is a winning move — opponent gets no move after. Thus, choosing N8 is optimal.</reason>\n<answer>N8</answer>", "episode_score": -0.6166666666666667, "llm_raw_text": "<reason>Starting at N12, the legal moves are to N11, N3, or N8. We analyze each:\n\n- N3 leads to N0 or N4. N0 leads to N6 or N2. N2 leads to N5 (terminal) or N9 (terminal); N6 or N9 end the game immediately. N4 leads to N2, N7, or N13. N7 ends; N2 as above; N13 → N6 (terminal) or N11 → N1 (terminal). All paths lead to terminal. Thus N3 leads to a loss for the player who moves next (opponent wins).\n\n- N8 leads to N10 (terminal). So opponent has no move, so current player wins.\n\n- N11 leads to N1 → terminal, opponent wins.\n\nClearly, N8 is a winning move — opponent gets no move after. Thus, choosing N8 is optimal.</reason>\n<answer>N8</answer>"}, {"prompt": "system\nYou are playing Directed Acyclic Graph Vertex Geography.user\nThe players alternate moving a token along one directed edge. A player with no legal move loses. Choose one legal destination that maximizes your final game outcome. Keep your thinking process concise.\n\nOutput exactly:\n<reason>your analysis</reason>\n<answer>NODE</answer>\n\nDo not output anything else. A response that does not follow this format results in immediate loss.\n\nCurrent node: N8\n\nDirected graph:\nN0 -> N6, N2\nN5 -> terminal\nN13 -> N6, N11\nN2 -> N5, N9\nN8 -> N10\nN3 -> N0, N4\nN12 -> N11, N3, N8\nN9 -> terminal\nN7 -> terminal\nN10 -> terminal\nN6 -> terminal\nN11 -> N1\nN1 -> terminal\nN4 -> N2, N7, N13\n\nLegal moves: N10assistant\n", "response": "<reason>Starting at N8, the only legal move is to N10, which is a terminal node. Moving to N10 ends the game immediately, and the player who made the move wins (since the opponent has no legal move). Thus, choosing N10 is optimal and results in an immediate win.</reason>\n<answer>N10</answer>", "episode_score": 0.05, "llm_raw_text": "<reason>Starting at N8, the only legal move is to N10, which is a terminal node. Moving to N10 ends the game immediately, and the player who made the move wins (since the opponent has no legal move). Thus, choosing N10 is optimal and results in an immediate win.</reason>\n<answer>N10</answer>"}]
