[2026-08-13 15:23:52] [agentic_pipeline.py (516)] [INFO] [DRIVER 0 / 1][PID 1538566] [{"prompt": "system\nYou are playing Directed Acyclic Graph Vertex Geography.user\nThe players alternate moving a token along one directed edge. A player with no legal move loses. Choose one legal destination that maximizes your final game outcome. Keep your thinking process concise.\n\nOutput exactly:\n<reason>your analysis</reason>\n<answer>NODE</answer>\n\nDo not output anything else. A response that does not follow this format results in immediate loss.\n\nCurrent node: N6\n\nDirected graph:\nN8 -> terminal\nN9 -> N8\nN0 -> N1, N2\nN1 -> terminal\nN2 -> terminal\nN5 -> terminal\nN4 -> N5, N0\nN3 -> N9, N7\nN7 -> N4\nN6 -> N9, N7, N3\n\nLegal moves: N9, N7, N3assistant\n", "response": "<reason>From N6, the legal moves are to N9, N7, or N3. N9 leads directly to terminal (win for the player who moves there, as the opponent has no move). N7 leads to N4, from which the opponent can move to N5 (terminal) or N0. N0 leads to N1 or N2, both terminal. Thus, moving to N9 immediately ends the game and wins. Moving to N7 or N3 gives the opponent control. N3 leads to N9 or N7, both of which can be followed by the opponent to terminal. The best move is N9, as it ends the game immediately. Therefore, the optimal choice is N9.</reason>\n<answer>N9</answer>", "episode_score": -0.6166666666666667, "llm_raw_text": "<reason>From N6, the legal moves are to N9, N7, or N3. N9 leads directly to terminal (win for the player who moves there, as the opponent has no move). N7 leads to N4, from which the opponent can move to N5 (terminal) or N0. N0 leads to N1 or N2, both terminal. Thus, moving to N9 immediately ends the game and wins. Moving to N7 or N3 gives the opponent control. N3 leads to N9 or N7, both of which can be followed by the opponent to terminal. The best move is N9, as it ends the game immediately. Therefore, the optimal choice is N9.</reason>\n<answer>N9</answer>"}, {"prompt": "system\nYou a