N4\n\nLegal moves: N3, N1, N6assistant\n", "response": "<reason>Starting at N9, the legal moves are to N3, N1, or N6. We evaluate each:\n\n- N6: leads to N2 or N5, both terminal. So if we go N9 → N6 → N2 or N5, the opponent gets no move. This is a winning move (we win immediately).\n- N1: leads to N8 → from N8, opponent has N4 or N3. N4 is terminal, N3 leads to N7 or N0. N0 → N4 is terminal. All paths eventually terminal. So opponent will win if they follow. N9 → N1 → N8 gives opponent the initiative to move to N3 or N4; they will win unless we can force terminal.\n- N3: N3 → N7 (terminal) or N0 → N4 (terminal). Opponent wins here too.\n\nOnly N6 leads to immediate terminal for opponent. So N6 is optimal.</reason>\n<answer>N6</answer>", "episode_score": -0.6166666666666667, "llm_raw_text": "<reason>Starting at N9, the legal moves are to N3, N1, or N6. We evaluate each:\n\n- N6: leads to N2 or N5, both terminal. So if we go N9 → N6 → N2 or N5, the opponent gets no move. This is a winning move (we win immediately).\n- N1: leads to N8 → from N8, opponent has N4 or N3. N4 is terminal, N3 leads to N7 or N0. N0 → N4 is terminal. All paths eventually terminal. So opponent will win if they follow. N9 → N1 → N8 gives opponent the initiative to move to N3 or N4; they will win unless we can force terminal.\n- N3: N3 → N7 (terminal) or N0 → N4 (terminal). Opponent wins here too.\n\nOnly N6 leads to immediate terminal for opponent. So N6 is optimal.</reason>\n<answer>N6</answer>"}, {"prompt": "system\nYou are playing Directed Acyclic Graph Vertex Geography.user\nThe players alternate moving a token along one directed edge. A player with no legal move loses. Choose one legal destination that maximizes your final game outcome. Keep your thinking process concise.\n\nOutput exactly:\n<reason>your analysis</reason>\n<answer>NODE</answer>\n\nDo not output anything else. A response that does not follow this format results in immediate loss.\n\nCurrent node: N6\n\nDirected graph:\nN6 ->