the opponent has no move). N2 also leads to terminal. Both are terminal moves, so either results in an immediate win for the player who moves. Since both moves end the game immediately, either is valid. However, choosing N13 is safer as it avoids any potential counterplay. But since both lead to terminal, either is optimal. However, N2 leads to N2 terminal, and N13 is terminal. Both are winning moves. But N13 is a direct terminal move with no risk. Thus, N13 is optimal.</reason>\n<answer>N13</answer>", "episode_score": 0.05, "llm_raw_text": "<reason>Starting at N5, the legal moves are to N13 or N2. N13 leads to terminal (win for the player who moves there, as the opponent has no move). N2 also leads to terminal. Both are terminal moves, so either results in an immediate win for the player who moves. Since both moves end the game immediately, either is valid. However, choosing N13 is safer as it avoids any potential counterplay. But since both lead to terminal, either is optimal. However, N2 leads to N2 terminal, and N13 is terminal. Both are winning moves. But N13 is a direct terminal move with no risk. Thus, N13 is optimal.</reason>\n<answer>N13</answer>"}]
