egal destination that maximizes your final game outcome. Keep your thinking process concise.\n\nOutput exactly:\n<reason>your analysis</reason>\n<answer>NODE</answer>\n\nDo not output anything else. A response that does not follow this format results in immediate loss.\n\nCurrent node: N6\n\nDirected graph:\nN4 -> terminal\nN7 -> N5, N0\nN2 -> terminal\nN5 -> N4, N8\nN1 -> N6, N3\nN3 -> terminal\nN0 -> N4, N1\nN6 -> N2\nN9 -> N7, N6\nN8 -> terminal\n\nLegal moves: N2assistant\n", "response": "<reason>Starting at N6, the only legal move is to N2. N2 leads to terminal, so the player who moves to N2 wins immediately (the opponent has no move). Thus, moving to N2 is optimal and results in an immediate win. No other move is available from N6. Therefore, the best choice is N2.</reason>\n<answer>N2</answer>", "episode_score": 0.05, "llm_raw_text": "<reason>Starting at N6, the only legal move is to N2. N2 leads to terminal, so the player who moves to N2 wins immediately (the opponent has no move). Thus, moving to N2 is optimal and results in an immediate win. No other move is available from N6. Therefore, the best choice is N2.</reason>\n<answer>N2</answer>"}, {"prompt": "system\nYou are playing Directed Acyclic Graph Vertex Geography.user\nThe players alternate moving a token along one directed edge. A player with no legal move loses. Choose one legal destination that maximizes your final game outcome. Keep your thinking process concise.\n\nOutput exactly:\n<reason>your analysis</reason>\n<answer>NODE</answer>\n\nDo not output anything else. A response that does not follow this format results in immediate loss.\n\nCurrent node: N12\n\nDirected graph:\nN0 -> terminal\nN7 -> N6, N0\nN13 -> terminal\nN3 -> N8, N9\nN11 -> terminal\nN6 -> N3, N8\nN8 -> terminal\nN9 -> terminal\nN5 -> terminal\nN4 -> N0, N13\nN1 -> N7, N5\nN10 -> N11, N13\nN12 -> N1, N2\nN2 -> N4, N10\n\nLegal moves: N1, N2assistant\n", "response": "<reason>Starting at N12, the player can move to N1 or N2. We analyze the outcomes of each move to maximize the chance of winning (i.e., forcing the opponent into a position with no legal moves). \n\n- Move to N1: Then opponent can go to N7 or N5.\n  - N5 leads to terminal (lose immediately).\n  - N7 leads to N6 or N0:\n    - N6 → N3 → N8 or N9 → both terminal (opponent loses).\n    - N0 → terminal (opponent loses).\n  So both paths from N7 eventually lead to opponent's loss. Thus, N1 leads to a win.\n\n- Move to N2: Then opponent moves to N4 or N10.\n  - N4 → N0 or N13 (both terminal → opponent wins).\n  - N10 → N11 or N13 → both terminal → opponent wins.\n\nSo moving to N2 results in opponent winning immediately.\n\nThus, the optimal move is N1.</reason>\n<answer>N1</answer>", "episode_score": -0.95, "llm_raw_text": "<reason>Starting at N12, the player can move to N1 or N2. We analyze the outcomes of each move to maximize the chance of winning (i.e., forcing the opponent into a position with no legal moves). \n\n- Move to N1: Then opponent can go to N7 or N5.\n  - N5 leads to terminal (lose immediately).\n  - N7 leads to N6 or N0:\n    - N6 → N3 → N8 or N9 → both terminal (opponent loses).\n    - N0 → terminal (opponent loses).\n  So both paths from N7 eventually lead to opponent's loss. Thus, N1 leads to a win.\n\n- Move to N2: Then opponent moves to N4 or N10.\n  - N4 → N0 or N13 (both terminal → opponent wins).\n  - N10 → N11 or N13 → both terminal → opponent wins.\n\nSo moving to N2 results in opponent winning immediately.\n\nThus, the optimal move is N1.</reason>\n<answer>N1</answer>"}, {"prompt": "system\nYou are playing Directed Acyclic Graph Vertex Geography.user\nThe players alternate moving a token along one directed edge. A player with no legal move loses. Choose one legal destination that maximizes your final game outcome. Keep your thinking process concise.\n\nOutput exactly:\n<reason>your analysis</reason>\n<answer>NODE</answer>\n\nDo not output anything else. A response that does not follow this format results in immediate loss.\n\nCurrent node: N1\n\nDirected graph:\nN0 -> terminal\nN7 -> N6, N0\nN13 -> terminal\nN3 -> N8, N9\nN11 -> terminal\nN6 -> N3, N8\nN8 -> terminal\nN9 -> terminal\nN5 -> terminal\nN4 -> N0, N13\nN1 -> N7, N5\nN10 -> N11, N13\nN12 -> N1, N2\nN2 -> N4, N10\n\nLegal moves: N7, N5assistant\n", "response": "<reason>Starting at N1, the legal moves are to N7 or N5. N5 leads directly to terminal (win for the player who moves there, as the opponent has no move). Thus, moving to N5 wins immediately. Moving to N7 leads to N6 or N0. N0 leads to terminal, so that is a win. N6 leads to N3 or N8; N8 is terminal, so that is a win. N3 leads to N8 or N9, both terminal. Thus, all moves from N7 lead to terminal. Therefore, choosing N5 is optimal and guarantees an immediate win.</reason>\n<answer>N5</answer>", "episode_score": 1.05, "llm_raw_text": "<reason>Starting at N1, the legal moves are to N7 or N5. N5 leads directly to terminal (win for the player who moves there, as the opponent has no move). Thus, moving to N5 wins immediately. Moving to N7 leads to N6 or N0. N0 leads to terminal, so that is a win. N6 leads to N3 or N8; N8 is terminal, so that is a win. N3 leads to N8 or N9, both terminal. Thus, all moves from N7 lead to terminal. Therefore, choosing N5 is optimal and guarantees an immediate win.</reason>\n<answer>N5</answer>"}, {"prompt": "system\nYou are playing Directed Acyclic Graph Vertex Geography.user\nThe players alternate moving a token along one directed edge. A player with no legal move loses. Choose one legal destination that maximizes your final game outcome. Keep your thinking process concise.\n\nOutput exactly:\n<reason>your analysis</reason>\n<answer>NODE</answer>\n\nDo not output anything else. A response that does not follow this format results in immediate loss.\n\nCurrent node: N7\n\nDirected graph:\nN1 -> N6, N9\nN3 -> N5, N4\nN2 -> N0\nN0 -> terminal\nN4 -> terminal\nN6 -> terminal\nN5 -> N1, N9\nN7 -> N3, N8, N2\nN8 -> N3\nN9 -> terminal\n\nLegal moves: N3, N8, N2assistant\n", "response": "<reason>Starting at N7, the legal moves are to N3, N8, or N2. We analyze each option to maximize the chance of winning (i.e., forcing the opponent into a terminal position or a losing position):\n\n- Moving to N2: N2 → N0 (terminal), so the next player has no move. So the current player wins immediately.\n- Moving to N8: N8 → N3 → N5/N4. From N3, N5 leads to N1 or N9. N9 leads to terminal, N1 leads back to N6/N9. N6 → terminal. So N3 → N1 → N6 → terminal or N1 → N9 → terminal. Eventually, the opponent will win. N3 → N4 → terminal. This means the opponent will eventually lose, so current player wins.\n- Moving to N3: N3 → N4 (terminal), so opponent wins next move. N3 → N5 → N1 → N6 → terminal, opponent wins. N3 → N5 → N9 → terminal. Opponent wins in both paths.\n\nBest move: N2 leads directly to terminal (current player wins immediately). So N2 is optimal.</reason>\n<answer>N2</answer>", "episode_score": -0.6166666666666667, "llm_raw_text": "<reason>Starting at N7, the legal moves are to N3, N8, or N2. We analyze each option to maximize the chance of winning (i.e., forcing the opponent into a terminal position or a losing position):\n\n- Moving to N2: N2 → N0 (terminal), so the next player has no move. So the current player wins immediately.\n- Moving to N8: N8 → N3 → N5/N4. From N3, N5 leads to N1 or N9. N9 leads to terminal, N1 leads back to N6/N9. N6 → terminal. So N3 → N1 → N6 → terminal or N1 → N9 → terminal. Eventually, the opponent will win. N3 → N4 → terminal. This means the opponent will eventually lose, so current player wins.\n- Moving to N3: N3 → N4 (terminal), so opponent wins next move. N3 → N5 → N1 → N6 → terminal, opponent wins. N3 → N5 → N9 → terminal. Opponent wins in both paths.\n\nBest move: N2 leads directly to terminal (current player wins immediately). So N2 is optimal.</reason>\n<answer>N2</answer>"}, {"prompt": "system\nYou are playing Directed Acyclic Graph Vertex Geography.user\nThe players alternate moving a token along one directed edge. A player with no legal move loses. Choose one legal destination that maximizes your final game outcome. Keep your thinking process concise.\n\nOutput exactly:\n<reason>your analysis</reason>\n<answer>NODE</answer>\n\nDo not output anything else. A response that does not follow this format results in immediate loss.\n\nCurrent node: N2\n\nDirected graph:\nN1 -> N6, N9\nN3 -> N5, N4\nN2 -> N0\nN0 -> terminal\nN4 -> terminal\nN6 -> terminal\nN5 -> N1, N9\nN7 -> N3, N8, N2\nN8 -> N3\nN9 -> terminal\n\nLegal moves: N0assistant\n", "response": "<reason>Starting at N2, the only legal move is to N0. N0 is a terminal node, so the player who moves to N0 wins immediately, as the opponent has no legal move. Thus, moving to N0 is optimal and results in an immediate win. No other move is available from N2. Therefore, the best choice is N0.</reason>\n<answer>N0</answer>", "episode_score": 0.05, "llm_raw_text": "<reason>Starting at N2, the only legal move is to N0. N0 is a terminal node, so the player who moves to N0 wins immediately, as the opponent has no legal move. Thus, moving to N0 is optimal and results in an immediate win. No other move is available from N2. Therefore, the best choice is N0.</reason>\n<answer>N0</answer>"}, {"prompt": "system\nYou are playing Directed Acyclic Graph Vertex Geography.user\nThe players alternate moving a token along one directed edge. A player with no legal move loses. Choose one legal destination that maximizes your final game outcome. Keep your thinking process concise.\n\nOutput exactly:\n<reason>your analysis</reason>\n<answer>NODE</answer>\n\nDo not output anything else. A response that does not follow this format results in immediate loss.\n\nCurrent node: N8\n\nDirected graph:\nN3 -> terminal\nN13 -> N11, N1\nN8 -> N7, N12, N10\nN6 -> N7, N5, N3\nN7 -> N2\nN5 -> N9, N0\nN10 -> N13, N1, N6\nN4 -> terminal\nN2 -> terminal\nN1 -> terminal\nN12 -> N13\nN9 -> N4\nN11 -> terminal\nN0 -> terminal\n\nLegal moves: N7, N12, N10assistant\n", "response": "<reason>Starting at N8, the legal moves are to N7, N12, or N10. We analyze each destination's outcome to maximize our chance of winning (i.e., forcing the opponent into a terminal state on their turn).  \n- N7 → N2 (terminal): opponent wins immediately. Bad.  \n- N12 → N13 → N11 or N1 (both terminal): opponent wins immediately. Bad.  \n- N10 → N13 → N11 or N1 (terminal); N10 → N1 (terminal); N10 → N6 → N7 → N2 (terminal). All paths from N10 lead to terminal states for opponent. So, N10 leads to opponent losing. Thus, N10 is best.  \nThus, choosing N10 is optimal as it leads to terminal states for the opponent.</reason>\n<answer>N10</answer>", "episode_score": -0.6166666666666667, "llm_raw_text": "<reason>Starting at N8, the legal moves are to N7, N12, or N10. We analyze each destination's outcome to maximize our chance of winning (i.e., forcing the opponent into a terminal state on their turn).  \n- N7 → N2 (terminal): opponent wins immediately. Bad.  \n- N12 → N13 → N11 or N1 (both terminal): opponent wins immediately. Bad.  \n- N10 → N13 → N11 or N1 (terminal); N10 → N1 (terminal); N10 → N6 → N7 → N2 (terminal). All paths from N10 lead to terminal states for opponent. So, N10 leads to opponent losing. Thus, N10 is best.  \nThus, choosing N10 is optimal as it leads to terminal states for the opponent.</reason>\n<answer>N10</answer>"}, {"prompt": "system\nYou are playing Directed Acyclic Graph Vertex Geography.user\nThe players alternate moving a token along one directed edge. A player with no legal move loses. Choose one legal destination that maximizes your final game outcome. Keep your thinking process concise.\n\nOutput exactly:\n<reason>your analysis</reason>\n<answer>NODE</answer>\n\nDo not output anything else. A response that does not follow this format results in immediate loss.\n\nCurrent node: N10\n\nDirected graph:\nN3 -> terminal\nN13 -> N11, N1\nN8 -> N7, N12, N10\nN6 -> N7, N5, N3\nN7 -> N2