esults in immediate loss.\n\nCurrent node: N1\n\nDirected graph:\nN1 -> N0, N2, N7\nN3 -> terminal\nN8 -> terminal\nN6 -> terminal\nN0 -> N2, N9\nN2 -> N3\nN7 -> N4, N6\nN5 -> terminal\nN9 -> N5, N7\nN4 -> N8\n\nLegal moves: N0, N2, N7assistant\n", "response": "<reason>Starting at N1, the players can move to N0, N2, or N7. We analyze each option to determine the best move in terms of winning probability. \n\n- Moving to N2 leads to N3, which is terminal (current player loses). So if the opponent follows, the current player loses immediately.\n- Moving to N0: From N0, next moves are N2 or N9. \n  - N2 → N3 (lose)\n  - N9 → N5 (terminal) or N7 → N4 or N6 (terminal). From N9, N7 leads to terminal. So N9 → N7 → N4 → N8 terminal. All routes from N0 eventually end in terminal. \n- Moving to N7 leads to N4 or N6, both terminal nodes. Thus, moving to N7 results in immediate terminal node for opponent, meaning current player wins (opponent loses immediately).\nThus, moving to N7 is a winning move. No matter what, opponent will face terminal. So choosing N7 wins. The best choice is N7.</reason>\n<answer>N7</answer>", "episode_score": -0.6166666666666667, "llm_raw_text": "<reason>Starting at N1, the players can move to N0, N2, or N7. We analyze each option to determine the best move in terms of winning probability. \n\n- Moving to N2 leads to N3, which is terminal (current player loses). So if the opponent follows, the current player loses immediately.\n- Moving to N0: From N0, next moves are N2 or N9. \n  - N2 → N3 (lose)\n  - N9 → N5 (terminal) or N7 → N4 or N6 (terminal). From N9, N7 leads to terminal. So N9 → N7 → N4 → N8 terminal. All routes from N0 eventually end in terminal. \n- Moving to N7 leads to N4 or N6, both terminal nodes. Thus, moving to N7 results in immediate terminal node for opponent, meaning current player wins (opponent loses immediately).\nThus, moving to N7 is a winning move. No matter what, opponent will face terminal. So choosing N7 wins. The best choice is N7.</reason>\n<answer>N7</answer>"}, {"prompt": "system\nYou are playing Directed Acyclic Graph Vertex Geography.user\nThe players alternate moving a token along one directed edge. A player with no legal move loses. Choose one legal destination that maximizes your final game outcome. Keep your thinking process concise.\n\nOutput exactly:\n<reason>your analysis</reason>\n<answer>NODE</answer>\n\nDo not output anything else. A response that does not follow this format results in immediate loss.\n\nCurrent node: N7\n\nDirected graph:\nN1 -> N0, N2, N7\nN3 -> terminal\nN8 -> terminal\nN6 -> terminal\nN0 -> N2, N9\nN2 -> N3\nN7 -> N4, N6\nN5 -> terminal\nN9 -> N5, N7\nN4 -> N8\n\nLegal moves: N4, N6assistant\n", "response": "<reason>Starting at N7, the legal moves are to N4 or N6. N6 leads directly to terminal (win for the player who moves there, as the opponent has no move). N4 leads to N8, which is terminal. Thus, moving to N6 wins immediately. Choosing N6 is optimal.</reason>\n<answer>N6</answer>", "episode_score": 1.05, "llm_raw_text": "<reason>Starting at N7, the legal moves are to N4 or N6. N6 leads directly to terminal (win for the player who moves there, as the opponent has no move). N4 leads to N8, which is terminal. Thus, moving to N6 wins immediately. Choosing N6 is optimal.</reason>\n<answer>N6</answer>"}, {"prompt": "system\nYou are playing Directed Acyclic Graph Vertex Geography.user\nThe players alternate moving a token along one directed edge. A player with no legal move loses. Choose one legal destination that maximizes your final game outcome. Keep your thinking process concise.\n\nOutput exactly:\n<reason>your analysis</reason>\n<answer>NODE</answer>\n\nDo not output anything else. A response that does not follow this format results in immediate loss.\n\nCurrent node: N7\n\nDirected graph:\nN6 -> terminal\nN8 -> N3\nN4 -> N0\nN7 -> N0, N8, N4\nN0 -> N2, N6, N1\nN2 -> N1, N9\nN5 -> terminal\nN9 -> terminal\nN3 -> terminal\nN1 -> N5\n\nLegal moves: N0, N8, N4assistant\n", "response": "<reason>Starting at N7, the player can move to N0, N8, or N4. We evaluate each option to find the one that maximizes the chance of winning, assuming optimal play.\n\n- From N7 → N0: N0 leads to N2, N6, or N1.\n  - N6 → terminal → losing for the next player → win if current player moves to N6\n  - N2 → N1, N9 (N9 terminal; N1 → N5 → terminal)\n  - N1 → N5 → terminal → thus any path from N2 or N1 eventually leads to terminal.\n  Thus, if opponent plays correctly from N0, they may lead to terminal moves.\n  All options from N0 lead to terminal, so if opponent can always force the next player into a win, this is risky.\n\n- N7 → N8 → N3: N3 → terminal → the current player wins immediately. So opponent cannot recover. So this is a win.\n\n- N7 → N4 → N0: N0 has same branching as above. This brings opponent back into a similar state.\n\nBest outcome is moving to N8 which leads immediately to N3 terminal — next player cannot move, so current player wins. Hence, N8 is the optimal move.</reason>\n<answer>N8</answer>", "episode_score": -0.6166666666666667, "llm_raw_text": "<reason>Starting at N7, the player can move to N0, N8, or N4. We evaluate each option to find the one that maximizes the chance of winning, assuming optimal play.\n\n- From N7 → N0: N0 leads to N2, N6, or N1.\n  - N6 → terminal → losing for the next player → win if current player moves to N6\n  - N2 → N1, N9 (N9 terminal; N1 → N5 → terminal)\n  - N1 → N5 → terminal → thus any path from N2 or N1 eventually leads to terminal.\n  Thus, if opponent plays correctly from N0, they may lead to terminal moves.\n  All options from N0 lead to terminal, so if opponent can always force the next player into a win, this is risky.\n\n- N7 → N8 → N3: N3 → terminal → the current player wins immediately. So opponent cannot recover. So this is a win.\n\n- N7 → N4 → N0: N0 has same branching as above. This brings opponent back into a similar state.\n\nBest outcome is moving to N8 which leads immediately to N3 terminal — next player cannot move, so current player wins. Hence, N8 is the optimal move.</reason>\n<answer>N8</answer>"}, {"prompt": "system\nYou are playing Directed Acyclic Graph Vertex Geography.user\nThe players alternate moving a token along one directed edge. A player with no legal move loses. Choose one legal destination that maximizes your final game outcome. Keep your thinking process concise.\n\nOutput exactly:\n<reason>your analysis</reason>\n<answer>NODE</answer>\n\nDo not output anything else. A response that does not follow this format results in immediate loss.\n\nCurrent node: N8\n\nDirected graph:\nN6 -> terminal\nN8 -> N3\nN4 -> N0\nN7 -> N0, N8, N4\nN0 -> N2, N6, N1\nN2 -> N1, N9\nN5 -> terminal\nN9 -> terminal\nN3 -> terminal\nN1 -> N5\n\nLegal moves: N3assistant\n", "response": "<reason>Starting at N8, the only legal move is to N3. N3 leads to terminal, so the player who moves to N3 wins immediately (the opponent has no move). Thus, moving to N3 is optimal and results in an immediate win. No other move from N8 is available. Therefore, the best choice is N3.</reason>\n<answer>N3</answer>", "episode_score": 0.05, "llm_raw_text": "<reason>Starting at N8, the only legal move is to N3. N3 leads to terminal, so the player who moves to N3 wins immediately (the opponent has no move). Thus, moving to N3 is optimal and results in an immediate win. No other move from N8 is available. Therefore, the best choice is N3.</reason>\n<answer>N3</answer>"}, {"prompt": "system\nYou are playing Directed Acyclic Graph Vertex Geography.user\nThe players alternate moving a token along one directed edge. A player with no legal move loses. Choose one legal destination that maximizes your final game outcome. Keep your thinking process concise.\n\nOutput exactly:\n<reason>your analysis</reason>\n<answer>NODE</answer>\n\nDo not output anything else. A response that does not follow this format results in immediate loss.\n\nCurrent node: N5\n\nDirected 