owever, N3's path is shorter and more direct. But since all lead to loss for opponent, any is optimal. Choosing N3 is safe and direct. Thus, N3 is selected.</reason>\n<answer>N3</answer>"}, {"prompt": "system\nYou are playing Directed Acyclic Graph Vertex Geography.user\nThe players alternate moving a token along one directed edge. A player with no legal move loses. Choose one legal destination that maximizes your final game outcome. Keep your thinking process concise.\n\nOutput exactly:\n<reason>your analysis</reason>\n<answer>NODE</answer>\n\nDo not output anything else. A response that does not follow this format results in immediate loss.\n\nCurrent node: N3\n\nDirected graph:\nN1 -> terminal\nN3 -> N6\nN8 -> N3, N1\nN7 -> terminal\nN0 -> N8, N7\nN2 -> N0\nN9 -> terminal\nN5 -> N2, N3, N4\nN4 -> N9, N7\nN6 -> terminal\n\nLegal moves: N6assistant\n", "response": "<reason>Starting at N3, the only legal move is to N6. N6 leads to terminal, so the player who moves to N6 wins immediately (the opponent has no move). Thus, moving to N6 is optimal and results in an immediate win. No other move from N3 is available. Therefore, the best choice is N6.</reason>\n<answer>N6</answer>", "episode_score": 0.05, "llm_raw_text": "<reason>Starting at N3, the only legal move is to N6. N6 leads to terminal, so the player who moves to N6 wins immediately (the opponent has no move). Thus, moving to N6 is optimal and results in an immediate win. No other move from N3 is available. Therefore, the best choice is N6.</reason>\n<answer>N6</answer>"}]
