er, since all are equivalent in outcome, pick one. Choose N1.</reason>\n<answer>N1</answer>", "episode_score": -0.6166666666666667, "llm_raw_text": "<reason>Starting at N3, the legal moves are to N10, N1, or N0.  \n- Moving to N10 leads to N12 (terminal) → opponent wins.  \n- Moving to N1 leads to N7 or N5.  \n  - N5 → terminal → opponent wins immediately.  \n  - N7 → N11, N9, N0, N8; N8 and N9 lead to terminal; N7 is a losing move.  \n- Moving to N0 leads to N4 → N6 (terminal), so opponent wins.  \nOnly move to N1 with option to N7 to potentially avoid terminal. But N7 can go to N11 → N8 (terminal) or N9 → N2 (terminal), or N0 → N4 → N6 (terminal). All paths from N7 eventually terminal. All options lead to opponent winning. So all moves result in opponent winning. But since we want to maximize outcome and all are losing, choose one. N1 is best as it opens more options, though still losing. However, since all are equivalent in outcome, pick one. Choose N1.</reason>\n<answer>N1</answer>"}]
