[2026-08-13 15:39:04] [agentic_pipeline.py (516)] [INFO] [DRIVER 0 / 1][PID 1538566] [{"prompt": "system\nYou are playing Directed Acyclic Graph Vertex Geography.user\nThe players alternate moving a token along one directed edge. A player with no legal move loses. Choose one legal destination that maximizes your final game outcome. Keep your thinking process concise.\n\nOutput exactly:\n<reason>your analysis</reason>\n<answer>NODE</answer>\n\nDo not output anything else. A response that does not follow this format results in immediate loss.\n\nCurrent node: N1\n\nDirected graph:\nN8 -> terminal\nN6 -> terminal\nN1 -> N9, N0\nN3 -> terminal\nN2 -> N7, N6\nN7 -> N3, N9\nN0 -> N2, N4\nN5 -> terminal\nN9 -> N5\nN4 -> N8, N5\n\nLegal moves: N9, N0assistant\n", "response": "<reason>Starting at N1, the player can move to N9 or N0. We analyze each choice using backward induction from terminal nodes (which are winning for the player who just moved, as the opponent has no moves).  \n- From N9: N9 → N5 → terminal → the next player loses. So N9 leads to a win for the current player.  \n- From N0: N0 → N2 → N7 → N3 or N9; N3 → terminal or N9 → terminal. Both lead to opponent's win. Alternatively N0 → N4 → N5 or N8, both terminal. So N0 leads to opponent's win.  \nThus, choosing N9 leads to a winning position. The optimal move is to N9.</reason>\n<answer>N9</answer>", "episode_score": -0.95, "llm_raw_text": "<reason>Starting at N1, the player can move to N9 or N0. We analyze each choice using backward induction from terminal nodes (which are winning for the player who just moved, as the opponent has no moves).  \n- From N9: N9 → N5 → terminal → the next player loses. So N9 leads to a win for the current player.  \n- From N0: N0 → N2 → N7 → N3 or N9; N3 → terminal or N9 → terminal. Both lead to opponent's win. Alternatively N0 → N4 → N5 or N8, both terminal. So N0 leads to opponent's win.  \nThus, choosing N9 leads to a winning position. The optimal move is to N9.</reason>\n<answe