ately loses.\n\nThus, moving to N0 gives us an immediate win. Choosing N0 is optimal.</reason>\n<answer>N0</answer>"}, {"prompt": "system\nYou are playing Directed Acyclic Graph Vertex Geography.user\nThe players alternate moving a token along one directed edge. A player with no legal move loses. Choose one legal destination that maximizes your final game outcome. Keep your thinking process concise.\n\nOutput exactly:\n<reason>your analysis</reason>\n<answer>NODE</answer>\n\nDo not output anything else. A response that does not follow this format results in immediate loss.\n\nCurrent node: N0\n\nDirected graph:\nN6 -> terminal\nN7 -> N8\nN3 -> N7, N1\nN5 -> N3, N0\nN0 -> N9, N4\nN8 -> terminal\nN1 -> N2, N8\nN9 -> terminal\nN2 -> N6, N7\nN4 -> terminal\n\nLegal moves: N9, N4assistant\n", "response": "<reason>Starting at N0, the legal moves are to N9 or N4. Both N9 and N4 lead directly to terminal nodes, so the player who moves to either wins immediately (the opponent has no move). Thus, moving to N9 or N4 both result in an immediate win. Since both are winning moves, either is optimal. However, N9 and N4 are terminal, so neither allows the opponent to move. Choosing either is equivalent. We select one. N9 is a valid and optimal choice.</reason>\n<answer>N9</answer>", "episode_score": 0.05, "llm_raw_text": "<reason>Starting at N0, the legal moves are to N9 or N4. Both N9 and N4 lead directly to terminal nodes, so the player who moves to either wins immediately (the opponent has no move). Thus, moving to N9 or N4 both result in an immediate win. Since both are winning moves, either is optimal. However, N9 and N4 are terminal, so neither allows the opponent to move. Choosing either is equivalent. We select one. N9 is a valid and optimal choice.</reason>\n<answer>N9</answer>"}, {"prompt": "system\nYou are playing Directed Acyclic Graph Vertex Geography.user\nThe players alternate moving a token along one directed edge. A player with no legal move loses. Choose one legal