ins.\n- Move to N3 → N3 → N6 → from above, N6 is winning for the next player, so now we are on N6 → eventually leads to opponent's loss. So N3 → N6 → N6 gives us a win.\n\nSo N4 leads to a win as well.\n\nBoth N4 and N6 are winning. But the goal is to maximize final outcome. Since both lead to win, we pick one. Choosing N6 gives immediate access to terminal paths (N1 → N8 or N5), and is simpler. However, N4 also leads to a win. But since N6 has more direct terminal options, and is a known safe move, it is optimal. However, both are winning. But N6 allows a direct terminal win via N5 or N1 → N8. Thus, N6 is safe and direct. We pick N6.</reason>\n<answer>N6</answer>", "episode_score": -0.95, "llm_raw_text": "<reason>Starting at N9, the player can move to N4 or N6. We analyze each choice:\n\nFrom N6:\n- Move to N1 → then N1 → N8 → terminal → opponent loses. So player wins.\n- Move to N5 → terminal → opponent loses. So player wins.\n\nThus, from N6, all moves lead to opponent losing. So N6 is winning.\n\nFrom N4:\n- Move to N2 → from N2: N→N5 (opponent wins), N→N7 (opponent wins), both terminal → opponent wins.\n- Move to N3 → N3 → N6 → from above, N6 is winning for the next player, so now we are on N6 → eventually leads to opponent's loss. So N3 → N6 → N6 gives us a win.\n\nSo N4 leads to a win as well.\n\nBoth N4 and N6 are winning. But the goal is to maximize final outcome. Since both lead to win, we pick one. Choosing N6 gives immediate access to terminal paths (N1 → N8 or N5), and is simpler. However, N4 also leads to a win. But since N6 has more direct terminal options, and is a known safe move, it is optimal. However, both are winning. But N6 allows a direct terminal win via N5 or N1 → N8. Thus, N6 is safe and direct. We pick N6.</reason>\n<answer>N6</answer>"}, {"prompt": "system\nYou are playing Directed Acyclic Graph Vertex Geography.user\nThe players alternate moving a token along one directed edge. A player with no legal move loses. Choose one legal destinat