along one directed edge. A player with no legal move loses. Choose one legal destination that maximizes your final game outcome. Keep your thinking process concise.\n\nOutput exactly:\n<reason>your analysis</reason>\n<answer>NODE</answer>\n\nDo not output anything else. A response that does not follow this format results in immediate loss.\n\nCurrent node: N1\n\nDirected graph:\nN1 -> N3, N2\nN0 -> terminal\nN5 -> terminal\nN7 -> N8, N4\nN2 -> N5\nN9 -> terminal\nN4 -> N9, N0\nN8 -> N5, N4\nN6 -> N7, N1\nN3 -> terminal\n\nLegal moves: N3, N2assistant\n", "response": "<reason>Starting at N1, the legal moves are to N3 or N2. N3 leads directly to terminal (win for the player who moves there, as the opponent has no move). N2 leads to N5, which is terminal. Thus, moving to N3 wins immediately. Moving to N2 results in the opponent winning. Therefore, the optimal move is to N3.</reason>\n<answer>N3</answer>", "episode_score": 1.05, "llm_raw_text": "<reason>Starting at N1, the legal moves are to N3 or N2. N3 leads directly to terminal (win for the player who moves there, as the opponent has no move). N2 leads to N5, which is terminal. Thus, moving to N3 wins immediately. Moving to N2 results in the opponent winning. Therefore, the optimal move is to N3.</reason>\n<answer>N3</answer>"}, {"prompt": "system\nYou are playing Directed Acyclic Graph Vertex Geography.user\nThe players alternate moving a token along one directed edge. A player with no legal move loses. Choose one legal destination that maximizes your final game outcome. Keep your thinking process concise.\n\nOutput exactly:\n<reason>your analysis</reason>\n<answer>NODE</answer>\n\nDo not output anything else. A response that does not follow this format results in immediate loss.\n\nCurrent node: N6\n\nDirected graph:\nN2 -> N3\nN4 -> N0, N1, N8\nN0 -> terminal\nN8 -> N9\nN1 -> terminal\nN7 -> N5\nN3 -> terminal\nN5 -> N4, N9\nN6 -> N5, N7, N2\nN9 -> terminal\n\nLegal moves: N5, N7, N2assistant\n", "response": "<reason>From N6, the legal moves are to N5, N7, or N2. We analyze each destination's outcome:  \n- Moving to N5: From N5, moves to N4 or N9. N9 leads to terminal (win for opponent). N4 leads to N0 or N1 or N8. N0 and N1 are terminal (opponent wins). N8 leads to N9 (terminal). So all paths from N5 lead to terminal eventually - opponent wins.  \n- Moving to N7: From N7 → N5. Then same as above: all paths from N5 lead to terminal. Opponent wins.  \n- Moving to N2: From N2 → N3 (terminal). So current player wins immediately.  \n\nThus, moving to N2 leads to an immediate win. This is the only winning move. Choosing N2 maximizes the outcome.</reason>\n<answer>N2</answer>", "episode_score": -0.6166666666666667, "llm_raw_text": "<reason>From N6, the legal moves are to N5, N7, or N2. We analyze each destination's outcome:  \n- Moving to N5: From N5, moves to N4 or N9. N9 leads to terminal (win for opponent). N4 leads to N0 or N1 or N8. N0 and N1 are terminal (opponent wins). N8 leads to N9 (terminal). So all paths from N5 lead to terminal eventually - opponent wins.  \n- Moving to N7: From N7 → N5. Then same as above: all paths from N5 lead to terminal. Opponent wins.  \n- Moving to N2: From N2 → N3 (terminal). So current player wins immediately.  \n\nThus, moving to N2 leads to an immediate win. This is the only winning move. Choosing N2 maximizes the outcome.</reason>\n<answer>N2</answer>"}, {"prompt": "system\nYou are playing Directed Acyclic Graph Vertex Geography.user\nThe players alternate moving a token along one directed edge. A player with no legal move loses. Choose one legal destination that maximizes your final game outcome. Keep your thinking process concise.\n\nOutput exactly:\n<reason>your analysis</reason>\n<answer>NODE</answer>\n\nDo not output anything else. A response that does not follow this format results in immediate loss.\n\nCurrent node: N7\n\nDirected graph:\nN4 -> N9, N3, N6\nN3 -> terminal\nN8 -> N5\nN2 -> terminal\nN5 -> terminal\nN6 -> N2\nN0 -> terminal\nN9 -> N0, N8\nN1 -> N4\nN7 -> N1, N4, N6\n\nLegal moves: N1, N4, N6assistant\n", "response": "<reason>Starting at N7, the legal moves are to N1, N4, or N6. We analyze each:\n\n- N4 leads to N9 or N3. N3 is terminal (win for opponent), N9 leads to N0 or N8. N0 is terminal, N8 leads to N5 (terminal). So N4 leads to a terminal state eventually. Thus, from N4, the player to move loses.\n- N1 leads to N4. Then the opponent faces N4, which as above leads to terminal states. So N1 leads to opponent's loss.\n- N6 leads to N2 (terminal), so opponent loses immediately.\n\nThus, moving to N6 leads to immediate terminal (opponent loses). Moving to N1 or N4 leads to opponent winning. The best move is N6, as it results in an immediate win for the current player.</reason>\n<answer>N6</answer>", "episode_score": -0.6166666666666667, "llm_raw_text": "<reason>Starting at N7, the legal moves are to N1, N4, or N6. We analyze each:\n\n- N4 leads to N9 or N3. N3 is terminal (win for opponent), N9 leads to N0 or N8. N0 is terminal, N8 leads to N5 (terminal). So N4 leads to a terminal state eventually. Thus, from N4, the player to move loses.\n- N1 leads to N4. Then the opponent faces N4, which as above leads to terminal states. So N1 leads to opponent's loss.\n- N6 leads to N2 (terminal), so opponent loses immediately.\n\nThus, moving to N6 leads to immediate terminal (opponent loses). Moving to N1 or N4 leads to opponent winning. The best move is N6, as it results in an immediate win for the current player.</reason>\n<answer>N6</answer>"}, {"prompt": "system\nYou are playing Directed Acyclic Graph Vertex Geography.user\nThe players alternate moving a token along one directed edge. A player with no legal move loses. Choose one legal destination that maximizes your final game outcome. Keep your thinking process concise.\n\nOutput exactly:\n<reason>your analysis</reason>\n<answer>NODE</answer>\n\nDo not output anything else. A response that does not follow this format results in immediate loss.\n\nCurrent node: N6\n\nDirected graph:\nN4 -> N9, N3, N6\nN3 -> terminal\nN8 -> N5\nN2 -> terminal\nN5 -> terminal\nN6 -> N2\nN0 -> terminal\nN9 -> N0, N8\nN1 -> N4\nN7 -> N1, N4, N6\n\nLegal moves: N2assistant\n", "response": "<reason>Starting at N6, the legal moves are to N2 or N9. N2 leads directly to terminal (win for the player who moves there, as the opponent has no move). N9 leads to N0 or N8; N0 and N8 both lead to terminal. Thus, moving to N2 wins immediately. Moving to N9 allows the opponent to move to N8 or N0, both of which end the game. Therefore, choosing N2 is optimal and guarantees a win.</reason>\n<answer>N2</answer>", "episode_score": 0.05, "llm_raw_text": "<reason>Starting at N6, the legal moves are to N2 or N9. N2 leads directly to terminal (win for the player who moves there, as the opponent has no move). N9 leads to N0 or N8; N0 and N8 both lead to terminal. Thus, moving to N2 wins immediately. Moving to N9 allows the opponent to move to N8 or N0, both of which end the game. Therefore, choosing N2 is optimal and guarantees a win.</reason>\n<answer>N2</answer>"}, {"prompt": "system\nYou are playing Directed Acyclic Graph Vertex Geography.user\nThe players alternate moving a token along one directed edge. A player with no legal move loses. Choose one legal destination that maximizes your final game outcome. Keep your thinking process concise.\n\nOutput exactly:\n<reason>your analysis</reason>\n<answer>NODE</answer>\n\nDo not output anything else. A response that does not follow this format results in immediate loss.\n\nCurrent node: N2\n\nDirected graph:\nN2 -> N3\nN4 -> N0, N1, N8\nN0 -> terminal\nN8 -> N9\nN1 -> terminal\nN7 -> N5\nN3 -> terminal\nN5 -> N4, N9\nN6 -> N5, N7, N2\nN9 -> terminal\n\nLegal moves: N3assistant\n", "response": "<reason>Starting at N2, the only legal move is to N3. N3 leads to terminal, so the player who moves to N3 wins immediately (the opponent has no move). Thus, moving to N3 is optimal and results in an