12, N11\nN3 -> terminal\nN1 -> N5, N2\nN12 -> N2, N7\nN10 -> terminal\n\nLegal moves: N12, N11assistant\n", "response": "<reason>Starting at N0, the players can move to N12 or N11. N12 leads to N2 (terminal) or N7. N2 is terminal, so the player who moves to N2 wins immediately (opponent has no move). N7 leads to N5 (terminal) or N13 (terminal), both terminal. So moving to N12 allows the opponent to move to N7, but then they face a terminal move, so we win. Thus, N12 is a winning move. N11 leads to N1 or N9. N1 leads to N5 or N2 (both terminal), so opponent wins immediately. N9 leads to N8 (terminal) or N6. N6 leads to N4 or N3 (both terminal). So from N11, opponent can force a win. Thus, N11 is losing. Therefore, the optimal move is to N12.</reason>\n<answer>N12</answer>", "episode_score": -0.95, "llm_raw_text": "<reason>Starting at N0, the players can move to N12 or N11. N12 leads to N2 (terminal) or N7. N2 is terminal, so the player who moves to N2 wins immediately (opponent has no move). N7 leads to N5 (terminal) or N13 (terminal), both terminal. So moving to N12 allows the opponent to move to N7, but then they face a terminal move, so we win. Thus, N12 is a winning move. N11 leads to N1 or N9. N1 leads to N5 or N2 (both terminal), so opponent wins immediately. N9 leads to N8 (terminal) or N6. N6 leads to N4 or N3 (both terminal). So from N11, opponent can force a win. Thus, N11 is losing. Therefore, the optimal move is to N12.</reason>\n<answer>N12</answer>"}, {"prompt": "system\nYou are playing Directed Acyclic Graph Vertex Geography.user\nThe players alternate moving a token along one directed edge. A player with no legal move loses. Choose one legal destination that maximizes your final game outcome. Keep your thinking process concise.\n\nOutput exactly:\n<reason>your analysis</reason>\n<answer>NODE</answer>\n\nDo not output anything else. A response that does not follow this format results in immediate loss.\n\nCurrent node: N12\n\nDirected graph:\nN4 -> N10