oosing N3 is safe and direct. However, N4 also guarantees a win. But N3's path includes N12 → N10 → N13 (which is terminal), so opponent has no move. Same with N4. \n\nSince both are winning, and no difference in outcome, pick one. N3 is a valid, optimal choice.</reason>\n<answer>N3</answer>"}, {"prompt": "system\nYou are playing Directed Acyclic Graph Vertex Geography.user\nThe players alternate moving a token along one directed edge. A player with no legal move loses. Choose one legal destination that maximizes your final game outcome. Keep your thinking process concise.\n\nOutput exactly:\n<reason>your analysis</reason>\n<answer>NODE</answer>\n\nDo not output anything else. A response that does not follow this format results in immediate loss.\n\nCurrent node: N3\n\nDirected graph:\nN0 -> terminal\nN5 -> terminal\nN13 -> terminal\nN11 -> N13, N5\nN8 -> N7, N11\nN9 -> N3, N4\nN1 -> N7, N0\nN6 -> terminal\nN2 -> terminal\nN12 -> N10, N0\nN10 -> N6, N13\nN4 -> N1, N8\nN3 -> N2, N12\nN7 -> terminal\n\nLegal moves: N2, N12assistant\n", "response": "<reason>Starting at N3, the legal moves are to N2 or N12. N2 leads directly to terminal (win for the player who moves there, as the opponent has no move). N12 leads to N10 or N0: N0 is terminal, so moving to N0 ends the game immediately. N10 leads to N6 (terminal) or N13 (terminal). Thus, moving to N12 allows the opponent to move to a terminal node immediately. Therefore, choosing N2 wins immediately. The optimal move is to N2.</reason>\n<answer>N2</answer>", "episode_score": 1.05, "llm_raw_text": "<reason>Starting at N3, the legal moves are to N2 or N12. N2 leads directly to terminal (win for the player who moves there, as the opponent has no move). N12 leads to N10 or N0: N0 is terminal, so moving to N0 ends the game immediately. N10 leads to N6 (terminal) or N13 (terminal). Thus, moving to N12 allows the opponent to move to a terminal node immediately. Therefore, choosing N2 wins immediately. The optimal move is to N2.</