[2026-08-13 16:21:16] [agentic_pipeline.py (516)] [INFO] [DRIVER 0 / 1][PID 1538566] [{"prompt": "system\nYou are playing Directed Acyclic Graph Vertex Geography.user\nThe players alternate moving a token along one directed edge. A player with no legal move loses. Choose one legal destination that maximizes your final game outcome. Keep your thinking process concise.\n\nOutput exactly:\n<reason>your analysis</reason>\n<answer>NODE</answer>\n\nDo not output anything else. A response that does not follow this format results in immediate loss.\n\nCurrent node: N5\n\nDirected graph:\nN7 -> N3, N6\nN4 -> N2\nN8 -> terminal\nN9 -> terminal\nN1 -> N8\nN0 -> N7\nN2 -> terminal\nN6 -> N2, N4, N9\nN3 -> terminal\nN5 -> N1, N7, N0\n\nLegal moves: N1, N7, N0assistant\n", "response": "<reason>From N5, the legal moves are to N1, N7, or N0. We analyze each:  \n- N1 → N8 (terminal): wins immediately (opponent has no move).  \n- N7 → N3 or N6:  \n  - N3 → terminal: opponent wins.  \n  - N6 → N2 (terminal), N4, N9 (terminal): N4 → N2 (terminal), so all paths from N7 lead to terminal nodes. Thus, moving to N7 leads to opponent winning.  \n- N0 → N7: then same as above, leads to opponent winning.  \n\nOnly N1 leads to a terminal node immediately, so the player moves to N1 and wins. Thus, N1 is the optimal choice.</reason>  \n<answer>N1</answer>", "episode_score": -0.6166666666666667, "llm_raw_text": "<reason>From N5, the legal moves are to N1, N7, or N0. We analyze each:  \n- N1 → N8 (terminal): wins immediately (opponent has no move).  \n- N7 → N3 or N6:  \n  - N3 → terminal: opponent wins.  \n  - N6 → N2 (terminal), N4, N9 (terminal): N4 → N2 (terminal), so all paths from N7 lead to terminal nodes. Thus, moving to N7 leads to opponent winning.  \n- N0 → N7: then same as above, leads to opponent winning.  \n\nOnly N1 leads to a terminal node immediately, so the player moves to N1 and wins. Thus, N1 is the optimal choice.</reason>  \n<answer>N1</answer>"}, {"prompt": "system\nYou are playing Directed Acyclic Graph Vertex Geography.user\nThe players alternate moving a token along one directed edge. A player with no legal move loses. Choose one legal destination that maximizes your final game outcome. Keep your thinking process concise.\n\nOutput exactly:\n<reason>your analysis</reason>\n<answer>NODE</answer>\n\nDo not output anything else. A response that does not follow this format results in immediate loss.\n\nCurrent node: N1\n\nDirected graph:\nN7 -> N3, N6\nN4 -> N2\nN8 -> terminal\nN9 -> terminal\nN1 -> N8\nN0 -> N7\nN2 -> terminal\nN6 -> N2, N4, N9\nN3 -> terminal\nN5 -> N1, N7, N0\n\nLegal moves: N8assistant\n", "response": "<reason>Starting at N1, the only legal move is to N8, which is a terminal node. Moving to N8 ends the game immediately, and the player who moved loses. Therefore, moving to N8 results in an immediate loss. However, since N1 only has one legal move (to N8), there is no choice available. Thus, the optimal move is to N8, but it results in loss. However, considering the problem asks to choose a legal move that maximizes final game outcome, and no other move from N1 is available, the only legal move is to N8. But since that leads to loss, and no other option exists, the player has no choice but to move to N8. Hence, the answer is N8.</reason>\n<answer>N8</answer>", "episode_score": 0.05, "llm_raw_text": "<reason>Starting at N1, the only legal move is to N8, which is a terminal node. Moving to N8 ends the game immediately, and the player who moved loses. Therefore, moving to N8 results in an immediate loss. However, since N1 only has one legal move (to N8), there is no choice available. Thus, the optimal move is to N8, but it results in loss. However, considering the problem asks to choose a legal move that maximizes final game outcome, and no other move from N1 is available, the only legal move is to N8. But since that leads to loss, and no other option exists, the player has no choice but to move to N8. Hence, the answer is N8.</reason>\n<answer>N8</answer>"}, {"prompt": "system\nYou are playing Directed Acyclic Graph Vertex Geography.user\nThe players alternate moving a token along one directed edge. A player with no legal move loses. Choose one legal destination that maximizes your final game outcome. Keep your thinking process concise.\n\nOutput exactly:\n<reason>your analysis</reason>\n<answer>NODE</answer>\n\nDo not output anything else. A response that does not follow this format results in immediate loss.\n\nCurrent node: N8\n\nDirected graph:\nN6 -> terminal\nN0 -> terminal\nN2 -> N1\nN1 -> N3\nN9 -> N6, N4\nN4 -> N6, N0\nN3 -> terminal\nN8 -> N7, N1, N2\nN7 -> N5, N9\nN5 -> terminal\n\nLegal moves: N7, N1, N2assistant\n", "response": "<reason>Starting at N8, the legal moves are to N7, N1, or N2. We analyze each option to determine which leads to a winning position (i.e., forces the opponent into a losing position). \n\n- Move to N1: N1 → N3 → terminal. Opponent loses immediately. This is a winning move.\n- Move to N2: N2 → N1 → N3 → terminal. Opponent loses immediately. This is also a winning move.\n- Move to N7: N7 → N5 (terminal) or N9. \n  - N5 leads to terminal (opponent loses). \n  - N9 → N6 or N4. \n    - N6 → terminal. \n    - N4 → N6 or N0, both terminal. So all paths from N9 lead to terminal. Thus, N7 leads to opponent's loss.\n\nAll moves from N8 lead to the opponent having no legal move eventually. Since all options win, any choice is optimal. However, N1 and N2 both lead directly to N3. N7 offers more complexity but still wins. Choosing N1 is simple and direct. Thus, N1 is a valid optimal choice.</reason>\n<answer>N1</answer>", "episode_score": -0.6166666666666667, "llm_raw_text": "<reason>Starting at N8, the legal moves are to N7, N1, or N2. We analyze each option to determine which leads to a winning position (i.e., forces the opponent into a losing position). \n\n- Move to N1: N1 → N3 → terminal. Opponent loses immediately. This is a winning move.\n- Move to N2: N2 → N1 → N3 → terminal. Opponent loses immediately. This is also a winning move.\n- Move to N7: N7 → N5 (terminal) or N9. \n  - N5 leads to terminal (opponent loses). \n  - N9 → N6 or N4. \n    - N6 → terminal. \n    - N4 → N6 or N0, both terminal. So all paths from N9 lead to terminal. Thus, N7 leads to opponent's loss.\n\nAll moves from N8 lead to the opponent having no legal move eventually. Since all options win, any choice is optimal. However, N1 and N2 both lead directly to N3. N7 offers more complexity but still wins. Choosing N1 is simple and direct. Thus, N1 is a valid optimal choice.</reason>\n<answer>N1</answer>"}, {"prompt": "system\nYou are playing Directed Acyclic Graph Vertex Geography.user\nThe players alternate moving a token along one directed edge. A player with no legal move loses. Choose one legal destination that maximizes your final game outcome. Keep your thinking process concise.\n\nOutput exactly:\n<reason>your analysis</reason>\n<answer>NODE</answer>\n\nDo not output anything else. A response that does not follow this format results in immediate loss.\n\nCurrent node: N1\n\nDirected graph:\nN6 -> terminal\nN0 -> terminal\nN2 -> N1\nN1 -> N3\nN9 -> N6, N4\nN4 -> N6, N0\nN3 -> terminal\nN8 -> N7, N1, N2\nN7 -> N5, N9\nN5 -> terminal\n\nLegal moves: N3assistant\n", "response": "<reason>Starting at N1, the only legal move is to N3, which leads to terminal (win for the player who moves there). Thus, moving to N3 results in immediate win. No other move from N1 is available. Therefore, the optimal choice is to move to N3.</reason>\n<answer>N3</answer>", "episode_score": 0.05, "llm_raw_text": "<reason>Starting at N1, the only legal move is to N3, which leads to terminal (win for the player who moves there). Thus, moving to N3 results in immediate win. No other move from N1 is available. Therefore, the optimal choice is to move to N3.</reason>\n<answer>N3</answer>"}, {"prompt": "system\nYou are playing Directed Acyclic Graph Vertex Geography.us