 Moving to N5: From N5 → N8 or N1.  \n  - N8 → N7 → terminal (opponent wins).  \n  - N1 → N0 or N6; N0 leads to opponent win, N6 leads to opponent win. So, from N5, opponent wins.  \n- Moving to N1: From N1 → N0 or N6; both lead to opponent win.  \n\nAll options lead to the opponent winning. Thus, no matter which move is chosen, the opponent wins. However, since the goal is to maximize final game outcome and all options result in loss, the best choice is the one that delays the loss longest or offers no advantage. N0 leads to N9 or N6; N9 leads to N3 or N2 (terminal), so it's a direct loss. N6 is terminal. Thus, N0 is the least detrimental. But all paths end in opponent win. Therefore, any move is equivalent. Chose N0 as it is a direct extension. </reason>  \n<answer>N0</answer>"}, {"prompt": "system\nYou are playing Directed Acyclic Graph Vertex Geography.user\nThe players alternate moving a token along one directed edge. A player with no legal move loses. Choose one legal destination that maximizes your final game outcome. Keep your thinking process concise.\n\nOutput exactly:\n<reason>your analysis</reason>\n<answer>NODE</answer>\n\nDo not output anything else. A response that does not follow this format results in immediate loss.\n\nCurrent node: N0\n\nDirected graph:\nN1 -> N0\nN2 -> terminal\nN6 -> terminal\nN8 -> N7\nN0 -> N9, N6\nN3 -> terminal\nN7 -> terminal\nN4 -> N0, N5, N1\nN9 -> N3, N2\nN5 -> N8, N1\n\nLegal moves: N9, N6assistant\n", "response": "<reason>Starting at N0, the legal moves are to N9 or N6. N6 leads directly to terminal (win for the player who moves there, as the opponent has no move). Thus, moving to N6 wins immediately. Moving to N9 leads to N3 or N2, both of which are terminal, so the opponent wins. Therefore, the optimal move is to N6.</reason>\n<answer>N6</answer>", "episode_score": 1.05, "llm_raw_text": "<reason>Starting at N0, the legal moves are to N9 or N6. N6 leads directly to terminal (win for the player who moves there, as the 