4, immediate move to N9 ends game, opponent has no move → win.  \n\nHence, moving to N4 is winning. Choosing N4 maximizes the outcome.</reason>  \n<answer>N4</answer>"}, {"prompt": "system\nYou are playing Directed Acyclic Graph Vertex Geography.user\nThe players alternate moving a token along one directed edge. A player with no legal move loses. Choose one legal destination that maximizes your final game outcome. Keep your thinking process concise.\n\nOutput exactly:\n<reason>your analysis</reason>\n<answer>NODE</answer>\n\nDo not output anything else. A response that does not follow this format results in immediate loss.\n\nCurrent node: N4\n\nDirected graph:\nN0 -> N2\nN6 -> N0, N8, N4\nN5 -> terminal\nN9 -> terminal\nN4 -> N9\nN7 -> terminal\nN2 -> N5, N7, N1\nN8 -> N2, N0\nN3 -> terminal\nN1 -> N3\n\nLegal moves: N9assistant\n", "response": "<reason>Starting at N4, the legal moves are to N9. N9 is a terminal node, so moving to N9 ends the game immediately. The player who moves to N9 wins because the opponent has no legal move. Thus, moving to N9 is optimal and guarantees a win. No other move from N4 is available. Therefore, the best choice is N9.</reason>\n<answer>N9</answer>", "episode_score": 0.05, "llm_raw_text": "<reason>Starting at N4, the legal moves are to N9. N9 is a terminal node, so moving to N9 ends the game immediately. The player who moves to N9 wins because the opponent has no legal move. Thus, moving to N9 is optimal and guarantees a win. No other move from N4 is available. Therefore, the best choice is N9.</reason>\n<answer>N9</answer>"}, {"prompt": "system\nYou are playing Directed Acyclic Graph Vertex Geography.user\nThe players alternate moving a token along one directed edge. A player with no legal move loses. Choose one legal destination that maximizes your final game outcome. Keep your thinking process concise.\n\nOutput exactly:\n<reason>your analysis</reason>\n<answer>NODE</answer>\n\nDo not output anything else. A response that does not