r N4:\n    - N4 → N5 (terminal): So N10 → N4 → N5: opponent wins.\n    - N10 → N6: opponent wins.\n  - N13 → N8 (terminal) or N12:\n    - N13 → N8: opponent wins.\n    - N12 → N3 (then N11 terminal), N9 (terminal), N4 (→ N5 terminal): all lead to opponent winning.\n  So N7 leads to opponent winning.\n- N1 → N0 (terminal) or N5 (terminal): both terminal. So move to N1 leads to opponent winning.\n\nThus, only N3 leads to an immediate win. Choosing N3 wins the game.</reason>\n<answer>N3</answer>", "episode_score": -0.6166666666666667, "llm_raw_text": "<reason>Starting at N2, the legal moves are to N3, N7, or N1. We analyze each:\n\n- N3 → N11 → terminal: Player who moves to N11 wins immediately (opponent has no move). So current player wins.\n- N7 → N10 or N13:\n  - N10 → N6 (terminal) or N4:\n    - N4 → N5 (terminal): So N10 → N4 → N5: opponent wins.\n    - N10 → N6: opponent wins.\n  - N13 → N8 (terminal) or N12:\n    - N13 → N8: opponent wins.\n    - N12 → N3 (then N11 terminal), N9 (terminal), N4 (→ N5 terminal): all lead to opponent winning.\n  So N7 leads to opponent winning.\n- N1 → N0 (terminal) or N5 (terminal): both terminal. So move to N1 leads to opponent winning.\n\nThus, only N3 leads to an immediate win. Choosing N3 wins the game.</reason>\n<answer>N3</answer>"}, {"prompt": "system\nYou are playing Directed Acyclic Graph Vertex Geography.user\nThe players alternate moving a token along one directed edge. A player with no legal move loses. Choose one legal destination that maximizes your final game outcome. Keep your thinking process concise.\n\nOutput exactly:\n<reason>your analysis</reason>\n<answer>NODE</answer>\n\nDo not output anything else. A response that does not follow this format results in immediate loss.\n\nCurrent node: N3\n\nDirected graph:\nN6 -> terminal\nN3 -> N11\nN13 -> N8, N12\nN10 -> N6, N4\nN8 -> terminal\nN4 -> N5\nN9 -> terminal\nN11 -> terminal\nN7 -> N10, N13\nN5 -> terminal\nN1 -> N0, N5\nN2 -> N3, N7, N1\nN12 -> N3, N9, N4\nN0 