answer>"}, {"prompt": "system\nYou are playing Directed Acyclic Graph Vertex Geography.user\nThe players alternate moving a token along one directed edge. A player with no legal move loses. Choose one legal destination that maximizes your final game outcome. Keep your thinking process concise.\n\nOutput exactly:\n<reason>your analysis</reason>\n<answer>NODE</answer>\n\nDo not output anything else. A response that does not follow this format results in immediate loss.\n\nCurrent node: N1\n\nDirected graph:\nN5 -> terminal\nN9 -> N5, N7, N8\nN4 -> N9\nN2 -> N1, N4, N6\nN0 -> terminal\nN6 -> N9, N4\nN1 -> N0\nN8 -> terminal\nN7 -> N3\nN3 -> terminal\n\nLegal moves: N0assistant\n", "response": "<reason>Starting at N1, the only legal move is to N0, which is terminal. The player who moves to N0 wins immediately, as the opponent has no legal move. Thus, moving to N0 ends the game immediately and wins. No other move from N1 is available. Therefore, the optimal move is to N0.</reason>\n<answer>N0</answer>", "episode_score": 0.05, "llm_raw_text": "<reason>Starting at N1, the only legal move is to N0, which is terminal. The player who moves to N0 wins immediately, as the opponent has no legal move. Thus, moving to N0 ends the game immediately and wins. No other move from N1 is available. Therefore, the optimal move is to N0.</reason>\n<answer>N0</answer>"}, {"prompt": "system\nYou are playing Directed Acyclic Graph Vertex Geography.user\nThe players alternate moving a token along one directed edge. A player with no legal move loses. Choose one legal destination that maximizes your final game outcome. Keep your thinking process concise.\n\nOutput exactly:\n<reason>your analysis</reason>\n<answer>NODE</answer>\n\nDo not output anything else. A response that does not follow this format results in immediate loss.\n\nCurrent node: N1\n\nDirected graph:\nN9 -> terminal\nN7 -> N2\nN0 -> terminal\nN3 -> N8, N9\nN2 -> terminal\nN6 -> N0, N5\nN8 -> terminal\nN1 -> N6, N7, N4\nN4 -> N6\n