[2026-08-13 17:00:05] [agentic_pipeline.py (516)] [INFO] [DRIVER 0 / 1][PID 1538566] [{"prompt": "system\nYou are playing Directed Acyclic Graph Vertex Geography.user\nThe players alternate moving a token along one directed edge. A player with no legal move loses. Choose one legal destination that maximizes your final game outcome. Keep your thinking process concise.\n\nOutput exactly:\n<reason>your analysis</reason>\n<answer>NODE</answer>\n\nDo not output anything else. A response that does not follow this format results in immediate loss.\n\nCurrent node: N9\n\nDirected graph:\nN8 -> N7, N1\nN7 -> N4, N0\nN2 -> terminal\nN4 -> terminal\nN3 -> N2\nN1 -> terminal\nN0 -> terminal\nN5 -> N8, N6\nN6 -> N4, N8\nN9 -> N5, N3\n\nLegal moves: N5, N3assistant\n", "response": "<reason>Starting at N9, the player can move to N5 or N3. We analyze each option:  \n- Moving to N5: From N5, the opponent can move to N8 or N6.  \n  - If to N8: N8 → N7 or N1. N1 and N7 lead to terminal (win for opponent). N7 → N4 or N0 (both terminal). So opponent wins.  \n  - If to N6: N6 → N4 or N8. Both N4 and N8 lead to terminal or N7 → terminal. Opponent wins.  \n  Thus, from N5, opponent wins.  \n- Moving to N3: N3 → N2 (terminal), so current player wins immediately.  \n\nThus, moving to N3 leads to an immediate win. Choosing N3 is optimal.</reason>  \n<answer>N3</answer>", "episode_score": -0.95, "llm_raw_text": "<reason>Starting at N9, the player can move to N5 or N3. We analyze each option:  \n- Moving to N5: From N5, the opponent can move to N8 or N6.  \n  - If to N8: N8 → N7 or N1. N1 and N7 lead to terminal (win for opponent). N7 → N4 or N0 (both terminal). So opponent wins.  \n  - If to N6: N6 → N4 or N8. Both N4 and N8 lead to terminal or N7 → terminal. Opponent wins.  \n  Thus, from N5, opponent wins.  \n- Moving to N3: N3 → N2 (terminal), so current player wins immediately.  \n\nThus, moving to N3 leads to an immediate win. Choosing N3 is optimal.</reason>  \n<answer>N3</answer>"}, {"prompt": "system\nYou are playing Directed Acyclic Graph Vertex Geography.user\nThe players alternate moving a token along one directed edge. A player with no legal move loses. Choose one legal destination that maximizes your final game outcome. Keep your thinking process concise.\n\nOutput exactly:\n<reason>your analysis</reason>\n<answer>NODE</answer>\n\nDo not output anything else. A response that does not follow this format results in immediate loss.\n\nCurrent node: N3\n\nDirected graph:\nN8 -> N7, N1\nN7 -> N4, N0\nN2 -> terminal\nN4 -> terminal\nN3 -> N2\nN1 -> terminal\nN0 -> terminal\nN5 -> N8, N6\nN6 -> N4, N8\nN9 -> N5, N3\n\nLegal moves: N2assistant\n", "response": "<reason>Starting at N3, the only legal move is to N2, which is a terminal node. Moving to N2 ends the game immediately, and the player who moved to N2 wins (since the opponent has no legal move). Thus, choosing N2 is optimal and guarantees a win.</reason>\n<answer>N2</answer>", "episode_score": 0.05, "llm_raw_text": "<reason>Starting at N3, the only legal move is to N2, which is a terminal node. Moving to N2 ends the game immediately, and the player who moved to N2 wins (since the opponent has no legal move). Thus, choosing N2 is optimal and guarantees a win.</reason>\n<answer>N2</answer>"}, {"prompt": "system\nYou are playing Directed Acyclic Graph Vertex Geography.user\nThe players alternate moving a token along one directed edge. A player with no legal move loses. Choose one legal destination that maximizes your final game outcome. Keep your thinking process concise.\n\nOutput exactly:\n<reason>your analysis</reason>\n<answer>NODE</answer>\n\nDo not output anything else. A response that does not follow this format results in immediate loss.\n\nCurrent node: N9\n\nDirected graph:\nN9 -> N1, N8, N6\nN8 -> N1\nN5 -> terminal\nN3 -> N2, N5\nN2 -> N7\nN1 -> N3, N0\nN0 -> terminal\nN7 -> terminal\nN4 -> terminal\nN6 -> N7, N4\n\nLegal moves: N1, N8, N6assistant\n", "response": "<reason>From N9, the legal moves are to N1, N8, or N6. We analyze each destination to determine which leads to a winning position (i.e., forces the opponent into a losing position).  \n- N1: N1 → N3 or N0. N0 leads to terminal (opponent wins), so N1 → N3. N3 → N2 or N5. N2 → N7 (terminal), N5 → terminal. Both lead to terminal. So from N1, the player can move to N3, then opponent can move to N7 or N5, both terminal. Thus, N1 leads to opponent winning.  \n- N8: N8 → N1. Then same as above, N1 → N3 or N0, both lead to terminal. So N8 leads to opponent winning.  \n- N6: N6 → N7 or N4. Both N7 and N4 are terminal. So the player can move directly to terminal. Thus, N6 ends the game immediately, opponent has no move. So N6 is a winning move.  \nThus, choosing N6 leads to an immediate win. Final move: N6.</reason>  \n<answer>N6</answer>", "episode_score": -0.6166666666666667, "llm_raw_text": "<reason>From N9, the legal moves are to N1, N8, or N6. We analyze each destination to determine which leads to a winning position (i.e., forces the opponent into a losing position).  \n- N1: N1 → N3 or N0. N0 leads to terminal (opponent wins), so N1 → N3. N3 → N2 or N5. N2 → N7 (terminal), N5 → terminal. Both lead to terminal. So from N1, the player can move to N3, then opponent can move to N7 or N5, both terminal. Thus, N1 leads to opponent winning.  \n- N8: N8 → N1. Then same as above, N1 → N3 or N0, both lead to terminal. So N8 leads to opponent winning.  \n- N6: N6 → N7 or N4. Both N7 and N4 are terminal. So the player can move directly to terminal. Thus, N6 ends the game immediately, opponent has no move. So N6 is a winning move.  \nThus, choosing N6 leads to an immediate win. Final move: N6.</reason>  \n<answer>N6</answer>"}, {"prompt": "system\nYou are playing Directed Acyclic Graph Vertex Geography.user\nThe players alternate moving a token along one directed edge. A player with no legal move loses. Choose one legal destination that maximizes your final game outcome. Keep your thinking process c