 options, but both paths lead to terminal. N5 also leads directly. Both are equivalent. Choosing N2 is safe and leads to a win. Thus, N2 is a valid optimal choice.</reason>\n<answer>N2</answer>"}, {"prompt": "system\nYou are playing Directed Acyclic Graph Vertex Geography.user\nThe players alternate moving a token along one directed edge. A player with no legal move loses. Choose one legal destination that maximizes your final game outcome. Keep your thinking process concise.\n\nOutput exactly:\n<reason>your analysis</reason>\n<answer>NODE</answer>\n\nDo not output anything else. A response that does not follow this format results in immediate loss.\n\nCurrent node: N2\n\nDirected graph:\nN3 -> terminal\nN0 -> terminal\nN1 -> N3\nN6 -> N2, N5\nN4 -> N5, N8\nN7 -> terminal\nN5 -> N1, N8\nN2 -> N9, N4\nN8 -> N7, N0\nN9 -> terminal\n\nLegal moves: N9, N4assistant\n", "response": "<reason>Starting at N2, the legal moves are to N9 or N4. N9 leads directly to terminal (win for the player who moves there, as the opponent has no move). Thus, moving to N9 wins immediately. Moving to N4 leads to N5 or N8. N5 leads to N1 or N8; N1 leads to N3 (terminal), and N8 leads to N7 or N0 (both terminal). All paths from N4 eventually lead to terminal. Therefore, choosing N9 is optimal and guarantees an immediate win.</reason>\n<answer>N9</answer>", "episode_score": 1.05, "llm_raw_text": "<reason>Starting at N2, the legal moves are to N9 or N4. N9 leads directly to terminal (win for the player who moves there, as the opponent has no move). Thus, moving to N9 wins immediately. Moving to N4 leads to N5 or N8. N5 leads to N1 or N8; N1 leads to N3 (terminal), and N8 leads to N7 or N0 (both terminal). All paths from N4 eventually lead to terminal. Therefore, choosing N9 is optimal and guarantees an immediate win.</reason>\n<answer>N9</answer>"}, {"prompt": "system\nYou are playing Directed Acyclic Graph Vertex Geography.user\nThe players alternate moving a token along one directed edge. A pla