[2026-08-13 17:04:32] [agentic_pipeline.py (516)] [INFO] [DRIVER 0 / 1][PID 1538566] [{"prompt": "system\nYou are playing Directed Acyclic Graph Vertex Geography.user\nThe players alternate moving a token along one directed edge. A player with no legal move loses. Choose one legal destination that maximizes your final game outcome. Keep your thinking process concise.\n\nOutput exactly:\n<reason>your analysis</reason>\n<answer>NODE</answer>\n\nDo not output anything else. A response that does not follow this format results in immediate loss.\n\nCurrent node: N8\n\nDirected graph:\nN7 -> terminal\nN5 -> N9, N2\nN2 -> terminal\nN1 -> terminal\nN6 -> N1, N3\nN3 -> N7\nN4 -> terminal\nN9 -> N4, N2\nN0 -> N6, N5\nN8 -> N0, N9\n\nLegal moves: N0, N9assistant\n", "response": "<reason>Starting at N8, the player can move to N0 or N9. We analyze each option:  \n- Moving to N0: From N0, moves are to N6 or N5.  \n  - N6 → N1 (terminal) or N3 → N7 (terminal) → both lead to terminal.  \n  - N5 → N9 or N2. N2 leads to terminal. N9 → N4 (terminal) or N2 (terminal). So all paths from N0 lead to terminal.  \n  - Thus, from N0, the opponent wins immediately.  \n- Moving to N9: From N9 → N4 (terminal) or N2 (terminal). Both are terminal. So opponent has no move. Current player wins.  \nHence, moving to N9 leads to an immediate win. Moving to N0 leads to loss. Therefore, choose N9.</reason>  \n<answer>N9</answer>", "episode_score": -0.95, "llm_raw_text": "<reason>Starting at N8, the player can move to N0 or N9. We analyze each option:  \n- Moving to N0: From N0, moves are to N6 or N5.  \n  - N6 → N1 (terminal) or N3 → N7 (terminal) → both lead to terminal.  \n  - N5 → N9 or N2. N2 leads to terminal. N9 → N4 (terminal) or N2 (terminal). So all paths from N0 lead to terminal.  \n  - Thus, from N0, the opponent wins immediately.  \n- Moving to N9: From N9 → N4 (terminal) or N2 (terminal). Both are terminal. So opponent has no move. Current player wins.  \nHence, moving to N9 leads to an immediate win. Moving to N0 leads to loss. Therefore, choose N9.</reason>  \n<answer>N9</answer>"}, {"prompt": "system\nYou are playing Directed Acyclic Graph Vertex Geography.user\nThe players alternate moving a token along one directed edge. A player with no legal move loses. Choose one legal destination that maximizes your final game outcome. Keep your thinking process concise.\n\nOutput exactly:\n<reason>your analysis</reason>\n<answer>NODE</answer>\n\nDo not output anything else. A response that does not follow this format results in immediate loss.\n\nCurrent node: N9\n\nDirected graph:\nN7 -> terminal\nN5 -> N9, N2\nN2 -> terminal\nN1 -> terminal\nN6 -> N1, N3\nN3 -> N7\nN4 -> terminal\nN9 -> N4, N2\nN0 -> N6, N5\nN8 -> N0, N9\n\nLegal moves: N4, N2assistant\n", "response": "<reason>Starting at N9, the legal moves are to N4 or N2. N4 leads to terminal (win for the player who moves there, as the opponent has no move). N2 leads to terminal as well. Both moves end the game immediately. Thus, either move wins. Since both are terminal moves, either is optimal. Choosing N4 or N2 is equivalent. However, N9 -> N2 also accesses N2 -> terminal, so both are winning. But N9 -> N4 leads to terminal directly. Both are equal. We choose one. N4 is a valid and terminal move. Therefore, the optimal choice is N4.</reason>\n<answer>N4</answer>", "episode_score": 0.05, "llm_raw_text": "<reason>Starting at N9, the legal moves are to N4 or N2. N4 leads to terminal (win for the player who moves there, as the opponent has no move). N2 leads to terminal as well. Both moves end the game immediately. Thus, either move wins. Since both are terminal moves, either is optimal. Choosing N4 or N2 is equivalent. However, N9 -> N2 also accesses N2 -> terminal, so both are winning. But N9 -> N4 leads to terminal directly. Both are equal. We choose one. N4 is a valid and terminal move. Therefore, the optimal choice is N4.</reason>\n<answer>N4</answer>"}, {"prompt": "system\nYou are playing Directed Acyclic Graph Vertex Geography.user\nThe players alternate moving a token along one directed edge. A player with no legal move loses. Choose one legal destination that maximizes your final game outcome. Keep your thinking process concise.\n\nOutput exactly:\n<reason>your analysis</reason>\n<answer>NODE</answer>\n\nDo not output anything else. A response that does not follow this format results in immediate loss.\n\nCurrent node: N1\n\nDirected graph:\nN6 -> terminal\nN2 -> terminal\nN3 -> N7, N0, N8\nN4 -> N6\nN7 -> terminal\nN1 -> N4, N5, N9\nN8 -> N2\nN0 -> terminal\nN5 -> N3\nN9 -> N4, N5\n\nLegal moves: N4, N5, N9assistant\n", "response": "<reason>Starting at N1, the legal moves are to N4, N5, or N9. We analyze each option to determine which leads to a winning position (i.e., forces the opponent into a terminal or losing position).  \n- N4 → N6 (terminal): Immediate win for the next player, so current player wins.  \n- N5 → N3 → N7, N0, N8.  \n  - N7 → terminal (opponent wins)  \n  - N0 → terminal (opponent wins)  \n  - N8 → N2 → terminal (opponent wins)  \n  All paths from N5 lead to terminal, so the next player loses. Thus, N5 leads to opponent winning.  \n- N9 → N4 or N5. Both N4 and N5 lead to terminal or opponent winning positions. So N9 leads to opponent winning.  \nThus, choosing N4 leads to immediate terminal (win). Other moves lead to opponent winning. Maximize outcome by choosing N4.</reason>\n<answer>N4</answer>", "episode_score": -0.6166666666666667, "llm_raw_text": "<reason>Starting at N1, the legal moves are to N4, N5, or N9. We analyze each option to determine which leads to a winning position (i.e., forces the opponent into a terminal or losing position).  \n- N4 → N6 (terminal): Immediate win for the next player, so current player wins.  \n- N5 → N3 → N7, N0, N8.  \n  - N7 → terminal (opponent wins)  \n  - N0 → terminal (opponent wins)  \n  - N8 → N2 → terminal (opponent wins)  \n  All paths from N5 lead to terminal, so the next player loses. Thus, N5 leads to opponent winning.  \n- N9 → N4 or N5. Both N4 and N5 lead to terminal or opponent winning positions. So N9 leads to opponent winning.  \nThus, choosing N4 leads to immediate terminal (win). Other moves lead to opponent winning. Maximize outcome by choosing N4.</reason>\n<answer>N4</answer>"}, {"prompt": "system\nYou are playing Directed Acyclic Graph Vertex Geography.user\nThe players alternate moving a token along one directed edge. A player with no legal move loses. Choose one legal destination that maximizes your final game outcome. Keep your thinking process concise.\n\nOutput exactly:\n<reason>your analysis</reason>\n<answer>NODE</answer>\n\nDo not output anything else. A response that does not follow this format results in immediate loss.\n\nCurrent node: N4\n\nDirected graph:\nN6 -> terminal\nN2 -> terminal\nN3 -> N7, N0, N8\nN4 -> N6\nN7 -> terminal\nN1 -> N4, N5, N9\nN8 -> N2\nN0 -> terminal\nN5 -> N3\nN9 -> N4, N5\n\nLegal moves: N6assistant\n", "response": "<reason>Starting at N4, the only legal move is to N6, which leads to terminal. Thus, the first player (me) moves to N6 and wins immediately. No other move is available, so choosing N6 is the only option. Since the game ends immediately after this move, and the opponent has no legal move, I win. Therefore, the optimal choice is N6.</reason>\n<answer>N6</answer>", "episode_score": 0.05, "llm_raw_text": "<reason>Starting at N4, the only legal move is to N6, which leads to terminal. Thus, the first player (me) moves to N6 and wins immediately. No other move is available, so choosing N6 is the only option. Since the game ends immediately after this move, and the opponent has no legal move, I win. Therefore, the optimal choice is N6.</reason>\n<answer>N6</answer>"}, {"prompt": "system\nYou are playing Directed Acyclic Graph Vertex Geography.user\nThe players alternate moving a token along one directed edge. A player with no legal move loses. Choose one legal destination that maximizes your final game outcome. Keep your thinking process concise.\n\nOutput exactly:\n<reason>your analysis</reason>\n<answer>NODE</answer>\n\nDo not output anything else. A response that does not follow this format results in immediate loss.\n\nCurrent node: N1\n\nDirected graph:\nN4 -> N5\nN5 -> terminal\nN2 -> terminal\nN6 -> N7, N4\nN0 -> N3\nN7 -> terminal\nN3 -> N2, N8, N6\nN1 -> N0, N8, N3\nN9 -> terminal\nN8 -> N9\n\nLegal moves: N0, N8, N3assistant\n", "response": "<reason>Starting at N1, the player can move to N0, N8, or N3. We analyze each option to determine which leads to a winning position (i.e., forces the opponent into a losing position).  \n- N0 → N3: N3 leads to N2 (terminal, opponent wins), N8 (to N9 terminal), or N6. N6 → N7 (terminal) or N4 → N5 → terminal. So from N3, all paths lead to terminal. So N0 → N3 is losing (all moves lead to terminal).  \n- N8 → N9 (terminal) immediately: opponent has no move, so current player wins. Thus N8 is a winning move.  \n- N3 → N2, N8, N6: N2, N8, N6 all lead to terminal or to N6 → N4 → N5 → terminal. So all are terminal. Thus N3 leads to opponent winning.  \nOnly N8 leads to immediate terminal. Thus, moving to N8 wins. So the optimal move is to N8.</reason>  \n<answer>N8</answer>", "episode_score": -0.6166666666666667, "llm_raw_text": "<reason>Starting at N1, the player can move to N0, N8, or N3. We analyze each option to determine which leads to a winning position (i.e., forces the opponent into a losing position).  \n- N0 → N3: N3 leads to N2 (terminal, opponent wins), N8 (to N9 terminal), or N6. N6 → N7 (terminal) or N4 → N5 → terminal. So from N3, all paths lead to terminal. So N0 → N3 is losing (all moves lead to terminal).  \n- N8 → N9 (terminal) immediately: opponent has no move, so current player wins. Thus N8 is a winning move.  \n- N3 → N2, N8, N6: N2, N8, N6 all lead to terminal or to N6 → N4 → N5 → terminal. So all are terminal. Thus N3 leads to opponent winning.  \nOnly N8 leads to immediate terminal. Thus, moving to N8 wins. So the optimal move is to N8.</reason>  \n<answer>N8</answer>"}, {"prompt": "system\nYou are playing Directed Acyclic Graph Vertex Geography.user\nThe players alternate moving a token along one directed edge. A player with no legal move loses. Choose one legal destination that maximizes your final game outcome. Keep your thinking process concise.\n\nOutput exactly:\n<reason>your analysis</reason>\n<answer>NODE</answer>\n\nDo not output anything else. A response that does not follow this format results in immediate loss.\n\nCurrent node: N8\n\nDirected graph:\nN4 -> N5\nN5 -> terminal\nN2 -> terminal\nN6 -> N7, N4\nN0 -> N3\nN7 -> terminal\nN3 -> N2, N8, N6\nN1 -> N0, N8, N3\nN9 -> terminal\nN8 -> N9\n\nLegal moves: N9assistant\n", "response": "<reason>Starting at N8, the legal moves are to N9. N9 leads to terminal, so the player who moves to N9 wins immediately (the opponent has no move). Thus, moving to N9 is a winning move. No other move from N8 is available. Therefore, the optimal move is to N9.</reason>\n<answer>N9</answer>", "episode_score": 0.05, "llm_raw_text": "<reason>Starting at N8, the legal moves are to N9. N9 leads to terminal, so the player who moves to N9 wins immediately (the opponent has no move). Thus, moving to N9 is a winning move. No other move from N8 is available. Therefore, the optimal move is to N9.</reason>\n<answer>N9</answer>"}, {"prompt": "system\nYou are playing Directed Acyclic Graph Vertex Geography.user\nThe players alternate moving a token along one directed edge. A player with no legal move loses. Choose one legal destination that maximizes your final game outcome. Keep your thinking process concise.\n\nOutput exactly:\n<reason>your analysis</reason>\n<answer>NODE</answer>\n\nDo not output anything else. A response that does not follow this format results in immediate loss.\n\nCurrent node: N11\n\nDirected graph:\nN4 -> N13\nN6 -> terminal\nN3 -> N4\nN10 -> N0, N3\nN13 -> terminal\nN11 -> N7, N3, N1\nN5 -> N6, N2\nN12 -> N13, N5\nN1 -> N0, N12, N8\nN9 -> terminal\nN7 -> N10, N9\nN0 -> terminal\nN2 -> terminal\nN8 -> terminal\n\nLegal moves: N7, N3, N1assistant\n", "response": "<reason>Starting at N11, player can move to N7, N3, or N1. We analyze each option:  \n- N3 → N4 → N13 → terminal (opponent wins immediately). So, N3 leads to opponent win.  \n- N7 → N10 or N9:  \n  - N10 → N0 (terminal) or N3 (leads to N4 → N13 → terminal). So N10 leads to opponent win.  \n  - N9 → terminal. So N7 → N9 wins immediately. Thus, N7 is winning.  \n- N1 → N0 (terminal), N12, or N8:  \n  - N0, N8 → terminal (opponent wins).  \n  - N12 → N13 (terminal) or N5 → N6 (terminal) or N2 (terminal). All terminal. So N1 leads to opponent win.  \nThus, only N7 leads to a win. Moving to N7 gives a winning position. The best choice is N7.</reason>  \n<answer>N7</answer>", "episode_score": -0.6166666666666667, "llm_raw_text": "<reason>Starting at N11, player can move to N7, N3, or N1. We analyze each option:  \n- N3 → N4 → N13 → terminal (opponent wins immediately). So, N3 leads to opponent win.  \n- N7 → N10 or N9:  \n  - N10 → N0 (terminal) or N3 (leads to N4 → N13 → terminal). So N10 leads to opponent win.  \n  - N9 → terminal. So N7 → N9 wins immediately. Thus, N7 is winning.  \n- N1 → N0 (terminal), N12, or N8:  \n  - N0, N8 → terminal (opponent wins).  \n  - N12 → N13 (terminal) or N5 → N6 (terminal) or N2 (terminal). All terminal. So N1 leads to opponent win.  \nThus, only N7 leads to a win. Moving to N7 gives a winning position. The best choice is N7.</reason>  \n<answer>N7</answer>"}, {"prompt": "system\nYou are playing Directed Acyclic Graph Vertex Geography.user\nThe players alternate moving a token along one directed edge. A player with no legal move loses. Choose one legal destination that maximizes your final game outcome. Keep your thinking process concise.\n\nOutput exactly:\n<reason>your analysis</reason>\n<answer>NODE</answer>\n\nDo not output anything else. A response that does not follow this format results in immediate loss.\n\nCurrent node: N7\n\nDirected graph:\nN4 -> N13\nN6 -> terminal\nN3 -> N4\nN10 -> N0, N3\nN13 -> terminal\nN11 -> N7, N3, N1\nN5 -> N6, N2\nN12 -> N13, N5\nN1 -> N0, N12, N8\nN9 -> terminal\nN7 -> N10, N9\nN0 -> terminal\nN2 -> terminal\nN8 -> terminal\n\nLegal moves: N10, N9assistant\n", "response": "<reason>Starting at N7, the legal moves are to N10 or N9. N9 leads directly to terminal (win for the player who moves there, as the opponent has no move). Thus, moving to N9 wins immediately. Moving to N10 leads to N0 or N3: N0 is terminal, so the opponent wins if they move there. N3 leads to N4, which leads to N13, terminal. So from N10, the opponent can force a win. Therefore, choosing N9 is optimal.</reason>\n<answer>N9</answer>", "episode_score": 1.05, "llm_raw_text": "<reason>Starting at N7, the legal moves are to N10 or N9. N9 leads directly to terminal (win for the player who moves there, as the opponent has no move). Thus, moving to N9 wins immediately. Moving to N10 leads to N0 or N3: N0 is terminal, so the opponent wins if they move there. N3 leads to N4, which leads to N13, terminal. So from N10, the opponent can force a win. Therefore, choosing N9 is optimal.</reason>\n<answer>N9</answer>"}, {"prompt": "system\nYou are playing Directed Acyclic Graph Vertex Geography.user\nThe players alternate moving a token along one directed edge. A player with no legal move loses. Choose one legal destination that maximizes your final game outcome. Keep your thinking process concise.\n\nOutput exactly:\n<reason>your analysis</reason>\n<answer>NODE</answer>\n\nDo not output anything else. A response that does not follow this format results in immediate loss.\n\nCurrent node: N0\n\nDirected graph:\nN1 -> N3\nN4 -> terminal\nN0 -> N2, N5, N6\nN9 -> terminal\nN2 -> N6\nN5 -> N1, N9\nN7 -> terminal\nN8 -> N7, N4\nN6 -> N9, N8\nN3 -> terminal\n\nLegal moves: N2, N5, N6assistant\n", "response": "<reason>Starting at N0, the player can move to N2, N5, or N6. We analyze each option to determine which leads to a winning position (i.e., forces the opponent into a losing position).  \n\n- N2 → N6 → N9 (terminal) or N8 → N7 (terminal) or N4 (terminal). From N6, opponent can move to N9 (terminal) or N8 → N7 (terminal). All are terminal. So N2 leads to immediate win for the opponent. Thus N2 is losing.  \n- N5 → N1 → N3 (terminal) or N9 (terminal). Both terminal. So N5 leads to immediate win for opponent. Thus N5 is losing.  \n- N6 → N9 (terminal) or N8 → N7 (terminal). Both terminal. So N6 leads to immediate win for opponent. Thus N6 is losing.  \n\nAll moves from N0 lead to terminal nodes immediately or to positions where opponent wins. Hence, all are losing. But since the player must choose a legal move, and all lead to opponent winning, the optimal choice is any; however, maximizing outcome means avoiding immediate loss. All options lead to opponent winning. Thus, any move is equivalent. Choose N6 as it is a safe, direct move to a terminal path. However, since all lead to opponent win, no move is winning. But per rule, choose one that maximizes outcome; all are equal. Pick N6.</reason>  \n<answer>N6</answer>", "episode_score": -0.6166666666666667, "llm_raw_text": "<reason>Starting at N0, the player can move to N2, N5, or N6. We analyze each option to determine which leads to a winning position (i.e., forces the opponent into a losing position).  \n\n- N2 → N6 → N9 (terminal) or N8 → N7 (terminal) or N4 (terminal). From N6, opponent can move to N9 (terminal) or N8 → N7 (terminal). All are terminal. So N2 leads to immediate win for the opponent. Thus N2 is losing.  \n- N5 → N1 → N3 (terminal) or N9 (terminal). Both terminal. So N5 leads to immediate win for opponent. Thus N5 is losing.  \n- N6 → N9 (terminal) or N8 → N7 (terminal). Both terminal. So N6 leads to immediate win for opponent. Thus N6 is losing.  \n\nAll moves from N0 lead to terminal nodes immediately or to positions where opponent wins. Hence, all are losing. But since the player must choose a legal move, and all lead to opponent winning, the optimal choice is any; however, maximizing outcome means avoiding immediate loss. All options lead to opponent winning. Thus, any move is equivalent. Choose N6 as it is a safe, direct move to a terminal path. However, since all lead to opponent win, no move is winning. But per rule, choose one that maximizes outcome; all are equal. Pick N6.</reason>  \n<answer>N6</answer>"}, {"prompt": "system\nYou are playing Directed Acyclic Graph Vertex Geography.user\nThe players alternate moving a token along one directed edge. A player with no legal move loses. Choose one legal destination that maximizes your final game outcome. Keep your thinking process concise.\n\nOutput exactly:\n<reason>your analysis</reason>\n<answer>NODE</answer>\n\nDo not output anything else. A response that does not follow this format results in immediate loss.\n\nCurrent node: N6\n\nDirected graph:\nN1 -> N3\nN4 -> terminal\nN0 -> N2, N5, N6\nN9 -> terminal\nN2 -> N6\nN5 -> N1, N9\nN7 -> terminal\nN8 -> N7, N4\nN6 -> N9, N8\nN3 -> terminal\n\nLegal moves: N9, N8assistant\n", "response": "<reason>Starting at N6, the legal moves are to N9 or N8. N9 leads directly to terminal (win for the player who moves there, as the opponent has no move). N8 leads to N7 or N4, both of which are terminal. Thus, moving to N9 wins immediately. Moving to N8 results in an immediate win for the opponent. Therefore, the optimal move is to N9.</reason>\n<answer>N9</answer>", "episode_score": 1.05, "llm_raw_text": "<reason>Starting at N6, the legal moves are to N9 or N8. N9 leads directly to terminal (win for the player who moves there, as the opponent has no move). N8 leads to N7 or N4, both of which are terminal. Thus, moving to N9 wins immediately. Moving to N8 results in an immediate win for the opponent. Therefore, the optimal move is to N9.</reason>\n<answer>N9</answer>"}]
