 to N4 is an immediate win. Thus, choosing N0 is optimal. The outcome is a win.</reason>\n<answer>N0</answer>", "episode_score": -0.6166666666666667, "llm_raw_text": "<reason>Starting at N7, the legal moves are to N3, N0, or N1. We analyze each option to find the one that maximizes the chance of winning (i.e., leads to a terminal node on the opponent's turn).  \n- N3 → N1 → N9 → N8 → N6 (terminal, opponent loses) or N5 (terminal). So N1 leads to N9, then N8, which eventually leads to terminal. So N3 → N1 → N9 → N8 → N6 (opponent loses).  \n- N0 → N4 (terminal) or N3. N4 is terminal, so if N0 → N4, current player wins immediately. But if N0 → N3, it leads to N1, then N9, then N8, then N6 or N5, terminal. So N0 → N4 is a win immediately.  \n- N1 → N9 → N8 → N6 or N5 (terminal). So N1 leads to terminal.  \nSo N0 to N4 is an immediate win. Thus, choosing N0 is optimal. The outcome is a win.</reason>\n<answer>N0</answer>"}, {"prompt": "system\nYou are playing Directed Acyclic Graph Vertex Geography.user\nThe players alternate moving a token along one directed edge. A player with no legal move loses. Choose one legal destination that maximizes your final game outcome. Keep your thinking process concise.\n\nOutput exactly:\n<reason>your analysis</reason>\n<answer>NODE</answer>\n\nDo not output anything else. A response that does not follow this format results in immediate loss.\n\nCurrent node: N0\n\nDirected graph:\nN7 -> N3, N0, N1\nN2 -> terminal\nN4 -> terminal\nN6 -> terminal\nN9 -> N8, N2\nN1 -> N9\nN3 -> N1\nN5 -> terminal\nN8 -> N6, N5\nN0 -> N4, N3\n\nLegal moves: N4, N3assistant\n", "response": "<reason>Starting at N0, the legal moves are to N4 or N3. N4 leads to terminal (win for the player who moves there, as the opponent has no move). N3 leads to N1, and from N1 leads to N9, then to N8, then to N6 or N5 (both terminal). Thus, moving to N3 leads to a chain that eventually ends in a terminal node, meaning the opponent wins. Therefore, choosing N4 immediately end