[2026-08-13 17:09:01] [agentic_pipeline.py (516)] [INFO] [DRIVER 0 / 1][PID 1538566] [{"prompt": "system\nYou are playing Directed Acyclic Graph Vertex Geography.user\nThe players alternate moving a token along one directed edge. A player with no legal move loses. Choose one legal destination that maximizes your final game outcome. Keep your thinking process concise.\n\nOutput exactly:\n<reason>your analysis</reason>\n<answer>NODE</answer>\n\nDo not output anything else. A response that does not follow this format results in immediate loss.\n\nCurrent node: N6\n\nDirected graph:\nN9 -> terminal\nN7 -> terminal\nN2 -> N8\nN0 -> N3, N5\nN3 -> N5\nN8 -> terminal\nN1 -> terminal\nN5 -> N1, N7, N4\nN4 -> N9\nN6 -> N0, N3, N2\n\nLegal moves: N0, N3, N2assistant\n", "response": "<reason>From N6, the legal moves are to N0, N3, or N2. We analyze each option by evaluating the outcomes recursively.  \n- N0 → N3, N5  \n  - N3 → N5  \n    - N5 → N1, N7, N4; N1 and N7 lead to terminal (loss for next player), N4 → N9 (terminal) → so N5 can lead to terminal. Thus, N3 → N5 → leads to opponent win.  \n  - N5 → N1, N7, N4 all lead to terminal. So N0 → N5 is winning for the opponent.  \n  - N0 leads to a winning move for the opponent.  \n- N3 → N5, same as above → N5 leads to terminal → opponent wins.  \n- N2 → N8 → terminal → current player wins immediately.  \n\nThus, moving to N2 leads to immediate terminal (opponent has no move), so it is a win. Other moves lead to opponent winning. Therefore, N2 is optimal.</reason>\n<answer>N2</answer>", "episode_score": -0.6166666666666667, "llm_raw_text": "<reason>From N6, the legal moves are to N0, N3, or N2. We analyze each option by evaluating the outcomes recursively.  \n- N0 → N3, N5  \n  - N3 → N5  \n    - N5 → N1, N7, N4; N1 and N7 lead to terminal (loss for next player), N4 → N9 (terminal) → so N5 can lead to terminal. Thus, N3 → N5 → leads to opponent win.  \n  - N5 → N1, N7, N4 all lead to terminal. So N0 → N5 is winning for the opponent.  \n  - N0 leads to a winning move for the opponent.  \n- N3 → N5, same as above → N5 leads to terminal → opponent wins.  \n- N2 → N8 → terminal → current player wins immediately.  \n\nThus, moving to N2 leads to immediate terminal (opponent has no move), so it is a win. Other moves lead to opponent winning. Therefore, N2 is optimal.</reason>\n<answer>N2</answer>"}, {"prompt": "system\nYou are playing Directed Acyclic Graph Vertex Geography.user\nThe players alternate moving a token along one directed edge. A player with no legal move loses. Choose one legal destination that maximizes your final game outcome. Keep your thinking process concise.\n\nOutput exactly:\n<reason>your analysis</reason>\n<answer>NODE</answer>\n\nDo not output anything else. A response that does not follow this format results in immediate loss.\n\nCurrent node: N2\n\nDirected graph:\nN9 -> terminal\nN7 -> terminal\nN2 -> N8\nN0 -> N3, N5\nN3 -> N5\nN8 -> terminal\nN1 -> terminal\nN5 -> N1, N7, N4\nN4 -> N9\nN6 -> N0, N3, N2\n\nLegal moves: N8assistant\n", "response": "<reason>Starting at N2, the only legal move is to N8. N8 leads to terminal, so the player who moves to N8 wins immediately (the opponent has no move). Thus, moving to N8 results in an immediate win. No other move from N2 is available. Therefore, the optimal move is to N8.</reason>\n<answer>N8</answer>", "episode_score": 0.05, "llm_raw_text": "<reason>Starting at N2, the only legal move is to N8. N8 leads to terminal, so the player who moves to N8 wins immediately (the opponent has no move). Thus, moving to N8 results in an immediate win. No other move from N2 is available. Therefore, the optimal move is to N8.</reason>\n<answer>N8</answer>"}, {"prompt": "system\nYou are playing Directed Acyclic Graph Vertex Geography.user\nThe players alternate moving a token along one directed edge. A player with no legal move loses. Choose one legal destination that maximizes your final game outcome. Keep your thinking process concise.\n\nOutput exactly:\n<reason>your analysis</reason>\n<answer>NODE</answer>\n\nDo not output anything else. A response that does not follow this format results in immediate loss.\n\nCurrent node: N7\n\nDirected graph:\nN4 -> terminal\nN6 -> N9\nN0 -> N3, N1, N6\nN7 -> N6, N5, N0\nN9 -> N2, N1\nN3 -> terminal\nN1 -> N4\nN2 -> terminal\nN8 -> terminal\nN5 -> N8\n\nLegal moves: N6, N5, N0assistant\n", "response": "<reason>From N7, the player can move to N6, N5, or N0. We analyze each option to determine which leads to a winning position (i.e., forces the opponent into a losing position).  \n\n- N6 → N9: N9 → N2 or N1. N2 leads to terminal (win for opponent). N1 → N4 → terminal. So from N9, opponent wins. Thus N6 leads to opponent winning.  \n- N5 → N8: N8 is terminal, so opponent has no move. Current player wins.  \n- N0 → N3 (terminal), N1 (→ N4 → terminal), or N6 (already analyzed). All paths from N0 lead to terminal. So opponent wins.  \n\nOnly N5 leads to an immediate terminal node (N8), meaning the opponent has no move and current player wins. Thus, moving to N5 is optimal.</reason>\n<answer>N5</answer>", "episode_score": -0.6166666666666667, "llm_raw_text": "<reason>From N7, the player can move to N6, N5, or N0. We analyze each option to determine which leads to a winning position (i.e., forces the opponent into a losing position).  \n\n- N6 → N9: N9 → N2 or N1. N2 leads to terminal (win for opponent). N1 → N4 → terminal. So from N9, opponent wins. Thus N6 leads to opponent winning.  \n- N5 → N8: N8 is terminal, so opponent has no move. Current player wins.  \n- N0 → N3 (terminal), N1 (→ N4 → terminal), or N6 (already analyzed). All paths from N0 lead to terminal. So opponent wins.  \n\nOnly N5 leads to an immediate terminal node (N8), meaning the opponent has no move and current player wins. Thus, moving to N5 is optimal.</reason>\n<answer>N5</answer>"}, {"prompt": "system\nYou are playing Directed Acyclic Graph Vertex Geography.user\nThe players alternate moving a token along one directed edge. A player with no legal move loses. Choose one legal destination that maximizes your final game outcome. Keep your thinking process concise.\n\nOutput exactly:\n<reason>your analysis</reason>\n<answer>NODE</answer>\n\nDo not output anything else. A response that does not follow this format results in immediate loss.\n\nCurrent node: N8\n\nDirected graph:\nN0 -> terminal\nN8 -> N5, N4, N1\nN9 -> N6, N3\nN1 -> N0\nN5 -> N9\nN7 -> N1, N6\nN3 -> terminal\nN4 -> N2, N7\nN6 -> terminal\nN2 -> terminal\n\nLegal moves: N5, N4, N1assistant\n", "response": "<reason>Starting at N8, the player can move to N5, N4, or N1. We analyze each option:  \n- N5 → N9 → N6 (N6 is terminal, so the next player loses). So, N5 leads to a win for the opponent.  \n- N4 → N2 (N2 is terminal, opponent loses) or N4 → N7 → N1 → N0 (N0 is terminal, opponent loses). Both paths end in terminal, so N4 is winning.  \n- N1 → N0 (terminal), opponent loses. So N1 is winning.  \n\nAll moves from N8 lead to a win for the current player. However, we must choose the move that maximizes outcome. Since all are winning, we pick one that leads to a terminal node immediately (e.g., N1 → N0). N1 is direct and safe. Thus, N1 is optimal.</reason>  \n<answer>N1</answer>", "episode_score": -0.6166666666666667, "llm_raw_text": "<reason>Starting at N8, the player can move to N5, N4, or N1. We analyze each option:  \n- N5 → N9 → N6 (N6 is terminal, so the next player loses). So, N5 leads to a win for the opponent.  \n- N4 → N2 (N2 is terminal, opponent loses) or N4 → N7 → N1 → N0 (N0 is terminal, opponent loses). Both paths end in terminal, so N4 is winning.  \n- N1 → N0 (terminal), opponent loses. So N1 is winning.  \n\nAll moves from N8 lead to a win for the current player. However, we must choose the move that maximizes outcome. Since all are winning, we pick one that leads to a terminal node immediately (e.g., N1 → N0). N1 is direct and safe. Thus, N1 is optimal.</reason>  \n<answer>N1</answer>"}, {"prompt": "system\nYou are playing Directed Acyclic Graph Vertex Geography.user\nThe players alternate moving a token along one directed edge. A player with no legal move loses. Choose one legal destination that maximizes your final game outcome. Keep your thinking process concise.\n\nOutput exactly:\n<reason>your analysis</reason>\n<answer>NODE</answer>\n\nDo not output anything else. A response that does not follow this format results in immediate loss.\n\nCurrent node: N5\n\nDirected graph:\nN4 -> terminal\nN6 -> N9\nN0 -> N3, N1, N6\nN7 -> N6, N5, N0\nN9 -> N2, N1\nN3 -> terminal\nN1 -> N4\nN2 -> terminal\nN8 -> terminal\nN5 -> N8\n\nLegal moves: N8assistant\n", "response": "<reason>Starting at N5, the legal moves are to N8 or N0. N8 leads directly to terminal (win for the player who moves there, as the opponent has no move). Thus, moving to N8 wins immediately. Moving to N0 leads to N3, N1, or N6. N3 and N6 lead to terminal, so those are winning moves for the opponent. N1 leads to N4, which leads to terminal. Thus, any move from N0 eventually leads to terminal for the opponent. Therefore, choosing N8 is optimal and guarantees an immediate win.</reason>\n<answer>N8</answer>", "episode_score": 0.05, "llm_raw_text": "<reason>Starting at N5, the legal moves are to N8 or N0. N8 leads directly to terminal (win for the player who moves there, as the opponent has no move). Thus, moving to N8 wins immediately. Moving to N0 leads to N3, N1, or N6. N3 and N6 lead to terminal, so those are winning moves for the opponent. N1 leads to N4, which leads to terminal. Thus, any move from N0 eventually leads to terminal for the opponent. Therefore, choosing N8 is optimal and guarantees an immediate win.</reason>\n<answer>N8</answer>"}, {"prompt": "system\nYou are playing Directed Acyclic Graph Vertex Geography.user\nThe players alternate moving a token along one directed edge. A player with no legal move loses. Choose one legal destination that maximizes your final game outcome. Keep your thinking process concise.\n\nOutput exactly:\n<reason>your analysis</reason>\n<answer>NODE</answer>\n\nDo not output anything else. A response that does not follow this format results in immediate loss.\n\nCurrent node: N1\n\nDirected graph:\nN0 -> terminal\nN8 -> N5, N4, N1\nN9 -> N6, N3\nN1 -> N0\nN5 -> N9\nN7 -> N1, N6\nN3 -> terminal\nN4 -> N2, N7\nN6 -> terminal\nN2 -> terminal\n\nLegal moves: N0assistant\n", "response": "<reason>Starting at N1, the legal move is to N0. N0 leads to terminal, so the player who moves to N0 wins immediately (the opponent has no move). Thus, moving to N0 is optimal and results in an immediate win. No other move from N1 is available. Therefore, the best choice is N0.</reason>\n<answer>N0</answer>", "episode_score": 0.05, "llm_raw_text": "<reason>Starting at N1, the legal move is to N0. N0 leads to terminal, so the player who moves to N0 wins immediately (the opponent has no move). Thus, moving to N0 is optimal and results in an immediate win. No other move from N1 is available. Therefore, the best choice is N0.</reason>\n<answer>N0</answer>"}, {"prompt": "system\nYou are playing Directed Acyclic Graph Vertex Geography.user\nThe players alternate moving a token along one directed edge. A player with no legal move loses. Choose one legal destination that maximizes your final game outcome. Keep your thinking process concise.\n\nOutput exactly:\n<reason>your analysis</reason>\n<answer>NODE</answer>\n\nDo not output anything else. A response that does not follow this format results in immediate loss.\n\nCurrent node: N8\n\nDirected graph:\nN2 -> terminal\nN11 -> N2, N9\nN13 -> terminal\nN4 -> N3, N11\nN0 -> N7, N5\nN12 -> N6, N1\nN10 -> N1, N12\nN3 -> terminal\nN1 -> terminal\nN6 -> terminal\nN9 -> terminal\nN7 -> N2, N13\nN5 -> N13, N10\nN8 -> N4, N0\n\nLegal moves: N4, N0assistant\n", "response": "<reason>Starting at N8, player can move to N4 or N0. We analyze each option:  \n- N4 → N3 (terminal) or N11.  \n  - N11 → N2 (terminal) or N9 (terminal) → wins for the opponent. So N11 leads to loss.  \n  - N3 → terminal: immediate win. So N4 → N3 is a winning move.  \n- N0 → N7 or N5.  \n  - N7 → N2 or N13 (both terminal) → opponent wins.  \n  - N5 → N13 (terminal) or N10.  \n    - N10 → N1 (terminal) or N12.  \n      - N12 → N6 (terminal) or N1 (terminal) → opponent wins.  \n    So all paths from N0 lead to opponent winning.  \nThus, moving to N4 (specifically to N3) wins immediately. Choose N4.</reason>  \n<answer>N4</answer>", "episode_score": -0.95, "llm_raw_text": "<reason>Starting at N8, player can move to N4 or N0. We analyze each option:  \n- N4 → N3 (terminal) or N11.  \n  - N11 → N2 (terminal) or N9 (terminal) → wins for the opponent. So N11 leads to loss.  \n  - N3 → terminal: immediate win. So N4 → N3 is a winning move.  \n- N0 → N7 or N5.  \n  - N7 → N2 or N13 (both terminal) → opponent wins.  \n  - N5 → N13 (terminal) or N10.  \n    - N10 → N1 (terminal) or N12.  \n      - N12 → N6 (terminal) or N1 (terminal) → opponent wins.  \n    So all paths from N0 lead to opponent winning.  \nThus, moving to N4 (specifically to N3) wins immediately. Choose N4.</reason>  \n<answer>N4</answer>"}, {"prompt": "system\nYou are playing Directed Acyclic Graph Vertex Geography.user\nThe players alternate moving a token along one directed edge. A player with no legal move loses. Choose one legal destination that maximizes your final game outcome. Keep your thinking process concise.\n\nOutput exactly:\n<reason>your analysis</reason>\n<answer>NODE</answer>\n\nDo not output anything else. A response that does not follow this format results in immediate loss.\n\nCurrent node: N4\n\nDirected graph:\nN2 -> terminal\nN11 -> N2, N9\nN13 -> terminal\nN4 -> N3, N11\nN0 -> N7, N5\nN12 -> N6, N1\nN10 -> N1, N12\nN3 -> terminal\nN1 -> terminal\nN6 -> terminal\nN9 -> terminal\nN7 -> N2, N13\nN5 -> N13, N10\nN8 -> N4, N0\n\nLegal moves: N3, N11assistant\n", "response": "<reason>From N4, the legal moves are