rminal), N5, N9 (all terminal or lead to N5). N5 → N3 → terminal. So all paths from N1 eventually lead to terminal. Thus, N0→N6 leads to opponent winning.  \n- N0 → N2: N2 → N6 or N5. N6 → N1 → leads to terminal options. N5 → N3 → terminal. All paths from N2 lead to terminal. Opponent wins.  \n\nOnly N0→N8 leads to an immediate terminal move for the opponent. Thus, N8 is the optimal choice.</reason>  \n<answer>N8</answer>"}, {"prompt": "system\nYou are playing Directed Acyclic Graph Vertex Geography.user\nThe players alternate moving a token along one directed edge. A player with no legal move loses. Choose one legal destination that maximizes your final game outcome. Keep your thinking process concise.\n\nOutput exactly:\n<reason>your analysis</reason>\n<answer>NODE</answer>\n\nDo not output anything else. A response that does not follow this format results in immediate loss.\n\nCurrent node: N8\n\nDirected graph:\nN4 -> terminal\nN6 -> N1\nN5 -> N3\nN0 -> N2, N8, N6\nN3 -> terminal\nN8 -> N4\nN7 -> terminal\nN2 -> N6, N5\nN9 -> terminal\nN1 -> N7, N5, N9\n\nLegal moves: N4assistant\n", "response": "<reason>Starting at N8, the only legal move is to N4. N4 leads to terminal, so the player who moves to N4 wins immediately (the opponent has no move). Thus, moving to N4 results in an immediate win. No other move from N8 is available. Therefore, the optimal move is to N4.</reason>\n<answer>N4</answer>", "episode_score": 0.05, "llm_raw_text": "<reason>Starting at N8, the only legal move is to N4. N4 leads to terminal, so the player who moves to N4 wins immediately (the opponent has no move). Thus, moving to N4 results in an immediate win. No other move from N8 is available. Therefore, the optimal move is to N4.</reason>\n<answer>N4</answer>"}, {"prompt": "system\nYou are playing Directed Acyclic Graph Vertex Geography.user\nThe players alternate moving a token along one directed edge. A player with no legal move loses. Choose one legal destination that maximizes your final game outcome. Keep your thinking process concise.\n\nOutput exactly:\n<reason>your analysis</reason>\n<answer>NODE</answer>\n\nDo not output anything else. A response that does not follow this format results in immediate loss.\n\nCurrent node: N9\n\nDirected graph:\nN3 -> N1, N7\nN6 -> N2\nN8 -> terminal\nN7 -> N5, N1\nN5 -> terminal\nN4 -> N0\nN1 -> terminal\nN9 -> N6, N4, N2\nN2 -> N3, N8\nN0 -> terminal\n\nLegal moves: N6, N4, N2assistant\n", "response": "<reason>Starting at N9, the player can move to N6, N4, or N2. We analyze each option to determine which leads to a winning position (i.e., forces the opponent into a losing position).  \n- N4 → N0 → terminal (win for the player who moves here; opponent has no move). So N4 is a winning move.  \n- N6 → N2 → N3 → N1 (terminal) or N2 → N8 (terminal). Both lead to terminal. So N6 leads to opponent winning immediately.  \n- N2 → N3 → N1 (terminal) or N2 → N8 (terminal). Both terminal. So N2 is a losing move.  \nThus, N4 leads to immediate terminal for the opponent. N6 and N2 lead to opponent winning. The best move is N4.</reason>  \n<answer>N4</answer>", "episode_score": -0.6166666666666667, "llm_raw_text": "<reason>Starting at N9, the player can move to N6, N4, or N2. We analyze each option to determine which leads to a winning position (i.e., forces the opponent into a losing position).  \n- N4 → N0 → terminal (win for the player who moves here; opponent has no move). So N4 is a winning move.  \n- N6 → N2 → N3 → N1 (terminal) or N2 → N8 (terminal). Both lead to terminal. So N6 leads to opponent winning immediately.  \n- N2 → N3 → N1 (terminal) or N2 → N8 (terminal). Both terminal. So N2 is a losing move.  \nThus, N4 leads to immediate terminal for the opponent. N6 and N2 lead to opponent winning. The best move is N4.</reason>  \n<answer>N4</answer>"}, {"prompt": "system\nYou are playing Directed Acyclic Graph Vertex Geography.user\nThe players alternate moving a token along one directed edge. A player with no leg