[2026-08-13 17:18:19] [agentic_pipeline.py (516)] [INFO] [DRIVER 0 / 1][PID 1538566] [{"prompt": "system\nYou are playing Directed Acyclic Graph Vertex Geography.user\nThe players alternate moving a token along one directed edge. A player with no legal move loses. Choose one legal destination that maximizes your final game outcome. Keep your thinking process concise.\n\nOutput exactly:\n<reason>your analysis</reason>\n<answer>NODE</answer>\n\nDo not output anything else. A response that does not follow this format results in immediate loss.\n\nCurrent node: N9\n\nDirected graph:\nN4 -> N6, N3\nN5 -> N3, N1, N0\nN3 -> N7\nN7 -> terminal\nN6 -> terminal\nN0 -> terminal\nN1 -> N2\nN9 -> N4, N8, N5\nN2 -> terminal\nN8 -> N5\n\nLegal moves: N4, N8, N5assistant\n", "response": "<reason>Starting at N9, the player can move to N4, N8, or N5. We analyze each option to determine which leads to a winning position (i.e., forces the opponent into a losing position).  \n- N4 → N6 or N3.  \n  - N6 → terminal (win for the player who moved to N6, so opponent loses).  \n  - N3 → N7 → terminal. So, N3 leads to opponent winning.  \n  → Prefer N4 → N6 (immediate win).  \n- N8 → N5  \n  - N5 → N3, N1, N0  \n    - N3 → N7 → terminal (opponent wins)  \n    - N1 → N2 → terminal (opponent wins)  \n    - N0 → terminal (opponent wins)  \n  → All moves from N5 lead to opponent winning. So N8 leads to loss.  \n- N5 → same as above, all lead to opponent winning.  \n\nThus, moving to N4 is best, as it allows immediate move to N6 (terminal), winning the game. The optimal choice is N4.</reason>  \n<answer>N4</answer>", "episode_score": -0.6166666666666667, "llm_raw_text": "<reason>Starting at N9, the player can move to N4, N8, or N5. We analyze each option to determine which leads to a winning position (i.e., forces the opponent into a losing position).  \n- N4 → N6 or N3.  \n  - N6 → terminal (win for the player who moved to N6, so opponent loses).  \n  - N3 → N7 → terminal. So, N3 leads to opponent winning.  \n  → Prefer N4 → N6 (immediate win).  \n- N8 → N5  \n  - N5 → N3, N1, N0  \n    - N3 → N7 → terminal (opponent wins)  \n    - N1 → N2 → terminal (opponent wins)  \n    - N0 → terminal (opponent wins)  \n  → All moves from N5 lead to opponent winning. So N8 leads to loss.  \n- N5 → same as above, all lead to opponent winning.  \n\nThus, moving to N4 is best, as it allows immediate move to N6 (terminal), winning the game. The optimal choice is N4.</reason>  \n<answer>N4</answer>"}, {"prompt": "system\nYou are playing Directed Acyclic Graph Vertex Geography.user\nThe players alternate moving a token along one directed edge. A player with no legal move loses. Choose one legal destination that maximizes your final game outcome. Keep your thinking process concise.\n\nOutput exactly:\n<reason>your analysis</reason>\n<answer>NODE</answer>\n\nDo not output anything else. A response that does not follow this format results in immediate loss.\n\nCurrent node: N4\n\nDirected graph:\nN4 -> N6, N3\nN5 -> N3, N1, N0\nN3 -> N7\nN7 -> terminal\nN6 -> terminal\nN0 -> terminal\nN1 -> N2\nN9 -> N4, N8, N5\nN2 -> terminal\nN8 -> N5\n\nLegal moves: N6, N3assistant\n", "response": "<reason>Starting at N4, the legal moves are to N6 or N3. N6 leads directly to terminal (win for the player who moves there, as the opponent has no move). N3 leads to N7, which leads to terminal. Thus, moving to N6 wins immediately. Moving to N3 results in the opponent winning. Therefore, the optimal move is to N6.</reason>\n<answer>N6</answer>", "episode_score": 1.05, "llm_raw_text": "<reason>Starting at N4, the legal moves are to N6 or N3. N6 leads directly to terminal (win for the player who moves there, as the opponent has no move). N3 leads to N7, which leads to terminal. Thus, moving to N6 wins immediately. Moving to N3 results in the opponent winning. Therefore, the optimal move is to N6.</reason>\n<answer>N6</answer>"}, {"prompt": "system\nYou are playing Directed Acyclic Graph Vertex Geography.user\nThe players alternate moving a token along one directed edge. A player with no legal move loses. Choose one legal destination that maximizes your final game outcome. Keep your thinking process concise.\n\nOutput exactly:\n<reason>your analysis</reason>\n<answer>NODE</answer>\n\nDo not output anything else. A response that does not follow this format results in immediate loss.\n\nCurrent node: N3\n\nDirected graph:\nN6 -> N9, N0\nN11 -> N2, N4\nN0 -> N13, N4\nN12 -> terminal\nN9 -> terminal\nN3 -> N5, N7\nN7 -> N11, N10\nN8 -> terminal\nN13 -> terminal\nN4 -> terminal\nN1 -> N12, N13\nN10 -> N9, N6\nN5 -> N8, N1\nN2 -> terminal\n\nLegal moves: N5, N7assistant\n", "response": "<reason>Starting at N3, the legal moves are to N5 or N7. We analyze each option to determine which leads to a winning position (i.e., forces the opponent into a losing position).  \n- Move to N5: N5 → N8 (terminal, opponent wins immediately) or N5 → N1.  \n  - N1 → N12 (terminal) or N1 → N13 (terminal). Both are terminal, so the opponent has no move after. Thus, N5 leads to immediate terminal on opponent's turn → **win**.  \n- Move to N7: N7 → N11 or N10.  \n  - N11 → N2 (terminal) or N4 (terminal) → both terminal, opponent wins.  \n  - N10 → N9 (terminal) or N6 → N9 or N0.  \n   - N6 → N9 (terminal), or N0 → N13 (terminal), N0 → N4 (terminal). All lead to terminal. So all paths from N7 eventually end in terminal. So **opponent wins**.  \nHence, N5 leads to a win; N7 leads to loss. Therefore, choose N5.</reason>  \n<answer>N5</answer>", "episode_score": -0.95, "llm_raw_text": "<reason>Starting at N3, the legal moves are to N5 or N7. We analyze each option to determine which leads to a winning position (i.e., forces the opponent into a losing position).  \n- Move to N5: N5 → N8 (terminal, opponent wins immediately) or N5 → N1.  \n  - N1 → N12 (terminal) or N1 → N13 (terminal). Both are terminal, so the opponent has no move after. Thus, N5 leads to immediate terminal on opponent's turn → **win**.  \n- Move to N7: N7 → N11 or N10.  \n  - N11 → N2 (terminal) or N4 (terminal) → both terminal, opponent wins.  \n  - N10 → N9 (terminal) or N6 → N9 or N0.  \n   - N6 → N9 (terminal), or N0 → N13 (terminal), N0 → N4 (terminal). All lead to terminal. So all paths from N7 eventually end in terminal. So **opponent wins**.  \nHence, N5 leads to a win; N7 leads to loss. Therefore, choose N5.</reason>  \n<answer>N5</answer>"}, {"prompt": "system\nYou are playing Directed Acyclic Graph Vertex Geography.user\nThe players alternate moving a token along one directed edge. A player with no legal move loses. Choose one legal destination that maximizes your final game outcome. Keep your thinking process concise.\n\nOutput exactly:\n<reason>your analysis</reason>\n<answer>NODE</answer>\n\nDo not output anything else. A response that does not follow this format results in immediate loss.\n\nCurrent node: N5\n\nDirected graph:\nN6 -> N9, N0\nN11 -> N2, N4\nN0 -> N13, N4\nN12 -> terminal\nN9 -> terminal\nN3 -> N5, N7\nN7 -> N11, N10\nN8 -> terminal\nN13 -> terminal\nN4 -> terminal\nN1 -> N12, N13\nN10 -> N9, N6\nN5 -> N8, N1\nN2 -> terminal\n\nLegal moves: N8, N1assistant\n", "response": "<reason>Starting at N5, the legal moves are to N8 or N1. N8 leads directly to terminal (win for the player who moves there, as the opponent has no move). N1 leads to N12 or N13, both of which are terminal. Thus, moving to N8 wins immediately. Moving to N1 results in immediate loss for the opponent. Therefore, choosing N8 is optimal.</reason>\n<answer>N8</answer>", "episode_score": 1.05, "llm_raw_text": "<reason>Starting at N5, the legal moves are to N8 or N1. N8 leads directly to terminal (win for the player who moves there, as the opponent has no move). N1 leads to N12 or N13, both of which are terminal. Thus, moving to N8 wins immediately. Moving to N1 results in immediate loss for the opponent. Therefore, choosing N8 is optimal.</reason>\n<answer>N8</answer>"}, {"prompt": "system\nYou are playing Directed Acyclic Graph Vertex Geography.user\nThe players alternate moving a token along one directed edge. A player with no legal move loses. Choose one legal destination that maximizes your final game outcome. Keep your thinking process concise.\n\nOutput exactly:\n<reason>your analysis</reason>\n<answer>NODE</answer>\n\nDo not output anything else. A response that does not follow this format results in immediate loss.\n\nCurrent node: N4\n\nDirected graph:\nN3 -> terminal\nN2 -> terminal\nN4 -> N7, N8\nN0 -> N8, N3\nN9 -> terminal\nN6 -> N9, N1\nN7 -> N5, N2\nN1 -> terminal\nN5 -> N0, N9\nN8 -> N6\n\nLegal moves: N7, N8assistant\n", "response": "<reason>Starting at N4, the player can move to N7 or N8. We analyze each option:  \n- Moving to N7: From N7, moves are to N5 or N2. N2 leads to terminal (win for opponent), N5 leads to N0 or N9. N0 → N8 → N6 → N9 (terminal), N9 → terminal. So N5 leads to terminal eventually. Thus, N7 leads to a losing position for the opponent.  \n- Moving to N8: From N8 → N6 → N9 or N1. N9 and N1 both lead to terminal. So N8 leads to immediate terminal. Thus, the player who moves to N8 loses.  \nTherefore, choosing N7 is better, as it leads to a position where the opponent is forced into a terminal or losing chain. N7 is the optimal move.</reason>  \n<answer>N7</answer>", "episode_score": -0.95, "llm_raw_text": "<reason>Starting at N4, the player can move to N7 or N8. We analyze each option:  \n- Moving to N7: From N7, moves are to N5 or N2. N2 leads to terminal (win for opponent), N5 leads to N0 or N9. N0 → N8 → N6 → N9 (terminal), N9 → terminal. So N5 leads to terminal eventually. Thus, N7 leads to a losing position for the opponent.  \n- Moving to N8: From N8 → N6 → N9 or N1. N9 and N1 both lead to terminal. So N8 leads to immediate terminal. Thus, the player who moves to N8 loses.  \nTherefore, choosing N7 is better, as it leads to a position where the opponent is forced into a terminal or losing chain. N7 is the optimal move.</reason>  \n<answer>N7</answer>"}, {"prompt": "system\nYou are playing Directed Acyclic Graph Vertex Geography.user\nThe players alternate moving a token along one directed edge. A player with no legal move loses. Choose one legal destination that maximizes your final game outcome. Keep your thinking process concise.\n\nOutput exactly:\n<reason>your analysis</reason>\n<answer>NODE</answer>\n\nDo not output anything else. A response that does not follow this format results in immediate loss.\n\nCurrent node: N7\n\nDirected graph:\nN3 -> terminal\nN2 -> terminal\nN4 -> N7, N8\nN0 -> N8, N3\nN9 -> terminal\nN6 -> N9, N1\nN7 -> N5, N2\nN1 -> terminal\nN5 -> N0, N9\nN8 -> N6\n\nLegal moves: N5, N2assistant\n", "response": "<reason>Starting at N7, the legal moves are to N5 or N2. N2 leads directly to terminal (win for the player who moves there, as the opponent has no move). Thus, moving to N2 wins immediately. Moving to N5 leads to N0 or N9: N9 is terminal, so N0 follows to N8, then to N6, then to N9 (terminal) or N1 (terminal), both ending in terminal. Thus, N5 leads to a losing position for the opponent. Therefore, choosing N2 is optimal.</reason>\n<answer>N2</answer>", "episode_score": 1.05, "llm_raw_text": "<reason>Starting at N7, the legal moves are to N5 or N2. N2 leads directly to terminal (win for the player who moves there, as the opponent has no move). Thus, moving to N2 wins immediately. Moving to N5 leads to N0 or N9: N9 is terminal, so N0 follows to N8, then to N6, then to N9 (terminal) or N1 (terminal), both ending in terminal. Thus, N5 leads to a losing position for the opponent. Therefore, choosing N2 is optimal.</reason>\n<answer>N2</answer>"}, {"prompt": "system\nYou are playing Directed Acyclic Graph Vertex Geography.user\nThe players alternate moving a token along one directed edge. A player with no legal move loses. Choose one legal destination that maximizes your final game outcome. Keep your thinking process concise.\n\nOutput exactly:\n<reason