 \nThus, moving to N7 leads to immediate terminal for opponent. This is optimal.  \nAnswer: N7</reason>  \n<answer>N7</answer>"}, {"prompt": "system\nYou are playing Directed Acyclic Graph Vertex Geography.user\nThe players alternate moving a token along one directed edge. A player with no legal move loses. Choose one legal destination that maximizes your final game outcome. Keep your thinking process concise.\n\nOutput exactly:\n<reason>your analysis</reason>\n<answer>NODE</answer>\n\nDo not output anything else. A response that does not follow this format results in immediate loss.\n\nCurrent node: N7\n\nDirected graph:\nN0 -> terminal\nN5 -> terminal\nN1 -> N6, N0, N3\nN6 -> terminal\nN9 -> N1, N2, N7\nN4 -> N1, N6\nN3 -> N8\nN8 -> terminal\nN2 -> N4\nN7 -> N5\n\nLegal moves: N5assistant\n", "response": "<reason>Starting at N7, the only legal move is to N5, which is a terminal node. Moving to N5 ends the game immediately, and the player who made the move wins (since the opponent has no legal move). Thus, choosing N5 is optimal and guarantees a win.</reason>\n<answer>N5</answer>", "episode_score": 0.05, "llm_raw_text": "<reason>Starting at N7, the only legal move is to N5, which is a terminal node. Moving to N5 ends the game immediately, and the player who made the move wins (since the opponent has no legal move). Thus, choosing N5 is optimal and guarantees a win.</reason>\n<answer>N5</answer>"}, {"prompt": "system\nYou are playing Directed Acyclic Graph Vertex Geography.user\nThe players alternate moving a token along one directed edge. A player with no legal move loses. Choose one legal destination that maximizes your final game outcome. Keep your thinking process concise.\n\nOutput exactly:\n<reason>your analysis</reason>\n<answer>NODE</answer>\n\nDo not output anything else. A response that does not follow this format results in immediate loss.\n\nCurrent node: N5\n\nDirected graph:\nN10 -> terminal\nN3 -> terminal\nN0 -> N13, N9\nN1 -> N8, N2\nN13 -> terminal