wever, since the player with no legal move loses, we must ensure the opponent is in a position where they face a terminal or forced loss. But all paths from any of N4, N5, N2 lead to terminal nodes soon. Thus, each move results in the opponent taking the last move. Therefore, all are equivalent in outcome. But since we must choose one that maximizes our outcome, and all lead to opponent's win, any is equal. Choosing N2 leads to N7 or N1, both terminal. So, it ends immediately. Thus, N2 is safe and optimal. \n\nHence, the best choice is N2.</reason>\n<answer>N2</answer>"}, {"prompt": "system\nYou are playing Directed Acyclic Graph Vertex Geography.user\nThe players alternate moving a token along one directed edge. A player with no legal move loses. Choose one legal destination that maximizes your final game outcome. Keep your thinking process concise.\n\nOutput exactly:\n<reason>your analysis</reason>\n<answer>NODE</answer>\n\nDo not output anything else. A response that does not follow this format results in immediate loss.\n\nCurrent node: N2\n\nDirected graph:\nN5 -> N1, N4\nN6 -> terminal\nN9 -> N0, N6\nN0 -> terminal\nN3 -> terminal\nN4 -> N9\nN8 -> N4, N5, N2\nN2 -> N7, N1\nN7 -> terminal\nN1 -> N3\n\nLegal moves: N7, N1assistant\n", "response": "<reason>Starting at N2, the legal moves are to N7 or N1. N7 leads directly to terminal (win for the player who moves there, as the opponent has no move). N1 leads to N3, which is terminal. Thus, moving to N7 wins immediately. Moving to N1 results in immediate loss for the opponent. Therefore, the optimal move is to N7.</reason>\n<answer>N7</answer>", "episode_score": 1.05, "llm_raw_text": "<reason>Starting at N2, the legal moves are to N7 or N1. N7 leads directly to terminal (win for the player who moves there, as the opponent has no move). N1 leads to N3, which is terminal. Thus, moving to N7 wins immediately. Moving to N1 results in immediate loss for the opponent. Therefore, the optimal move is to N7.</reason>\n<ans