pt": "system\nYou are playing Directed Acyclic Graph Vertex Geography.user\nThe players alternate moving a token along one directed edge. A player with no legal move loses. Choose one legal destination that maximizes your final game outcome. Keep your thinking process concise.\n\nOutput exactly:\n<reason>your analysis</reason>\n<answer>NODE</answer>\n\nDo not output anything else. A response that does not follow this format results in immediate loss.\n\nCurrent node: N2\n\nDirected graph:\nN5 -> terminal\nN2 -> N9, N6\nN3 -> N2, N8, N6\nN1 -> N7, N2, N0\nN9 -> N5\nN7 -> N3\nN6 -> terminal\nN0 -> N4\nN8 -> terminal\nN4 -> terminal\n\nLegal moves: N9, N6assistant\n", "response": "<reason>Starting at N2, the legal moves are to N9 or N6. N6 leads directly to terminal (win for the player who moves there, as the opponent has no move). N9 leads to N5, which leads to terminal. Thus, moving to N6 wins immediately. Moving to N9 allows the opponent to move to N5 and win. Therefore, choosing N6 is optimal.</reason>\n<answer>N6</answer>", "episode_score": 1.05, "llm_raw_text": "<reason>Starting at N2, the legal moves are to N9 or N6. N6 leads directly to terminal (win for the player who moves there, as the opponent has no move). N9 leads to N5, which leads to terminal. Thus, moving to N6 wins immediately. Moving to N9 allows the opponent to move to N5 and win. Therefore, choosing N6 is optimal.</reason>\n<answer>N6</answer>"}]
