[2026-08-13 17:33:09] [agentic_pipeline.py (516)] [INFO] [DRIVER 0 / 1][PID 1538566] [{"prompt": "system\nYou are playing Directed Acyclic Graph Vertex Geography.user\nThe players alternate moving a token along one directed edge. A player with no legal move loses. Choose one legal destination that maximizes your final game outcome. Keep your thinking process concise.\n\nOutput exactly:\n<reason>your analysis</reason>\n<answer>NODE</answer>\n\nDo not output anything else. A response that does not follow this format results in immediate loss.\n\nCurrent node: N3\n\nDirected graph:\nN8 -> terminal\nN6 -> terminal\nN4 -> N9\nN7 -> N2, N1\nN1 -> N8, N0\nN2 -> N4, N9\nN0 -> N6, N5\nN3 -> N7, N1\nN5 -> terminal\nN9 -> terminal\n\nLegal moves: N7, N1assistant\n", "response": "<reason>Starting at N3, the player can move to N7 or N1. Moving to N1 leads to N8 or N0. N8 and N0 lead to terminal nodes, so the opponent wins immediately. Thus, N1 is losing. Moving to N7 leads to N2 or N1. N2 leads to N4 or N9 (both terminal), so the opponent wins. N1 leads to terminal. Thus, both moves from N7 lead to opponent winning. Therefore, all moves from N3 lead to the opponent winning. The optimal move is N1, as it is the only one that does not immediately lose, but still results in opponent win. However, since all options lead to opponent win, any move is equivalent. Choosing N1 is valid and maximizes minimizing loss. </reason>\n<answer>N1</answer>", "episode_score": -0.95, "llm_raw_text": "<reason>Starting at N3, the player can move to N7 or N1. Moving to N1 leads to N8 or N0. N8 and N0 lead to terminal nodes, so the opponent wins immediately. Thus, N1 is losing. Moving to N7 leads to N2 or N1. N2 leads to N4 or N9 (both terminal), so the opponent wins. N1 leads to terminal. Thus, both moves from N7 lead to opponent winning. Therefore, all moves from N3 lead to the opponent winning. The optimal move is N1, as it is the only one that does not immediately lose, but still results in opponent win. However, since all options lead to opponent win, any move is equivalent. Choosing N1 is valid and maximizes minimizing loss. </reason>\n<answer>N1</answer>"}, {"prompt": "system\nYou are playing Directed Acyclic Graph Vertex Geography.user\nThe players alternate moving a token along one directed edge. A player with no legal move loses. Choose one legal destination that maximizes your final game outcome. Keep your thinking process concise.\n\nOutput exactly:\n<reason>your analysis</reason>\n<answer>NODE</answer>\n\nDo not output anything else. A response that does not follow this format results in immediate loss.\n\nCurrent node: N1\n\nDirected graph:\nN8 -> terminal\nN6 -> terminal\nN4 -> N9\nN7 -> N2, N1\nN1 -> N8, N0\nN2 -> N4, N9\nN0 -> N6, N5\nN3 -> N7, N1\nN5 -> terminal\nN9 -> terminal\n\nLegal moves: N8, N0assistant\n", "response": "<reason>Starting at N1, the legal moves are to N8 or N0. N8 leads directly to terminal (win for the player who moves there, as the opponent has no move). N0 leads to N6 or N5, both of which lead to terminal. Thus, moving to N8 wins immediately. Moving to N0 allows the opponent to move to N6 or N5, both of which end the game. Therefore, choosing N8 is optimal. </reason>\n<answer>N8</answer>", "episode_score": 1.05, "llm_raw_text": "<reason>Starting at N1, the legal moves are to N8 or N0. N8 leads directly to terminal (win for the player who moves there, as the opponent has no move). N0 leads to N6 or N5, both of which lead to terminal. Thus, moving to N8 wins immediately. Moving to N0 allows the opponent to move to N6 or N5, both of which end the game. Therefore, choosing N8 is optimal. </reason>\n<answer>N8</answer>"}, {"prompt": "system\nYou are playing Directed Acyclic Graph Vertex Geography.user\nThe players alternate moving a token along one directed edge. A player with no legal move loses. Choose one legal destination that maximizes your final game outcome. Keep your thinking process concise.\n\nOutput exactly:\n<reason>your analysis</reason>\n<answer>NODE</answer>\n\nDo not output anything else. A response that does not follow this format results in immediate loss.\n\nCurrent node: N4\n\nDirected graph:\nN7 -> N1, N3, N9\nN1 -> terminal\nN0 -> terminal\nN6 -> terminal\nN4 -> N2, N8, N5\nN9 -> N6\nN5 -> N8, N2\nN2 -> N0\nN8 -> N7\nN3 -> terminal\n\nLegal moves: N2, N8, N5assistant\n", "response": "<reason>From N4, the legal moves are to N2, N8, or N5. We analyze each option by following the graph and identifying if the destination leads to a terminal node immediately or to a non-terminal node where the opponent will face a winning position.  \n- N4 → N2: N2 → N0 (terminal), so the current player wins immediately.  \n- N4 → N8: N8 → N7; N7 → N1, N3, N9. N1, N3 are terminal, N9 → N6 (terminal). All lead to terminal. So N8 leads to opponent's win.  \n- N4 → N5: N5 → N8 or N2. N2 leads to terminal (win for next player). N8 leads to N7, which leads to terminal. So N5 leads to opponent's win.  \nOnly N2 leads to an immediate terminal node (win for current player). Thus, N2 is optimal.</reason>\n<answer>N2</answer>", "episode_score": -0.6166666666666667, "llm_raw_text": "<reason>From N4, the legal moves are to N2, N8, or N5. We analyze each option by following the graph and identifying if the destination leads to a terminal node immediately or to a non-terminal node where the opponent will face a winning position.  \n- N4 → N2: N2 → N0 (terminal), so the current player wins immediately.  \n- N4 → N8: N8 → N7; N7 → N1, N3, N9. N1, N3 are terminal, N9 → N6 (terminal). All lead to terminal. So N8 leads to opponent's win.  \n- N4 → N5: N5 → N8 or N2. N2 leads to terminal (win for next player). N8 leads to N7, which leads to terminal. So N5 leads to opponent's win.  \nOnly N2 leads to an immediate terminal node (win for current player). Thus, N2 is optimal.</reason>\n<answer>N2</answer>"}, {"prompt": "system\nYou are playing Directed Acyclic Graph Vertex Geography.user\nThe players alternate moving a token along one directed edge. A player with no legal move loses. Choose one legal destination that maximizes your final game outcome. Keep your thinking process concise.\n\nOutput exactly:\n<reason>your analysis</reason>\n<answer>NODE</answer>\n\nDo not output anything else. A response that does not follow this format results in immediate loss.\n\nCurrent node: N2\n\nDirected graph:\nN7 -> N1, N3, N9\nN1 -> terminal\nN0 -> terminal\nN6 -> terminal\nN4 -> N2, N8, N5\nN9 -> N6\nN5 -> N8, N2\nN2 -> N0\nN8 -> N7\nN3 -> terminal\n\nLegal moves: N0assistant\n", "response": "<reason>Starting at N2, the only legal move is to N0, which is a terminal node. The player who moves to N0 wins immediately, as the opponent has no legal move. Thus, moving to N0 is optimal and results in an immediate win. No other move from N2 is available. Therefore, the best choice is N0.</reason>\n<answer>N0</answer>", "episode_score": 0.05, "llm_raw_text": "<reason>Starting at N2, the only legal move is to N0, which is a terminal node. The player who moves to N0 wins immediately, as the opponent has no legal move. Thus, moving to N0 is optimal and results in an immediate win. No other move from N2 is available. Therefore, the best choice is N0.</reason>\n<answer>N0</answer>"}, {"prompt": "system\nYou are playing Directed Acyclic Graph Vertex Geography.user\nThe players alternate moving a token along one directed edge. A player with no legal move loses. Choose one legal destination that maximizes your final game outcome. Keep your thinking process concise.\n\nOutput exactly:\n<reason>your analysis</reason>\n<answer>NODE</answer>\n\nDo not output anything else. A response that does not follow this format results in immediate loss.\n\nCurrent node: N0\n\nDirected graph:\nN8 -> N7\nN5 -> N3, N1\nN9 -> terminal\nN0 -> N2, N6\nN3 -> terminal\nN2 -> N5, N1\nN6 -> N4, N9\nN7 -> terminal\nN1 -> N8, N7\nN4 -> terminal\n\nLegal moves: N2, N6assistant\n", "response": "<reason>Starting at N0, the legal moves are to N2 or N6. We analyze each option:  \n- If move to N2: From N2, moves are to N5 or N1.  \n  - N5 → N3 (terminal, win for opponent) or N1.  \n    - N1 → N8 → N7 (terminal, opponent wins) or N7 (terminal, opponent wins). So N5 leads to opponent win.  \n    - N1 → N8 → N7 (opponent wins). So both paths from N5 or N1 eventually lead to opponent winning.  \n  - So N2 leads to opponent winning.  \n- If move to N6: From N6 → N4 (terminal, immediate win) or N9 (terminal, immediate win). Both are terminal. So player wins immediately.  \nThus, choosing N6 leads to an immediate win. N2 leads to loss. Therefore, choose N6.</reason>  \n<answer>N6</answer>", "episode_score": -0.95, "llm_raw_text": "<reason>Starting at N0, the legal moves are to N2 or N6. We analyze each option:  \n- If move to N2: From N2, moves are to N5 or N1.  \n  - N5 → N3 (terminal, win for opponent) or N1.  \n    - N1 → N8 → N7 (terminal, opponent wins) or N7 (terminal, opponent wins). So N5 leads to opponent win.  \n    - N1 → N8 → N7 (opponent wins). So both paths from N5 or N1 eventually lead to opponent winning.  \n  - So N2 leads to opponent winning.  \n- If move to N6: From N6 → N4 (terminal, immediate win) or N9 (terminal, immediate win). Both are terminal. So player wins immediately.  \nThus, choosing N6 leads to an immediate win. N2 leads to loss. Therefore, choose N6.</reason>  \n<answer>N6</answer>"}, {"prompt": "system\nYou are playing Directed Acyclic Graph Vertex Geography.user\nThe players alternate moving a token along one directed edge. A player with no legal move loses. Choose one legal destination that maximizes your final game outcome. Keep your thinking process concise.\n\nOutput exactly:\n<reason>your analysis</reason>\n<answer>NODE</answer>\n\nDo not output anything else. A response that does not follow this format results in immediate loss.\n\nCurrent node: N6\n\nDirected graph:\nN8 -> N7\nN5 -> N3, N1\nN9 -> terminal\nN0 -> N2, N6\nN3 -> terminal\nN2 -> N5, N1\nN6 -> N4, N9\nN7 -> terminal\nN1 -> N8, N7\nN4 -> terminal\n\nLegal moves: N4, N9assistant\n", "response": "<reason>Starting at N6, the legal moves are to N4 or N9. N4 leads to terminal (win for the player who moves there, as the opponent has no move), and N9 leads to terminal similarly. Both N4 and N9 are terminal nodes, so moving to either ends the game immediately. Since the player who makes the move to a terminal node wins (the opponent has no legal move), both moves result in an immediate win. However, since the goal is to maximize outcome and both options lead to win, either is optimal. But N9 leads to terminal directly, and N4 also leads to terminal. Thus, both are equivalent. Choosing N9 is safe and direct. However, N6 -> N9 is a legal move to a terminal node, so the current player wins. Therefore, either is valid, but N9 is a terminal move. We choose N9 as it is a direct win.</reason>\n<answer>N9</answer>", "episode_score": 0.05, "llm_raw_text": "<reason>Starting at N6, the legal moves are to N4 or N9. N4 leads to terminal (win for the player who moves there, as the opponent has no move), and N9 leads to terminal similarly. Both N4 and N9 are terminal nodes, so moving to either ends the game immediately. Since the player who makes the move to a terminal node wins (the opponent has no legal move), both moves result in an immediate win. However, since the goal is to maximize outcome and both options lead to win, either is optimal. But N9 leads to terminal directly, and N4 also leads to terminal. Thus, both are equivalent. Choosing N9 is safe and direct. However, N6 -> N9 is a legal move to a terminal node, so the current player wins. Therefore, either is valid, but N9 is a terminal move. We choose N9 as it is a direct win.</reason>\n<answer>N9</answer>"}, {"prompt": "system\nYou are playing Directed Acyclic Graph Vertex Geography.user\nThe players alternate moving a token along one directed edge. A player with no legal move loses. Choose one legal destination that 