 \n\n- Move to N5: From N5, options are N1 or N8.  \n  - N1 as above leads to a winning position.  \n  - N8 → N0 (terminal) is a losing move. But since player can choose N1, which is winning, N5 leads to a winning position.  \n\n- Move to N4: From N4 → N7 (terminal). Opponent loses immediately. So N4 is a winning move.  \n\nAll moves lead to a win. However, we must pick the one that maximizes outcome. Since N4 leads directly to terminal (opponent has no move), it is a guaranteed win with no risk. Thus, N4 is optimal.</reason>  \n<answer>N4</answer>"}, {"prompt": "system\nYou are playing Directed Acyclic Graph Vertex Geography.user\nThe players alternate moving a token along one directed edge. A player with no legal move loses. Choose one legal destination that maximizes your final game outcome. Keep your thinking process concise.\n\nOutput exactly:\n<reason>your analysis</reason>\n<answer>NODE</answer>\n\nDo not output anything else. A response that does not follow this format results in immediate loss.\n\nCurrent node: N4\n\nDirected graph:\nN9 -> terminal\nN1 -> N9, N3\nN7 -> terminal\nN6 -> terminal\nN5 -> N1, N8\nN2 -> N1, N5, N4\nN0 -> terminal\nN8 -> N0\nN3 -> N8, N6\nN4 -> N7\n\nLegal moves: N7assistant\n", "response": "<reason>Starting at N4, the only legal move is to N7, which leads to terminal. Thus, the first player (me) moves to N7 and wins immediately. No other move is available, so this is the only option. Since the opponent has no legal move after that, I win. Therefore, the optimal move is to N7.</reason>\n<answer>N7</answer>", "episode_score": 0.05, "llm_raw_text": "<reason>Starting at N4, the only legal move is to N7, which leads to terminal. Thus, the first player (me) moves to N7 and wins immediately. No other move is available, so this is the only option. Since the opponent has no legal move after that, I win. Therefore, the optimal move is to N7.</reason>\n<answer>N7</answer>"}, {"prompt": "system\nYou are playing Directed Acyclic Graph Vertex 